(70945, 'Biomedical Sciences Departmental Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'First Friday of the month, 1:30-2:30pm', 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose of the BMSC Departmental GSA is to facilitate intellectual exchange through social events and to provide a forum for addressing graduate student concerns.', null, 'kzhao028@ucr.edu', 'https://biomed.ucr.edu/meet-our-biomedical-sciences-graduate-students', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_biomedical_sciences/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/bmscgsa'),
(405273, 'Black Graduate Student Association at UCR', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The mission of the Black Graduate Student Association is to foster a vibrant and inclusive space that promotes the academic, professional, social, and cultural well-being of Black graduate students at UCR.', 'The mission of the Black GSA is to foster a vibrant and inclusive space that promotes the academic, professional, social, and cultural well-being of Black graduate students at UCR. We are committed to honoring the intersectional identities within our community, addressing systemic inequities, and empowering members to lead and advocate for positive change. Additionally, the Black GSA strives to mentor and inspire future generations of Black students, ensuring a legacy of excellence and representation in graduate education and beyond.', null, 'https://linktr.ee/officialblackgsaucr?utm_source=linktree_admin_share', 'https://www.instagram.com/officialblackgsaucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/blkgsa'),
(386434, 'Black Psych Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Thursdays, 5:00 - 6:00pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'B’Psych will connect students with similar backgrounds and create more accessible opportunities to advance their careers through mentorship, networking, and more. B’Psych will strive to unite and welcome Black scholars to the broad field of psychology.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to provide a space that is specifically structured for the academic and professional development of Black scholars at UCR interested in psychology. B’PSYCH will connect students with similar backgrounds and create more accessible opportunities to advance their careers through mentorship, networking, and more. B’PSYCH will strive to unite and welcome Black scholars to the broad field of psychology.', 'blackpsychsociety@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/blackpsychsociety/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/bpsych'),
(293647, 'Black Scholars in Business', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tues. and Thurs. at 6pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Black Scholars in Business (BSIB) aims to provide a community for students at UCR that drives academic, professional, and personal success through transformative actions in business, socioeconomic, and global education.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization, Black Scholars in Business, is to provide a community for students at UCR that drives academic, professional, and personal success through transformative actions in business, socioeconomic, and global education. BSIB is intended to serve as a gateway in which students can enhance their skill sets, expand their network, and hone in on their passion with the goal of not only being leaders in today’s professional climate, but also laying the foundation for students to be progressive in business. Black Scholars in Business will help all students in all areas of study succeed in the professional world by providing them with numerous resources and opportunities.', 'bsibucr@gmail.com', 'http://www.bsibucr.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/bsibucr?igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrbridge'),
(70956, 'Black Student Union', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Thursdays at 7pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'To provide a space for all students to gain personal knowledge and information about African/African American/Black populations in an effort to help bring down the cultural barriers and stereotypes that have plagued the Afrikan minority for centuries.', 'Black Student Union (BSU) of the
University of California Riverside
A cohesive organization that works to support Black students and improve cultural awareness through the congregation of black students. The Black Student Union is committed to embracing our Black cultural traditions, unity, and consciousness.
In the context of the University of California, Riverside community as well as the greater Inland Empire, BSU serves to be an all-inclusive outlet in which anyone is welcome to gain knowledge or be a member within our organization.', 'ucriversidebsu@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/UCR.BSU', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/blackstudentunion'),
(419279, 'Black Students in Education', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Every Friday', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to provide a space that is specifically structured for the academic and professional development of Black scholars at UCR interested in education. BSE will connect students with similar professional interests.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to provide a supportive and empowering space specifically structured for the academic, professional, and personal development of Black scholars at UCR who are interested in the field of education. Black Scholars in Education (BSE) seeks to cultivate a community where students can connect with others who share similar backgrounds, experiences, and aspirations. Through mentorship, networking, leadership development, and educational workshops, BSE aims to create more accessible and equitable pathways for Black students pursuing careers in teaching, educational policy, counseling, administration, research, and related fields.
In addition to promoting professional growth, BSE will serve as a platform for dialogue and collaboration on issues that impact Black educators and students within the education system. The organization will encourage members to engage critically with topics such as representation, equity, cultural responsiveness, and systemic barriers in education. By fostering a sense of belonging and purpose, BSE strives to unite, inspire, and prepare the next generation of Black educators and advocates who will transform classrooms, institutions, and communities for the better. Founded by Krystal Belzonie', 'blackstudenteducatorsorg@gmail.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/bseucr_?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://www.instagram.com/bseucr_?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/httpswwwinstagramcombseucrigshntc4mtiwnjq'),
(321410, 'Book Bears at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Wednesday 6:30 pm', 'Weekly', null, 'A book will be decided on and then read by the members who will then come together to discuss the book. We hope to increase the understanding and importance of literature. We also hope to understand and interpret the perspectives of our peers.', 'A book will be decided on and read by club members, who will then come together to discuss what they have read.
We want to provide a sense of community, comfort, and leisure to students throughout their academic journey by increasing the understanding and importance of literature. We also hope to understand and interpret the perspectives of our peers. Additionally, this organization will provide an outlet for creativity.', 'sanan035@ucr.edu', null, 'https://instagram.com/ucrbookbears?igshid=umtzuj9h9jng', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/bookbearsatucr'),
(70911, 'Botany and Entomology Undergraduate Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'SPRING 2023 Every other Friday from 1-2pm in Chapman Hall 109', 'Weekly', null, 'BEUSA welcomes all undergraduate students to explore Botany/Plant Sciences and Entomology through activities including insect collecting and garden&museum tours. We also provide insight for research, professional development workshops, and outreach to IE', 'BEUSA welcomes all undergraduate students to explore Botany/Plant Sciences and Entomology through activities including insect collecting and garden&museum tours. We also provide insight for research, professional development workshops, and outreach to IE
Check out our ongoing iNaturalist project here, where members can upload their botany and entomology observations to share.
Please email: beusa.officers@gmail.com to join our mailing list and receive updates! Or check out our instagram @beusaucr as this site will not be checked regularly.', 'BEUSA.Officers@gmail.com', null, 'www.instagram.com/beusaucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/beusa'),
(71155, 'Botany Graduate Student Association (BGSA)', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 9:30 am to 10:30 am.', 'Weekly', null, 'To represent botany graduate students and provide an environment to share knowledge, contacts and resources.', 'To represent botany graduate students and provide an environment to share knowledge, contacts, and resources.', 'bpscminigsa@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/bpscminigsa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/botanygraduatestudentassociation'),
(419868, 'Bridging Voices in Healthcare', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'We aim to bridge the language barriers prevalent in our healthcare system by teaching our members important medical terminology. We also aim to educate our members how to pursue medicine by bringing in physician and medical student guest speakers.', 'The Bridging Voices in Healthcare club aims to bridge the language barriers prevalent in our healthcare system. Although there have been many improvements, such as translators and more diverse staff, communication is still an issue that needs to be addressed. Patients that do not speak English acknowledge the effort of physicians who try to speak their language. Patients who see their future medical team trying their best to understand them and make a difference will allow them to have more trust in the healthcare system and more likely want to take care of their own health.
We aim to accomplish this mission by teaching our members common and important medical terminology in different languages. We also aim to educate premeds how to pursue medicine by bringing in physician and medical student guest speakers to talk about their journey.', 'bridgingvoicesinhealthcare.ucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/bridgingvoices_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/bvh'),
(400397, 'Bright Smiles Medical Association at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Thursdays', 'Every two weeks', 'At Bright Smiles Medical Association, we aim to empower the local community, especially underserved communities, by promoting dental health awareness and addressing oral healthcare disparities. We plan to equip undergraduate pre-dental students with the tools and knowledge necessary to make a meaningful impact. Through interactive workshops, volunteerism, and guest speakers, we seek to provide comprehensive education on oral health. Our initiatives include oral hygiene workshops, hygiene kit creation, community health fairs, and developing a health hub with educational materials on topics like the link between oral health and diseases, dietary impacts on oral health, and preventive practices. Through these efforts, we strive to foster a commitment to preventive care, education, and community service while promoting oral health equity for all.', 'Bright Smiles Medical Association serves underserved communities by promoting dental health awareness and addressing oral healthcare disparities. We offer volunteerism, workshops, and other events to promote oral health equity, and preventive care.', 'At Bright Smiles Medical Association, we aim to empower the local community, especially underserved communities, by promoting dental health awareness and addressing oral healthcare disparities. We plan to equip undergraduate pre-dental students with the tools and knowledge necessary to make a meaningful impact. Through interactive workshops, volunteerism, and guest speakers, we seek to provide comprehensive education on oral health. Our initiatives include oral hygiene workshops, hygiene kit creation, community health fairs, and developing a health hub with educational materials on topics like the link between oral health and diseases, dietary impacts on oral health, and preventive practices. Through these efforts, we strive to foster a commitment to preventive care, education, and community service while promoting oral health equity for all.', 'ucrbsma@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/bsma_ucr?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/bsma'),
(407228, 'Brothers Leading African Americans through Consciousness and Knowledge', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'An organization of individuals across campus dedicated to foster a sense of belonging, brotherhood, and community.', 'Brothers Leading African Americans Through Consciousness and Knowledge is an organization dedicated towards developing a sense of belonging at UCR despite the feeling of being a minority amongst minorities at UCR. We uplift one-another and develop initiatives to ensure the flourishing of our community on campus.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/blaack.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/blaack1'),
(418954, 'Business Entertainment Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays at 6PM', 'Weekly', null, 'Connecting students with opportunities in Business Entertainment and sharing insights into how things operate behind companies focused on Entertainment.', 'The Business Entertainment Association connects students with opportunities in Business Entertainment, fostering meaningful relationships and networks with industry professionals and students alike. Through workshops, visits, guest speakers, and networking events, students in the Business Entertainment Association will be able to immerse themselves in the field and take a next step in their careers.', 'ucrbea@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrbea', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/bea'),
(350999, 'Business Strategy Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 6pm', 'Weekly', null, 'BSC is a new club focused on business strategy that provides a space for members to practice and grow as future business leaders. BSC will host strategic exercises and case studies throughout the quarter.', 'The Business Strategy Club is a resource aimed at improving your knowledge and skills on strategy from an executive’s perspective. At BSC you will learn business strategy from the corporate to the competitive level while also improving soft skills including leadership, critical thinking and problem solving, and public speaking. Throughout the quarter, you will engage in strategic exercises and case studies where you will compete against fellow members in presenting the best solutions and alternatives to problems faced by today''s most powerful executives. If you are unfamiliar with business strategy, feel free to check out our instagram page(@ucrbsc) and newsletter which includes posts that introduce helpful concepts equipping you for the upcoming challenge. Our goal is to provide cases that are easy to understand but challenging to work through.', 'ucrbsc@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrbsc/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pending'),
(71002, 'CA Public Interest Research Group (CALPIRG)', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Monday, 6-7 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'CALPIRG is a statewide, student run, and student directed non-profit advocacy group that provides service through educating and mobilizing students on issues like protecting our environment, addressing basic needs, and making college more affordable.', 'CALPIRG is a student run and student directed non-profit advocacy group that provides service through educating and mobilizing the community on public interest issues like fighting global warming and making college more affordable. CALPIRG provides volunteer and internship opportunities that teach students how to lobby elected officials, how to organize a big event, a press conference, how to run a campaign and overall how to make real social change.', 'bvacc002@ucr.edu', 'http://www.calpirgstudents.org/riverside', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_calpirg', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/calpirg'),
(71203, 'California Alliance for Maximizing Potential', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'CAMP exists at nine of the UC campuses and at various California State Universities, California Community Colleges, independent colleges and universities, and national laboratories that together work to achieve a goal of doubling the numbers of minority students receiving a B.S. or a B.A. degree in the many science disciplines.
CAMP, in addition to being a federally funded program for maximizing participation in scientific research, is a student organization that welcomes everyone! We will be revamping our meeting styles in the following school years with professional development workshops, fun social events, and faculty networking opportunities!
2025-2026 Officers:
President - Yuna Aguilar
Vice President - Talmage (TJ) Cobb', 'The California Alliance for Maximizing Potential (CAMP) is designed for students in the Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics [STEM] fields pursuing graduate (Master/Doctoral) degrees.', 'Our Motto
Scientists are best developed by other scientists serving as mentors who exhibit and expect scholarly excellence.
The California Alliance for Maximizing Potential is designed for students in the Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics [STEM] fields pursuing graduate (Master/Doctoral) degrees.
CAMP was established at the University of California, Riverside in 1991 and is funded by the National Science Foundation [NSF].
CAMP is a program that works to encourage NSF-declared underrepresented students in the STEM fields to successfully complete undergraduate science degrees and further pursue their studies at the graduate and professional level. The National Science Foundation considers an underrepresented minority in STEM as students with Black/African-American, Hispanic/Latino, Native American, and Non-Filipino-Pacific Islander ethnic backgrounds reported at UCR at the time of admission.
CAMP exists at nine of the UC campuses and at various California State Universities, California Community Colleges, independent colleges and universities, and national laboratories that together work to achieve a goal of doubling the numbers of minority students receiving a B.S. or a B.A. degree in the many science disciplines.
CAMP, in addition to being a federally funded program for maximizing participation in scientific research, is a student organization that welcomes everyone! We will be revamping our meeting styles in the following school years with professional development workshops, fun social events, and faculty networking opportunities!
2025-2026 Officers:
President - Yuna Aguilar
Vice President - Talmage (TJ) Cobb
Treasurer - Jason Herrera
Social Media Coordinator - Galilea Flores', 'brandon.brown@medsch.ucr.edu', 'https://camp.ucr.edu', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrcamp/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/california_alliance_for_minority_participation'),
(139871, 'California College Republicans', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Wednesdays between 5:30pm to 6:30pm', 'Monthly', null, 'We are a Republican activism group looking to change of the culture at UCR.', 'We are an Independent chartered Republican Organization with many local and state connections. We put on discussions, host speakers, and help campaign for Republican candidates. Our fundamental mission is to change the conversation at UCR and make students aware that it’s okay to hold populist viewpoints outside the mainstream narrative. If you feel alienated by the extreme repetitive talking points that take hold in conversations at UCR, this club is here for you with open arms. We provide like-minded fellowship and opportunities to be more politically active in our state communities.', 'collegerepublicansucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://instagram.com/gopatucr?r=nametag', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/collegerepublicans'),
(415037, 'CampusCycle at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'CampusCycle aims to reduce waste on campus by promoting the reuse and redistribution of non-perishable, pre-packaged food, dorm supplies, and additional everyday items. Our mission is to build a more sustainable, mindful community by giving unwanted goods a second life and connecting students and community members with the resources they need. Through awareness events, educational meetings, and collaboration with other organizations, CampusCycle shall reduce waste while fostering community cooperation.', 'CampusCycle reduces campus waste by promoting the reuse of non-perishable food, dorm supplies, and everyday items. We build a mindful, sustainable community through education, events, and partnerships that give unwanted goods a second life.', 'CampusCycle aims to reduce waste on campus by promoting the reuse and redistribution of non-perishable, pre-packaged food, dorm supplies, and additional everyday items. Our mission is to build a more sustainable, mindful community by giving unwanted goods a second life and connecting students and community members with the resources they need. Through awareness events, educational meetings, and collaboration with other organizations, CampusCycle shall reduce waste while fostering community cooperation.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/campuscycle'),
(425456, 'Career Accelerator at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to provide students with a welcoming place on campus to explore careers together through peer support, mentorship, and career events. The goal is to make career preparation feel less overwhelming.', null, null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/careeracceleratoratucr'),
(414729, 'Careers in Scrubs', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Careers in Scrubs provides pre-health students with hands-on experience, mentorship, and networking to explore careers in medicine, dentistry, nursing, pharmacy, public health, and allied health through workshops, events, and community engagement.', 'Careers in Scrubs is a pre-health organization at UC Riverside dedicated to helping students prepare for and explore careers in medicine, dentistry, nursing, pharmacy, public health, and other allied health fields. We provide opportunities for professional development, career exploration, and building a strong pre-health network.
Our events include skill-building workshops, panels with healthcare professionals and graduate students, and networking sessions to help members learn about different career paths and what it takes to succeed in them. We also host mentorship programs that connect members with peers and professionals who can offer academic guidance, application tips, and career advice.
Beyond career preparation, we engage in community service projects that give members a chance to contribute to local health initiatives and develop leadership skills. Active members can also run for officer positions, plan events, and take on meaningful roles in shaping the organization’s direction.
Open to all UCR students, Careers in Scrubs is the place to gain knowledge, build connections, and strengthen your professional skills while being part of a supportive pre-health community.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/careersinscrubs_/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/careersinscrubs'),
(419427, 'Caring 4 Children', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Friday evenings (6-7pm or 7-8pm)', 'Weekly and Biweekly depending on events. We will let leadership, members, and staff know about times beforehand.', null, 'Caring 4 Children (C4C) at UC Riverside is a student-led organization dedicated to making a positive impact in the lives of children throughout Riverside and the Inland Empire.', 'Caring 4 Children (C4C) at UC Riverside is a student-led organization dedicated to making a positive impact in the lives of children throughout Riverside and the Inland Empire. By partnering with local organizations, C4C provides education on child safety, distributes community resources, and raises awareness about preventable forms of child abuse. Chiefly, the club strives to create a safe, supportive, and empathetic network where students, families, and community members can come together to ensure every child grows up in a safe and nurturing environment. Our mission is to spread awareness on the complexities, causes, and impact of child abuse while also providing an environment for students, faculty, and staff to further prevent it.', 'caring4childrenucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/caring4children'),
(419002, 'Carribbean Student Union', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Thursday/ Friday after 5pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Caribbean Student Union (CSU) aims to celebrate and share Caribbean culture by fostering unity, inclusion, and education within the UCR community. The organization supports students of Caribbean descent and allies and promotes cultural awareness.', 'All Students are welcome, you do not have to be of Caribbean descent to learn and take part in Caribbean Culture! Our instagram is @ucrcsu for current updates!', 'mhenr025@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrcsu'),
(71129, 'Catholic Student Fellowship', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Monday 7:00pm at the St. Andrew''s Newman Center Library', 'Weekly', 'Hi there! We are a Catholic group associated with UCR, RCC, and the local St. Andrew''s Newman Center whose goal is to make faithful, passionate disciples of Jesus Christ and leaders of the Catholic Church! We hold general meetings every Monday at 7:00 pm, table on Wednesdays at the UCR bell tower, and hold other events such as socials, bible study, retreats, and much more throughout the quarter! Many if not all of our events take place at the St. Andrew''s Newman Center (we provide rides!). The address is 105 W. Big Springs Rd. Come check us out and make new friends! All are welcome!', 'We are a Catholic group associated with UCR, RCC, and the local St. Andrew''s Newman Center. We aim to help students learn more about the Catholic faith and how to practice it.', 'Hi there! We are a Catholic group associated with UCR, RCC, and the local St. Andrew''s Newman Center whose goal is to make faithful, passionate disciples of Jesus Christ and leaders of the Catholic Church! We hold general meetings every Monday at 7:00 pm, table on Wednesdays at the UCR bell tower, and hold other events such as socials, bible study, retreats, and much more throughout the quarter! Many if not all of our events take place at the St. Andrew''s Newman Center (we provide rides!). The address is 105 W. Big Springs Rd. Come check us out and make new friends! All are welcome!', 'csfucrnewman@gmail.com', 'https://sanccatholic.org/', 'http://www.instagram.com/newmancentercsf', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/csf'),
(234293, 'Center for Conservation Biology', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'Wednesdays 6-7:30 PM', 'twice a quarter', null, 'We are an interdisciplinary group of students stemming from various departments, coming together to promote theta conservation and restoration of species and ecosystems. We also provide opportunities for outreach and professional development.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be for students from multiple disciplinary backgrounds to collaborate on activities which promote conservation of California’s natural resources. Our goal is to expand the knowledge and interest in conservation biology and provide opportunities to promote science to the public, as well as providing opportunities for fellow students with developmental training. We have the Center for Conservation Biology facility on campus as a direct resource for collaborative opportunities and events associated with conservation.', 'mbuck007@ucr.edu', 'https://ccb.ucr.edu/gradstudents.html', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ccb'),
(81804, 'Central American Student Alliance', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Wednesdays, 7pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Central American Student Alliance (CASA) is a student-led organization that empowers and unites the Central American Community at UCR. The mission is to bring cultural awareness and build space for students that identify as Central American.', 'Central American Student Alliance (CASA) is a family of students committed to preserving Central American history, culture, and identity. We work to build a supportive community that celebrates our heritage and empowers unity through workshops and cultural engagement.
CASA''s mission is to foster community, represent, and empower the Central American student body. We affirm identities, cultures, and histories that are often overlooked in higher education, and we commit to creating a space rooted in belonging, resistance, and empowerment.
We’d love to have you join us!', 'casadeucrr@gmail.com', 'https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1zNskFsa9AgXneIm7TsOVAJq8iJTHjBjPSVR5dvmeOSM/edit', 'https://www.instagram.com/casaucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/casa'),
(425286, 'Ceramics Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Monday', 'Every two weeks', null, 'A social club dedicated to spreading information and skills regarding ceramics.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to spread knowledge and skills relating to Ceramics and Pottery.', 'ucrceramics@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ceramicsclub'),
(381935, 'Chabad on Campus at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Tuesday 11AM', 'Weekly', null, 'Chabad on Campus at UCR attempts to provide students (both Jewish and non-Jewish) the opportunity to experience and engage with Jewish culture as well as promote Jewish values in fun and engaging events', 'Chabad on Campus at UCR attempts to provide students (both Jewish and non-Jewish) with the opportunity to experience and engage with Jewish culture as well as promote Jewish values in fun and engaging events.', null, 'https://www.jewishriverside.com/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/chabadatucr'),
(71161, 'Chamber Singers Club at UCR', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], 'Tuesdays and Thursdays, 12:40P.M.-2P.M.', 'Weekly', null, 'We, the Chamber Singers Club at the University of California, Riverside, are established to welcome students to explore choral music through the learning and performing of classic and contemporary works.', 'We, the Chamber Singers Club at the University of California, Riverside, are established to welcome students to explore choral music through the learning and performing of classic and contemporary works.', 'chambersingers@ucr.edu', 'http://music.ucr.edu/ensembles/chamber_singers/index.html', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/chambersingers'),
(119158, 'Change in Scientific Importance for Youth', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'The First and Third Wednesday from 6:30pm-7:30pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Delta SIFY aims to provide immersive educational opportunities for students in underserved communities to explore the fields of STEM. We believe that access to a quality, fulfilling education should be a fundamental human right, not a privilege.', 'Change in Scientific Importance for Youth, also known as "Delta SIFY," is a movement intended to provide immersive educational opportunities for students in underserved communities to explore the fields of STEM. We believe that access to a quality, fulfilling education should be a fundamental human right, not a privilege.', 'deltasify@gmail.com', 'http://deltasify.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/deltasify/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/deltasify'),
(108721, 'CHASS Transfers First Program', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], null, 'Weekly', 'Transfers F1RST provides workshops, resources, and mentoring to ensure that students are equipped for a successful transition. The Transfers F1RST Program holds workshops that assist students by raising awareness of campus resources and academic activities. The workshops promote effective educational practices and campus engagement, which increases transfer students'' chances of success at the University of California, Riverside.
For more information, please contact:
Stella Rocha, CHASS Transfers FIRST
transfers1st@ucr.edu', 'CHASS Transfers F1RST Program aims to provide useful information and resources to help incoming first-year transfer students navigate their life at UCR.', 'Transfers F1RST provides workshops, resources, and mentoring to ensure that students are equipped for a successful transition. The Transfers F1RST Program holds workshops that assist students by raising awareness of campus resources and academic activities. The workshops promote effective educational practices and campus engagement, which increases transfer students'' chances of success at the University of California, Riverside.
For more information, please contact:
Stella Rocha, CHASS Transfers FIRST
transfers1st@ucr.edu', 'transfers1st@ucr.edu', 'https://chassf1rst.ucr.edu/transfers-f1rst', 'https://instagram.com/transfersf1rst?igshid=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/transfersfirst'),
(71060, 'Chemical and Environmental Engineering Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Thursday from 5:30-6:30 pm', 'One to two times a quarter', null, 'Social Organization for Chemical and Environmental Engineering Graduate Students', 'Hello everyone!
Welcome to the social page for the CEE GSA group!', 'ceegsa@engr.ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cee_gsa'),
(71150, 'Chemistry Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesday/Wednesday, 5pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Our goal is to show, the students within the UCR community, the many opportunities in the field of chemical sciences, networking, and outreach for higher-level education in the sciences. If you have any questions, send us an email! Open to ALL majors!', 'The mission of Chemistry Club is to stimulate the minds of students within the UCR communities by exposing to different opportunities in the field of chemistry, network with professors & other students, and outreach to local schools and communities on the importance value of chemistry.
You don''t have to be a chemistry major to join. Whether you are in CNAS, BCOE, or CHASS, all majors are welcome!', 'chemistryclubatucr@gmail.com', null, 'http://www.instagram.com/chemclubatucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/chemistryclub'),
(70861, 'Chemistry Graduate Student Association at UCR', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'First Wednesday of each month from 5-6 PM', 'Monthly', null, 'Organization for chemistry graduate students to socialize, professionalize, and spread an interest in chemistry to the community.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to represent the chemistry graduate students at UCR by promoting an interest in chemistry while providing a sense of unity throughout the department. This will include a series of social and academic events involving the graduate students as well as faculty, staff, and/or members of the community.', 'ucrchemgsa@gmail.com', null, 'www.instagram.com/ucr_chemgsa', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/chemgsa'),
(71213, 'Chess Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Our schedule currently includes weekly tabling for several hours a week, which occurs on Wednesdays (11 PM - 7 PM) and Fridays from 2PM to 7PM. We meet at the metal tables outside of Coffee Bean & Tea Leaf.', 'Weekly', 'Chess Club at UCR is a recreational club dedicated to providing its members opportunities at or away from the Chess board. We host events such as socials, fundraisers, and tournaments. Players of any level are welcome!
Our schedule currently includes weekly tabling for several hours a week, which occurs on Wednesdays 11 AM-7 PM and every other Friday 2PM-7PM at the metal tables outside of Coffee Bean & Tea Leaf.
We also post daily updates such as online chess tournaments, collaborative events, and different ways to get involved on our Discord! Please join our Discord because it is the primary form of communication. If you also want to be considered a member, register on Highlander Link.
Join the Discord here: https://discord.com/invite/runQG8UAma
Email us at ucr.chessclub@gmail.com if you have any questions!', 'Welcome to the Chess Club at UCR! Whether you''re a beginner or planning to take your chess skills to the next level, we invite you to join us and play chess with our fellow members! Follow us on social media to learn when our next events will be held.', 'Chess Club at UCR is a recreational club dedicated to providing its members opportunities at or away from the Chess board. We host events such as socials, fundraisers, and tournaments. Players of any level are welcome!
Our schedule currently includes weekly tabling for several hours a week, which occurs on Wednesdays 11 AM-7 PM and every other Friday 2PM-7PM at the metal tables outside of Coffee Bean & Tea Leaf.
We also post daily updates such as online chess tournaments, collaborative events, and different ways to get involved on our Discord! Please join our Discord because it is the primary form of communication. If you also want to be considered a member, register on Highlander Link.
Join the Discord here: https://discord.com/invite/runQG8UAma
Email us at ucr.chessclub@gmail.com if you have any questions!
Last updated: 9/30/2026', 'ucr.chessclub@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/chessclub_ucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/chessclubatucr?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/chessclubatucr'),
(71014, 'Chinese Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Wednesdays 8:00pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'To promote the awareness of the Chinese culture on campus through the establishment of student connections via community service events and social events and to unify Asian Americans throughout the community.', 'The Chinese Student Association at U.C. Riverside is a social, cultural, and service-orientated organization that strives to promote the Chinese American culture throughout the Riverside community. CSA not only emphasizes cultural and political awareness as Chinese Americans, but also community awareness. We provide various opportunities throughout the quarter that allow our members to develop leadership skills through our service-oriented activities. CSA also provides a social outlet for students with similar backgrounds and interests to form connections with one another.
Our logo is the Chinese character "xin" which stands for heart. The theme that we have been promoting is "Two Worlds, One Heart” which is a representation of our Chinese Heritage fused with the American Culture that defines the Chinese American.
Chinese Culture Night is a proud tradition that presents the Chinese American identity while showcasing the uniqueness of our culture in a live stage performance. Culture Night significantly influences all those that are involved because it allows us to come together to celebrate our heritage, acknowledge our culture, and by doing so, we understand that those constituents are an underlying definition of who we are as Chinese Americans; Celebrating the past, understanding the present, looking to the future.
Introducing the 2026-2027 Staff:
President: Ethan Pho
Internal Vice President: Rachel Lu
External Vice President: Angelina Sun
Financial Vice President: Garrett Fong
Senior Advisors: Anson Gao, Kyle Chan
Social: Joyce Wang, Bradley Chen
