Public Relations: Kylee Vuong, Mary Ng
Philanthropy: Yu Gao, Sharolen Ma
Academic: Audrey Mai, Clarice Lai
Culture Night Directors: Chance Nguyen, Joshua Shiu
Culture Night Producer: Jaden Tsai
Culture Night Dance Chairs: Ashley Tem, Emily Hernandez
Stage Crew Manager: Patrick Yee, Isabel Lum
Designer: Kelsey Tsai
Media Director: Katherine Li, Kai Tieu
Sports: Chloe Lim, Ethan Yu
Esports: Simon Liang, Daniel Chu
Families: Brandon Ha, Tuscan Lee
To subscribe to our email list, email us here: UCRiversideCSA@gmail.com
Youtube: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5NspSZuuSLGgKkwhq8CeXQ
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/ucrcsa/
Website: ucrcsastrawpage
Event Links: https://ucrcsa.carrd.co
Linkedin: https://www.linkedin.com/company/chinese-student-association/', 'UCRiversideCSA@gmail.com', 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/UCRCSA/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrcsa'),
(70855, 'Chinese Students and Scholars Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Wednesday 7pm', 'Monthly', null, 'To Promote understanding and cooperation among Chinese students and scholars as well as with other groups in the university.', 'Preamble
The Chinese Students and Scholars Association (CSSA) is a non-profit organization and is dedicated to serve the Chinese community in University of California, Riverside.
Name of Organization
The name of this organization shall be Chinese Students and Scholars Association, hereinafter referred to as CSSA, as it will appear throughout the constitution.
Purpose of Organization
The purposes of this organization shall be:
To promote communication, friendship and academic exchange and to improve mutual understanding among its members.
To preserve and maintain cultural identity among Chinese community.
To help all Chinese International students who live on UCR Campus solve their difficulties.', 'jessieli0806@gmail.com', 'http://www.cssa.ucr.edu/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cssa'),
(71085, 'Christians on Campus', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Spring Quarter Bible Studies: Tuesday 1pm-2pm HUB367& zoom, Fridays 1pm-2pm SSC Group Meeting 1 & zoom. College Meeting: Thursday 7 PM - 9 PM, off campus.  (Contact us for off campus address and Zoom link)', 'Weekly', null, 'To provide an environment for seekers of the truth to know God and His economy, and to grow, function and be built with other believers.', 'To provide an environment for seekers of the truth to know God and His economy, and to grow, function and be built with other believers.', 'coc.ucriverside@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/cocatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/christiansoncampus'),
(421103, 'Circle K International', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Circle K International (CKI) is a global, student-led collegiate service organization sponsored by Kiwanis International. It focuses on three main pillars: community service, leadership development, and fellowship.', 'Circle K International (CKI) is a global student lead service organization sponsor by the Kiwanis Interational. It focuses on three main pillars: community service, leadership development, and fellowship. CKI empowers college and university students to serve their communities through various projects, develop leadership skills through their programs, and build friendships with peers locally and internationally.
Service: CKI engages in a variety of service projects, both on their campuses and in their local and global communities.
Leadership: The organization provides opportunities for leadership development through its self-governing structure, where students elect their own officers to run club activities.
Fellowship: CKI aims to create a fun and inclusive environment for students to connect and build lifelong friendships.
Affiliation: CKI is the collegiate branch of the Kiwanis International family, which also includes Key Club for high school students and Kiwanis clubs for adults.
Motto: CKI''s motto is "Live to Serve, Love to Serve," and its mission is to develop college students into a global network of responsible citizens and leaders.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrcki'),
(364326, 'Citrus Free Care', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Monday 6-7PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Citrus Free Care aims to provide essential wellness resources to underserved communities, to effectively educate the next generation of healthcare leaders, and partner with local organizations to address the health inequality.', 'Striving for equity, inclusion, care, and education, the Citrus Free Care is a non-profit, interdisciplinary student-run initiative to serve the Jurupa Valley, Riverside, and Coachella Valley regions and the diverse needs of the community. A collaborative effort uniting students from different backgrounds, we aim to reduce health disparities, develop educational resources, and provide healthcare accessibility for underserved communities.
The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to promote equity through the diversity of every medical-aspiring student narrative. In cultivating an inclusive student base, we strive to empower patients in their health autonomy through our mission for representation. In addition, we wish to serve the Coachella Valley and Riverside communities educational resources for a multitude of topics. Through these educational initiatives, we also aim to empower health educators and make information accessible to the local community.
The Citrus Free Care volunteer application is now closed.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/citrusfreecare/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/citrusfreeclinic'),
(401453, 'Classical Studies Society at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Thursdays, 8:00pm', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to build community through discussion of the ancient world, its history, its art, and its culture, as well as being a positive force in the goings-on of members’ academic and social lives.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to build community through discussion of the ancient world, its history, its art, and its culture, as well as being a positive force in the goings-on of members’ academic and social lives.', 'fyuma001@ucr.edu', 'https://linktr.ee/cssucr?fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAAaZJaGf1kEQHw3ik_bYXOiuZq-4NiatFCYb5HQ3CiyvjOUiIzKbprr7yQWg_aem_dP1AxSZBX3J43BSRxhTJ_g', 'https://www.instagram.com/cssucr?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/classicalstudiessociety'),
(122499, 'Club Baseball at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesdays, Thursdays, 7:00 pm at Lot 26 Field A', 'Weekly', null, 'Club Baseball at UCR strives to create an inclusive environment for baseball fanatics while also promoting competition on the field. We host games, socials, and trips to MLB games to create a community for all UCR baseball lovers.', 'The purpose of this organization is create an inclusive environment for baseball fanatics while also promoting competition on the field. We are registered with the National Club Baseball Association (NCBA) and will compete against other university club baseball teams in both conference and non-conference games. Follow our Instagram account to stay updated on any and all events! "@ucrclubbaseball". Click the link below or in bio on our Instagram page to join our Discord for updates and information!
https://discord.gg/9SUKFB6Y4j', 'Clubbaseballucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/clubbaseball_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/clubbaseballucr'),
(276910, 'Club Basketball', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Every Thursday and Sunday', 'Weekly', 'Club Basketball provides students with an opportunity to compete at a high level while representing UCR in games, tournaments, and intercollegiate competition. The organization fosters teamwork, sportsmanship, leadership, and commitment by bringing together dedicated student-athletes who are passionate about basketball. Through practices, competitive play, and team activities, members build camaraderie, develop their skills, and contribute to a positive and competitive community on campus.', 'The games would provide the members and the comradely to put together teams to compete and represent UCR against other schools and in tournaments.The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to provide a place for high level competition and commitment.', 'Club Basketball provides students with an opportunity to compete at a high level while representing UCR in games, tournaments, and intercollegiate competition. The organization fosters teamwork, sportsmanship, leadership, and commitment by bringing together dedicated student-athletes who are passionate about basketball. Through practices, competitive play, and team activities, members build camaraderie, develop their skills, and contribute to a positive and competitive community on campus.', 'rrien001@ucr.edu', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/clubball', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrmcbb?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/clubball'),
(349592, 'Club Swim at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Monday/Wednesday/Thursday 6:30 pm-8:00 pm', 'Weekly', 'Welcome to the Club Swim. Our goal as a club is to bring students together through the sport of swimming and compete in competitions. While also expanding our club members'' network/connections by competing against other Universities.
We practice every Monday/Wednesday/Thursday from 6:30 pm-8:00 pm. Follow us on Instagram and join our GroupMe for news regarding practices, meets, and social events that we may have.
Our website has all the information to sign up: https://swim.ucrhighlanders.org/
Practices start Week 1 for Fall 26, Monday 9/28. Can''t wait to see you!', 'Welcome to the Swim Club at UCR. Our goal as a club is to bring students together through the sport of swimming and compete in competitions. While also taking the opportunity to meet with other swimmers from different schools.', 'Welcome to the Club Swim. Our goal as a club is to bring students together through the sport of swimming and compete in competitions. While also expanding our club members'' network/connections by competing against other Universities.
We practice every Monday/Wednesday/Thursday from 6:30 pm-8:00 pm. Follow us on Instagram and join our GroupMe for news regarding practices, meets, and social events that we may have.
Our website has all the information to sign up: https://swim.ucrhighlanders.org/
Practices start Week 1 for Fall 26, Monday 9/28. Can''t wait to see you!', 'ucr.swimming@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrclubswim/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/swimclubatucr'),
(365505, 'CNAS Peer Mentors', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 1 pm', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to provide mentorship, resources, professional, personal and academic development to CNAS Students with an emphasis on first year students.', null, 'cnasscholars@ucr.edu', 'https://cnasscholars.ucr.edu/cnas-scholars-peer-programs', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cnas_peer_mentors'),
(353013, 'Coachella Valley Free Clinic at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], '2nd Saturday of every month', 'Monthly', null, 'The Coachella Valley Free Clinic was created by a group of UCR School of Medicine students in 2019 under the supervision of Dr. Ann Cheney and other UCR SOM faculty. CVFC provides free primary care services to underserved and marginalized populations.', 'The goal of Coachella Valley Free Clinic is to provide language-appropriate primary care medical services and resources to educate and engage community members. CVFC will operate as a Student-Run Clinic, an environment where students are leading the care under the mentorship of licensed healthcare professionals.
Applications for the organization ARE CLOSED. Follow us on Instagram @coachellavalley.fc for updates on when our application is open.', 'bleon020@ucr.edu', 'https://unidoporsalud.squarespace.com/cvfc', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cvfc'),
(71112, 'Collaborative Multicultural Council', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Every other Tuesday at 7:30pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'To facilitate and strengthen the relations among the Sororities and Fraternities who compose it. This council will promote academic excellence, cultural awareness, alliance, community service, and integrity while developing leadership skills.', 'The Collaborative Multicultural Council (CMC) takes pride in being a diverse council on the UCR campus.
​This council is comprised of 5 organizations (brotherhood and sororities): La Union Estudiantil de la Raza (UER), Sigma Pi Alpha (Beta Ellas), Alpha Pi Sigma (APS), Alpha Gamma Alpha (AGA) and Latinic Societas Unitas (LSU).
​
The goal of the Collaborative Multicultural Council is to establish a symbiotic relationship between the cultural fraternities and sororities.
Check out the Collaborative Multicultural Council at UC Riverside:
Instagram | Link Tree', 'cmcatucr@gmail.com', 'https://collaborative-multicultural-council.square.site/#', 'https://www.instagram.com/cmcatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cmc'),
(71143, 'Collective Faction', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], '8-10PM on Monday, 8-12 PM on Tuesdays, and Thursdays', 'Weekly', 'Looking to branch out and join a dance team? Look no further! Collective Faction is a competitive, co-ed dance team here at UCR, open to all experience levels. There’s a place for everyone here—we’re all about growth and community.
If you''re not ready to commit to a team just yet, no worries! We also host weekly workshops open to everyone where we bring in awesome guest choreographers to teach fun, challenging pieces. The choreographers we bring are known throughout the community and have been on other teams, including Team Millennia, Hall of Fame, Natural St8, GRV, and more.
Make sure to check out our Instagram to stay up to date on events and learn more about the team
;)
- @collectivefaction', 'The purpose of this dance team is to connect dancers of all experience levels and bring out the potential dancer within each of its members. This team also aims to support each member’s growth and dance journey, regardless of their experience.', 'Looking to branch out and join a dance team? Look no further! Collective Faction is a competitive, co-ed dance team here at UCR, open to all experience levels. There’s a place for everyone here—we’re all about growth and community.
If you''re not ready to commit to a team just yet, no worries! We also host weekly workshops open to everyone where we bring in awesome guest choreographers to teach fun, challenging pieces. The choreographers we bring are known throughout the community and have been on other teams, including Team Millennia, Hall of Fame, Natural St8, GRV, and more.
Make sure to check out our Instagram to stay up to date on events and learn more about the team
;)
- @collectivefaction', 'collectivefaction@gmail.com', 'https://collectivefaction.my.canva.site/cf-linktree?utm_source=ig&utm_medium=social&utm_content=link_in_bio&fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQMMjU2MjgxMDQwNTU4AAGnU_33qBujT6wyktmCqWyGjouq794Oh76kIEgSuIiQ0ATmBxKHTdneuJxPZwU_aem_qArzDbfnk6CyFKsV3C2cGg', 'http://www.instagram.com/collectivefaction', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/collectivefaction'),
(139894, 'College Democrats at UC Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Monday at 7pm in the Bear''s Den, across from the HUB Scotty''s.', 'Weekly', null, 'The College Democrats at UCR seek to promote the Democratic Party by hosting speaker events, debates, and Voter Registration/GOTV efforts on campus.', 'The purpose of the College Democrats is to pursue the principles of equity, justice, and freedom for all regardless of race, religion, gender, sexual orientation or income. We shall pursue these principles through support of the candidates and ideas of the
Democratic Party. College Democrats will organize Voter Registration (VR), Get Out The Vote (GOTV), debates, speaker events, and other events that promote Democratic principles at UCR for the student body and surrounding community.
Please refer to our Instagram page for updates.', 'ucrcollegedemocrats@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/ucrdems', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrdems'),
(70972, 'College Panhellenic Association', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Friday 12:00', 'Weekly', null, 'Develop and maintain fraternity life and interfraternity relations at a high level of accomplishment.', 'We, as Undergraduate Members of women’s fraternities, stand for good scholarship, for guarding of good health, for maintenance of fine standards, and for serving, to the best of our ability, our college community. Cooperation for furthering fraternity life, in harmony with its best possibilities, is the ideal that shall guide our fraternity activities.
We, as Fraternity Women, stand for service through the development of character, inspired by the close contact and deep friendship of individual fraternity and Panhellenic life. The opportunity for wide and wise human service, through mutual respect and helpfulness, is the tenet by which we strive to live.', 'president.ucrpanhellenic@gmail.com', 'https://www.npcwomen.org/index.aspx', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrpanhellenic/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/collegepanhellenicassociation'),
(75392, 'Community OUTreach Educators', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization','Peer Educator Group']::text[], null, null, null, 'Summary goes here', 'description goes here', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/OUT'),
(75416, 'Community Service Ambassadors', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], null, null, null, 'The Community Service Ambassadors work to connect student organizations as well as individuals to service projects on campus and in the community.', 'In addition to hosting several service opportunities each quarter, the Service Ambassadors keep an up-to-date list of ways to get involved and make an impact in our community and on campus. Visit The Well to learn more or to find the perfect service project for you or your organization!', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/communityserviceambassadors'),
(425114, 'Community, Outreach, Resources and Action', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'This mission is about helping underdeveloped communities by providing support, resources, and services through community outreach and volunteering. The organization runs different projects to meet the needs of various communities. It also focuses on empowering students by giving them opportunities to serve others, take initiative, develop leadership skills, and work toward important goals while making a positive impact.', 'We are about outreach and community service. We focus on underfunded and underepresented communities.', 'This mission is about helping underdeveloped communities by providing support, resources, and services through community outreach and volunteering. The organization runs different projects to meet the needs of various communities. It also focuses on empowering students by giving them opportunities to serve others, take initiative, develop leadership skills, and work toward important goals while making a positive impact.', 'tnguy1215@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cora'),
(71043, 'Comparative Literature Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Week 2 & Week 7 (Location TBD)', 'Twice per quarter', null, 'Our organization is for the support of the ideas, concerns, and friendship of the graduate students in the CPLT department.', 'Graduate Student Association for the Department of Comparative Literature and Languages works to be a bridge between the department graduate students, the faculty, and the campus-wide GSA. In addition, we work to foster a co-operative and welcoming work environment for all graduate students in the department.', 'skoba008@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cplt-gsa'),
(349663, 'Competitive Coding Club At UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Saturday 11AM - 2PM', 'Weekly', null, 'We are a community of students interested in learning and applying advanced algorithms and data structures to algorithmic programming contests. We compete in the ICPC SoCal regionals and we have been climbing the ranks steadily each year', 'We are a community of students interested in learning and applying advanced algorithms and data structures to algorithmic programming contests. We compete in the ICPC SoCal regionals and we have been climbing the ranks steadily each year.
Discord: https://discord.gg/mBvvmuzue3', 'competitivecodingclub@gmail.com', 'https://ucrpc.net/', 'https://www.instagram.com/CCC_UCR/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ccc'),
(420794, 'Competitive Pickleball at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Monday and Wednesday 7:00PM - 9:00PM @ SRC pickleball courts', 'Weekly', null, 'Our club fosters an inclusive pickleball community for health, skill, and lasting friendships. We host competitive events with nearby schools and our mission is guided by inclusivity, sportsmanship, growth & fun—everyone plays, respects, and improves.', null, null, 'https://cpbucr.com/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/competitivepickleballatucr'),
(303209, 'COPE Health Scholars', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesday 6-7pm, Thursday 6-7pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to provide access to information about health care and the different careers in health care. Furthermore, the club is not only for the career, but to give students the opportunity to community service.', 'Our mission is to provide a gateway into the world of healthcare, where we offer invaluable insights into the diverse career paths while also equipping you with the knowledge and skills to succeed. But we’re more than a resource — this is a vibrant community where you can gain hands on experience through impactful service projects and building a meaningful vibrant community with likeminded peers.', 'copeucrclub@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_copeclub/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/copehealthscholars'),
(70932, 'Coptic Orthodox Christian Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Thursday at 7 PM', 'Weekly', 'The Coptic Church is about 2000 years old - it is enriched with knowledge and tradition taken all the way from St. Mark, an apostle of the Lord Jesus Christ. St. Mark ended up being a martyr for our church, as so have been most of our preachers and believers, but he did spread the faith to us and we are here to learn more about it as well as spread that knowledge to all others! The purpose of our club is to reach out to all students, no matter what religion or ethnicity at UCR. We exist so that we may provide a means by which the Orthodox community can grow spiritually. Our goal is to make sure that we all grow stronger in knowledge, faith, unity, and love. We do so by providing fun activities, spiritual meetings, prayer meetings, Bible studies, community service, etc. It is not just limited to Copts, but to everyone who is seeking God and would like to find Him; we welcome questions and curiosity! Please ask and contact us if you would like to learn more!', 'The purpose of our club is to reach out to all students at UCR. We exist so that we may provide a means by which the Orthodox community can grow spiritually in togetherness through learning about the Bible and Christ!', 'The Coptic Church is about 2000 years old - it is enriched with knowledge and tradition taken all the way from St. Mark, an apostle of the Lord Jesus Christ. St. Mark ended up being a martyr for our church, as so have been most of our preachers and believers, but he did spread the faith to us and we are here to learn more about it as well as spread that knowledge to all others! The purpose of our club is to reach out to all students, no matter what religion or ethnicity at UCR. We exist so that we may provide a means by which the Orthodox community can grow spiritually. Our goal is to make sure that we all grow stronger in knowledge, faith, unity, and love. We do so by providing fun activities, spiritual meetings, prayer meetings, Bible studies, community service, etc. It is not just limited to Copts, but to everyone who is seeking God and would like to find Him; we welcome questions and curiosity! Please ask and contact us if you would like to learn more!', 'jibra011@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/coptic_club'),
(415039, 'Council for Global Health Scholars Chapter @ UC Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Honors']::text[], 'Not decided yet', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Our Chapter empowers students through leadership training, global healthcare projects, and networking, partnering with Global Medical Brigades to innovate for underserved communities while offering resources, certifications, and career support.', 'The mission of this Chapter is to provide students with leadership development, hands-on healthcare project opportunities, and access to a global professional network through CGHS programs such as the Honors Member Program and Global Impact Fellowship. This Chapter is part of the Council for Global Health Scholars, a cooperative initiative that has spent the past twenty years helping top students navigate and succeed in demanding medical professions while contributing to healthcare infrastructure and volunteer networks worldwide, impacting over 1,000,000 patients.
As a distinguished Chapter, our focus is to bring together like-minded scholars to develop healthcare innovations that support underserved communities globally, in partnership with Global Medical Brigades®. Through these efforts, students will gain real-world experience in implementing solutions that address healthcare challenges in various communities.
Additionally, members will benefit from leadership training and project management development, along with immediate access to exclusive resources such as certification programs, free graduate school preparation materials, scholarship opportunities, and global networking connections that will help advance their careers in healthcare leadership.', 'dhyan.safal@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cghsorg'),
(347730, 'Creative Community of Writers', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Tuesdays 12–1 PM', 'Weekly', 'The Creative Community of Writers, or C-COW, is an organization dedicated to building a community for writers of all creeds who wish to improve their craft. We welcome everyone from poets to novelists to playwrights, and hope to form a productive, enthusiastic culture of like-minded students who love the literary arts.
We host weekly workshops for peer critique & review, and have more events planned to help our members collaborate & hone their craft to become the best writer they can be.
Join us!', 'The Creative Community of Writers, or C-COW, is an organization dedicated to building a community for writers of all creeds who wish to improve their craft. We host weekly workshops for peer critique & review, among other activities and discussions.', 'The Creative Community of Writers, or C-COW, is an organization dedicated to building a community for writers of all creeds who wish to improve their craft. We welcome everyone from poets to novelists to playwrights, and hope to form a productive, enthusiastic culture of like-minded students who love the literary arts.
We host weekly workshops for peer critique & review, and have more events planned to help our members collaborate & hone their craft to become the best writer they can be.
Join us!', 'creativecoworg@gmail.com', 'https://discord.gg/hqxgR3kPG5', 'https://www.instagram.com/ccowucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/c-cow'),
(346731, 'Creative Writer''s Guild at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Wednesdays 8-10pm', 'Weekly', 'We are an organization that provides a home for creative writers of any skill level, background or major! Whether you''re just starting our or a seasoned veteran, we have something for everybody!
Each of our meetings will begin with an informational presentation about some aspect of writing, then we will offer weekly prompts and fun activities to get your creative juices flowing! You can collaborate with others or work on your own!
Every month, our club hosts monthly writing competitions based on certain themes, with the top voted works being published at the end of the year!
In addition to informational presentations, weekly prompts, and monthly writing competitions, we also offer workshopping, beta reading, editing, and publishing for member proposed works.
Our club is here to support all writers in their creative endeavors, whether that involves improving your craft or publishing your first novel! If you like what we have to offer, we would love to see you at one of our meetings!
Come join us Wednesdays at 8pm in CHASS INT South Room 1134!
Join our Discord server here for more updates!', 'A place where creative writers of any skill, background or major can gather to harbor friendships, create professional careers, work on collaborative projects, get their work published, and have a good time! 

All types of creative writing are welcome!', 'Welcome to The Creative Writer''s Guild!
We are an organization that provides a home for creative writers of any skill level, background or major! Whether you''re just starting our or a seasoned veteran, we have something for everybody!
Each of our meetings will begin with an informational presentation about some aspect of writing, then we will offer weekly prompts and fun activities to get your creative juices flowing! You can collaborate with others or work on your own!
Every month, our club hosts monthly writing competitions based on certain themes, with the top voted works being published at the end of the year!
In addition to informational presentations, weekly prompts, and monthly writing competitions, we also offer workshopping, beta reading, editing, and publishing for member proposed works.
Our club is here to support all writers in their creative endeavors, whether that involves improving your craft or publishing your first novel! If you like what we have to offer, we would love to see you at one of our meetings!
Come join us Wednesdays at 8pm in CHASS INT South Room 1134!
Join our Discord server here for more updates!', 'creativewritersguild.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://thecreativewritersguild.weebly.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/creativewritersguild.ucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/creativewritersguild'),
(414589, 'Creatives In Business', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], null, null, 'Creatives in Business is a graduate student organization that empowers students interested in blending creativity with business. Whether your passions lie in marketing, branding, fashion, entertainment, media, or design, creatives is a space for innovative thinkers who want to explore how creativity drives industry success.
Our mission is to bridge the gap between creative expression and strategic business practices. We offer networking opportunities, guest speaker panels, workshops, and hands-on projects that prepare students for careers in creative industries.
Whether you’re looking to break into creative marketing, start your own brand, or simply find your people, creatives is here to support you.', 'A graduate student organization that brings together students interested in the creative side of business whether it’s marketing, branding, media, fashion, or entertainment. We create space for collaboration, industry exploration and skill-building.', 'Creatives in Business is a graduate student organization that empowers students interested in blending creativity with business. Whether your passions lie in marketing, branding, fashion, entertainment, media, or design, creatives is a space for innovative thinkers who want to explore how creativity drives industry success.
Our mission is to bridge the gap between creative expression and strategic business practices. We offer networking opportunities, guest speaker panels, workshops, and hands-on projects that prepare students for careers in creative industries.
Whether you’re looking to break into creative marketing, start your own brand, or simply find your people, creatives is here to support you.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/creatives.in.business/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/creativesinbusiness'),
(419484, 'Creator Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Thursday''s 6-7 SSC112', 'Weekly', 'We are currently meeting Thursday''s 6:00-7:00 PM in the SSC112! See you there <3', 'Open Minds, Creative Minds, Free Minds

Come to Creator Club to learn how to go viral on social media, build a life long audience, make money through UGC and more! Come to Creator Club to meet some of your favorite online influencers!', 'We are currently meeting Thursday''s 6:00-7:00 PM in the SSC112! See you there <3', 'nwong089@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/creatorsatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/creatorclub'),
(401041, 'Cricket Team at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Mondays and Thursdays for practice and matches/tournament TBD', 'Weekly', null, 'Welcome to the official UC Riverside Cricket. Operating Division 1, our program is dedicated to elite performance, tactical excellence, and rigorous physical conditioning. We compete fiercely on the regional and national level representing the university', 'The UC Riverside Cricket Team is the university''s cricket program on the pitch, competing at the highest tier of collegiate sports with a focus on national dominance. Representing the blue and gold with unyielding authority, this team operate as an elite high-performance unit defined by tactical mastery and a professional-grade training infrastructure. Every season is an uncompromising pursuit of championship gold, fueled by the discipline, hardworking, commitment, and a roster of top-tier athletes. As a respected and professional program for UCR Athletics, we are dedicated to advancing the legacy of the sport through clinical execution, rigorous recruitment of world-class talent, and a commitment to excellence at the regional and national level.', 'cricktucr@gmail.com', 'https://ucrcricket.vercel.app/', 'www.instagram.com/ucrcricket', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrc'),
(120467, 'CSGSA', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'We usually meet Fridays for a coffee social, games, and music.', 'Weekly', null, 'Graduate Student Association for Dept. of Computer Science graduate students', null, 'jbars004@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_csgsa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/computergsa'),
(180615, 'Cybersecurity at the University of California, Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Spring Quarter 2026: Meetings will take place at Winston Chung Hall room 102 every Monday 3:30 - 4:00. We love to see new faces, so come check us out!! Each quarter, meeting times will vary depending on majority''s availability.', 'Weekly', 'Our club offers:
-General meetings and technical demonstrations to promote learning
-Networking events to build connections with like-minded peers
-Offensive and defensive cyber team competitions
It is our hope to provide you with the tools needed for your success. Please contact us if you have any more questions at our email, cyberucr@gmail.com.', 'We hope to encourage beginners and experts alike to learn more about physical and digital security. Cyber@UCR provides multiple avenues for students to be involved in technology. Whether you are a computer science major or an arts major, all is welcome!', 'The mission of Cyber@UCR is the advancement of cybersecurity education at the University of California, Riverside. All students are welcome, no matter what year or major!
Our club offers:
-General meetings and technical demonstrations to promote learning
-Networking events to build connections with like-minded peers
-Offensive and defensive cyber team competitions
It is our hope to provide you with the tools needed for your success. Please contact us if you have any more questions at our email, cyberucr@gmail.com.
Discord is our primary form of delivering updates. Feel free to join here. After joining, please follow the steps provided to become a complete member of the Discord.
Instagram : https://www.instagram.com/cyber_ucr/?hl=en
https://youtu.be/vOR4__1MKgc', 'cyberucr@gmail.com', 'https://ucrcyber.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/cyber_ucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cyberatucr'),
(425200, 'Dale Play Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Here at Dale Play, we celebrate the rhythm and spirit of Latin music, creating a space where students connect through reggaetón, salsa, bachata, cumbia, and more. We encourage exploration of culture, creativity, and community.', 'Dale Play is a club that celebrates the rhythm, sound, and soul of Latin music. Our mission is to create a space where students can connect through reggaetón, salsa, bachata, cumbia, merengue, and other Latin genres, not just through dancing and listening, but by exploring their cultural roots, creativity, and community. Dale Play empowers women and allies to take the lead in shaping how Latin music is shared, experienced, and appreciated on campus.', 'daleplayucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/daleplayucr?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/daleplay'),
(70944, 'Dance Graduate Student Association at UCR', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Monday, 12-1 pm PT', 'Twice a quarter', null, 'Dance Graduate Student Association at UCR (DaGSA) is an association of MFA students in Experimental Choreography and PhD students in Critical Dance Studies at University of California, Riverside.', 'The Dance Graduate Student Association is an association of MFA students in Experimental Choreography and PhD students in Critical Dance Studies at University of California, Riverside. The Dance GSA exists as a social, research, and professional community forum that promotes creative collaboration at the graduate level. Our mission is to foster community within the Department of Dance, and to support and advocate for dance graduate students.', 'mpete009@ucr.edu and schat024@ucr.edu', 'https://3.basecamp.com/4533563/projects/17411252', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/dancegsa'),
(70961, 'Dancesport at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesdays and Thursdays at 8:30pm for the entire quarter.', 'Twice a week. Tuesday and Thursday for two hours each day. The first hour is lesson and the second hour is practice.', 'To enhance the practice and knowledge of Ballroom and Latin dances, through competition and practice. We offer a variety of dances such as Cha Cha, Rumba, Tango, Waltz, Swing, Jive, Hustle, V. Waltz, Mambo and much more. No experience required. Open to anyone who wishes to dance!', 'To enhance the practice and knowledge of Ballroom and Latin dances through competition and practice. For all newcomer students who wish to dance.', 'To enhance the practice and knowledge of Ballroom and Latin dances, through competition and practice. We offer a variety of dances such as Cha Cha, Rumba, Tango, Waltz, Swing, Jive, Hustle, V. Waltz, Mambo and much more. No experience required. Open to anyone who wishes to dance!', 'dancesportatucr@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/dancesportatucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/dancesport'),
(387405, 'Darbar', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Thursdays at 7pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Darbar serves as a platform to showcase the rich Indian culture by facilitating performances of top classical artists at UC Riverside, putting together workshops, and bringing together a community of students who appreciate cultural heritage.', 'The purpose of this organization is to promote the magic of South Asian classical music to the UCR community because these art forms are currently in decline and many youth are not pursuing education in these art forms across South Asian regions or the rest of the world. Our organization creates a space where students can experience world-class classical performances, dive into hands-on workshops featuring renowned artists and professionals, and connect with a community that shares a love for cultural roots. Whether you are deeply connected to this heritage or curious to learn more about this side of music, we hope to make these traditions accessible, meaningful, and supportive for everyone in the UCR community.', 'ucrdarbar@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/darbaratucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/darbar-ucr'),
(70948, 'Delta Chi Fraternity', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Sundays at 7:00pm', 'Weekly', 'Founding
On October 13, 1890 eleven law students at Cornell University formed a Law Fraternity, Delta Chi. In 1922, the Fraternity officially went "general", thus opening its membership to men in all areas of study. Delta Chi, in 1929, became the first fraternity to officially abolish the hazing practices associated with "hell week".
Eleven Basic Expectations of a Delta Chi
I will strive for academic achievement and practice academic integrity.
I will respect the dignity and worth of all persons. I will not physically, mentally, psychologically or sexually abuse or haze any human being.
I will protect the health and safety of all human beings.
I will respect my property and the property of others; therefore, I will neither abuse nor support the abuse of property.
I will meet my financial obligations in a timely manner.
I will neither use nor support the use of illegal drugs. I will neither abuse nor support the abuse of alcohol.
I will acknowledge that a clean and attractive environment is essential to both physical and mental health; therefore, I will do all in my power to see that the chapter property is safe, properly cleaned and maintained.
I will know and understand the ideals expressed in my fraternity Ritual and will incorporate them into my daily life.', 'Delta Chi is an internationally recognized social fraternity with more than 130 chapters. The organization has a high appreciation for academic and social excellence that will greatly enhance a man''s college experience.', 'Mission
We, the members of The Delta Chi Fraternity, believing that great advantages are to be derived from a brotherhood of college and university men, appreciating that close association may promote friendship, develop character, advance justice, and assist in the acquisition of a sound education, do ordain and establish this Constitution.
Founding
On October 13, 1890 eleven law students at Cornell University formed a Law Fraternity, Delta Chi. In 1922, the Fraternity officially went "general", thus opening its membership to men in all areas of study. Delta Chi, in 1929, became the first fraternity to officially abolish the hazing practices associated with "hell week".
Eleven Basic Expectations of a Delta Chi
I will strive for academic achievement and practice academic integrity.
I will respect the dignity and worth of all persons. I will not physically, mentally, psychologically or sexually abuse or haze any human being.
I will protect the health and safety of all human beings.
I will respect my property and the property of others; therefore, I will neither abuse nor support the abuse of property.
I will meet my financial obligations in a timely manner.
I will neither use nor support the use of illegal drugs. I will neither abuse nor support the abuse of alcohol.
I will acknowledge that a clean and attractive environment is essential to both physical and mental health; therefore, I will do all in my power to see that the chapter property is safe, properly cleaned and maintained.
I will know and understand the ideals expressed in my fraternity Ritual and will incorporate them into my daily life.
I will exercise compassion and understanding in dealing with all persons.
I will sustain my commitment to and involvement with the Fraternity throughout my lifetime.
I will challenge all my fraternity members to abide by these fraternity obligations and will confront those who violate them.', 'dxucrpres@gmail.com', 'http://www.deltachiucr.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/deltachiucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/deltachiucr'),
(71087, 'Delta Gamma', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Monday at 8:00', 'Weekly', null, 'Article II: To foster high ideals of friendship among college women, to promote their educational and cultural interests, to create in them a true sense of social responsibility, and to develop in them the best qualities of character', 'Article II of the Fraternity Constitution reads:
The objects of this Fraternity shall be to foster high ideals of friendship among college women, to promote their educational and cultural interests, to create in them a true sense of social responsibility, and to develop in them the best qualities of character.
Delta Gamma’s primary purpose is to create an environment for its members in which lasting friendships are established and in which members find the processes, the experiences and the disciplines that will stimulate clear thought. Its aim is to foster an atmosphere in which women will develop a deeper love and consideration for mankind, a more profound understanding of the purpose of life and a basic wisdom upon which to build their lives.
Delta Gamma’s purpose is accomplished through planned collegiate and alumnae programs that provide intellectual motivation, the opportunity for graciousness in daily living, and community awareness which will enrich the lives of members and instill in them a respect for the enduring values to be gained from the Fraternity.
Mission Statement: Delta Gamma offers to women of all ages a rich heritage based on principles of personal integrity, personal responsibility and intellectual honesty. Its primary purpose is to foster high ideals of friendship, promote educational and cultural interests, create a true sense of social responsibility, and develop the finest qualities of character.', 'ucrdgpresident@gmail.com', 'http://www.ucrdeltagamma.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/deltagamma_ucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/deltagamma'),
(71458, 'Delta Sigma Theta Sorority, Incorporated', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'The Mu Chi Chapter of Delta Sigma Theta Sorority, Incorporated meetings are the first Wednesday of every month.', 'Monthly', null, 'Delta Sigma Theta is an organization of college educated women committed to the constructive development of its members and to public service with a primary focus on the Black community.', 'Delta Sigma Theta Sorority, Incorporated. is a private, not-for-profit organization whose purpose is to provide assistance and support through established programs in local communities throughout the world. The organization is a sisterhood of predominantly Black, college educated women. Since its founding, more than 300,000 women have joined the organization. The sorority currently has 1,000 collegiate and alumnae chapters located in the United States, England, Japan (Tokyo and Okinawa), Germany, the Virgin Islands, Bermuda, the Bahamas, Jamaica and the Republic of Korea.
The major programs of the sorority are based upon the organization''s Five Point Programmatic Thrust: Economic Development, Educational Development, International Awareness and Involvement, Physical and Mental Health, and Political Awareness and Involvement.', 'muchideltas1976@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/muchidst/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/muchideltasigmatheta'),
(405267, 'Dental Global Brigades', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Fridays 7pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Global Dental Brigades at UCR is a student-led organization focused on improving oral health in underserved communities. Through education, preventative care, and service trips, we empower communities while offering members hands-on experience.', 'Global Dental Brigades at UCR is a student-led organization dedicated to improving oral health and providing access to dental care for underserved communities worldwide. As part of the larger Global Brigades network, we collaborate with passionate students and dental professionals to address global health disparities through sustainable, community-driven initiatives.
Our mission is to empower communities to achieve long-term dental health by providing education, preventative care, and treatment during service trips. At UC Riverside, we aim to foster a community of students committed to making a positive impact through outreach, advocacy, and hands-on volunteer opportunities.
By joining Dental Global Brigades, members will gain invaluable experiences in global health, cultural exchange, and teamwork, all while contributing to a meaningful cause. Together, we can create healthier smiles and brighter futures for communities in need.', null, 'https://dental.globalbrigades.org/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/dentalglobalbrigades'),
(350957, 'Dependents and Military Family', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Fridays 12:30pm-1:30pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose of this organization is to create a community where dependents and military loved ones can get together and support one another. Our mission is to create a welcoming organization where we can all learn about the Veteran benefits together.', 'The purpose of this organization is to create a community where dependents and military loved ones can get together and support one another. Our mission is to create a welcoming organization where we can all get together, learn about the benefits we have, and provide support to one another. Our values are respect, integrity, teamwork, and communication.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/dmf_ucr?igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/dependentsandmilitarylovedones'),
(419648, 'Desi Chai Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to learn about important historical contexts surrounding South Asian culture while including professionalism.', 'Our purpose is to give South Asian professionals a platform to enlighten us with their stories while being inclusive about the role their identity played. The goal of this club is for students to gain a strong skillset that they are not only able to use within social settings but also professional environments.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/dcs'),
(339956, 'Design at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'All of our events will be hosted on particular dates. Check our socials for updates!', 'All of our events will be hosted on particular dates. Check our socials for updates!', 'Everyone is welcome to join regardless of major and background! We''re hoping to build a strong and supportive community of people who share an interest in design! Please feel free to reach out with any questions on our Instagram or our email!
📌 Be sure to follow us on Instagram and join our Slack to get the latest updates on our events including our first general meeting of the quarter, workshops, socials, and more!
Check out our important links here: Linktree', 'University of California, Riverside’s first & only design club to support students interested in UI/UX, web design, and design thinking.', 'If you''re interested in learning more about design in the tech world, networking, professional development, tool workshops, design opportunities, and more, then join design at UCR! ✨
Everyone is welcome to join regardless of major and background! We''re hoping to build a strong and supportive community of people who share an interest in design! Please feel free to reach out with any questions on our Instagram or our email!
📌 Be sure to follow us on Instagram and join our Slack to get the latest updates on our events including our first general meeting of the quarter, workshops, socials, and more!
Check out our important links here: Linktree', 'designatucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.designatucr.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/designatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucr'),
(401979, 'Designing Dreams', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Wednesdays/Thursdays/Fridays 4-8pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Learn to sew from UCR’s very own sewing club! Join our step-by-step workshops, our volunteer opportunities, and take part in our fun events to show off your sewing creations!', 'Designing Dreams is UCR''s sewing club!
We hold follow along step-by-step workshops which are designed for COMPLETE beginners so you can learn to design your sewing dreams.
You can also design other’s dreams by participating in our volunteer opportunities avaliable only for active members. This group of sewists will volunteer at shelters/hospitals to make the kids there the outfits of their dreams.
We also hold very fun events from time to time for our members to show off their sewing creations!', 'designingdreamsucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/designingdreamsucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/designingdreams'),
(104090, 'Destino', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'for Spring 2025, Thursdays at 8:00 pm - in Student Success Center (SSC) Group Meeting Room 2', 'Weekly', 'For Spring 2026
We meet every Thursday @ 8pm in Dundee A1107
Park in Lot 23 if you have a permit.
Check us our on Instagram! @destinoucr for updates and events AND/OR contact ereye107@ucr.edu for more information!
Our Mission', 'Raising up a generation of Latino leaders to change the world!! God has a purpose for your life! ¡Cual es tu Destino!', 'For Spring 2026
We meet every Thursday @ 8pm in Dundee A1107
Park in Lot 23 if you have a permit.
Check us our on Instagram! @destinoucr for updates and events AND/OR contact ereye107@ucr.edu for more information!
Our Mission
To journey with students and faculty to follow Jesus and fulfill their God-given destiny.
Our Vision
We envision spiritual of Latino students, faculty, and community everywhere, so that everyone on earth knows someone who truly follows Jesus.
Our Values
We value faith, growth and fruitfulness in a compassionate community committed to being
-Culturally connected.
-Academically achieving.
-Financially responsible.
-Empowered spiritually.
Our Roots
Destino is a ministry of Cru, and so our roots stretch back to the founding of Campus Crusade for Christ in 1951.', 'ereye107@ucr.edu', 'https://cruinlandempire.com/ucr-destino', 'https://www.instagram.com/destinoucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/cru'),
(419926, 'DKMS at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 5 pm', 'Weekly', null, 'We are an organization dedicated to fighting blood cancer and disorders by creating awareness and recruiting stem cell donors to provide a second chance at life to those in need.', 'We are an organization dedicated to fighting blood cancer and disorders by creating awareness and recruiting stem cell donors to provide a second chance at life to those in need. We do this by providing registration forms and swab kits so volunteers can sign themselves up to join the potential donor list. We provide all the materials including swab kits and registration materials, and postage as well as mailing/submitting for potential donors, so to sign up is cost free and as simple as possible.', 'csimo025@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/dkmsatucr'),
(303401, 'Drag Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'For fall quarter 2026 we are still trying to find the time to meet.', 'Weekly', 'Here at Drag Club, we strive to share the experience of the performative art that is Drag. Our mission is to support and educate performers who are new to the art form or experience. As a club, we highlight Queerness, Transness, those questioning identity, and the expression of oneself through the art of Drag. Allowing a space for all forms of drag to flourish and grow. We aim to bring all types of Drag to the UCR Student Life and UCR. We fight for the right to exist, perform, educate, and slay.
Our Winter 2025 meetings are Mondays 2-3 pm. We meet in the LGBTQ resource center at the COSTO hall.
Join our amazing club by attending our meetings and joining our Discord: https://discord.gg/Kseq5WQrQS', 'To share the experience of the performative art that is Drag is our purpose, support and educate performers who are new to the art-form, or experienced. We value creativity, freedom of expression, “charisma, uniqueness, nerve and talent.”', 'Here at Drag Club, we strive to share the experience of the performative art that is Drag. Our mission is to support and educate performers who are new to the art form or experience. As a club, we highlight Queerness, Transness, those questioning identity, and the expression of oneself through the art of Drag. Allowing a space for all forms of drag to flourish and grow. We aim to bring all types of Drag to the UCR Student Life and UCR. We fight for the right to exist, perform, educate, and slay.
Our Winter 2025 meetings are Mondays 2-3 pm. We meet in the LGBTQ resource center at the COSTO hall.
Join our amazing club by attending our meetings and joining our Discord: https://discord.gg/Kseq5WQrQS', 'dragclubatucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrdragclub/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrdragclub'),
(216954, 'EARS Student Group', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Thursdays 6:30-8:30PM', 'Weekly', null, 'MUSIC AND TECHNOLOGY PRODUCTION GROUP. We make sounds sound beautiful.

We want to apply YOUR UC education to the world of audio and acoustics! We''re pushing the limits of music technology, production, artistic expression, and much more.', 'Straight from the constitution:
"The purpose of this organization shall be to facilitate diverse interdisciplinary collaboration centered around experimental acoustic projects. EARS Student group will facilitate interactive examples of our work on campus and in the community to inspire and challenge campus culture. All activities serve a symbiotic relationship with the EARS facility by UC Riverside."
☆♬○♩●♪✧♩ Welcome to the EARS Student Group! ♩✧♪●♩○♬☆
The EARS Student Group is known for conducting experimental research on acoustic sound to solve problems by offering innovative solutions. While social distancing has made acoustic sound research more of a challenge it has also proven that EARS is one of the most resilient student organizations on campus.
If you are interested in collaborating in music production, developing your career path within the music business, joining a supportive and uplifting community, or discovering opportunities in places that you would’ve never thought to have looked, then EARS is an organization that can give you all of that... and more.
Don’t miss out on this interdisciplinary goldmine of creative thinkers.
Join in the fun & our email list!
Create | Inspire | Build
Contact us: earsucr@gmail.com', 'earsucr@gmail.com', 'https://ears.ucr.edu/', 'https://www.instagram.com/earsstudentgroup/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ears'),
(71141, 'Earth and Planetary Science Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], null, 'Quarterly', null, 'The EPS-GSA represents the graduate students of the Earth and Planetary Science Department.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to provide a channel for communication between the graduate students, the faculty of the Department of Earth and Planetary Sciences, and the UCR Graduate Student Association (UCR GSA). The organization shall also enhance interaction and communication among the student body.', 'astro019@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/epsgsa'),
(71156, 'East African Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Mon-Friday depending on the week, 6-8pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'East African Student Association is established to provide, teach, and share our culture of East African countries with UCR students and faculty. With unity as our passion, we strive to bring all East Africans together.', 'East African Student Association was established to provide, teach, and share our culture from different East African countries with UCR students and faculty. With unity as our passion, we strive to bring all East Africans together.', 'easaucr@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/easaucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/easaucr'),
(400214, 'Egyptian  Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'To be determined with everyone''s availability', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Egyptian Student Association is an organization that focuses on creating a safe space for Egyptian Students and those interested in Egyptian culture. ESA’s goal is to allow members to engage in educational, cultural, and social activities.', 'The Egyptian Student Association (ESA) at UCR is a student-led organization committed to fostering a welcoming space for Egyptian students and anyone interested in Egyptian culture. Through a variety of cultural, social, and educational events, ESA celebrates Egypt’s rich heritage while creating opportunities for students to connect, build community, and engage in meaningful dialogue. Our mission is to promote cultural awareness, support one another academically and socially, and share the beauty of Egyptian traditions with the broader campus community.', 'esaucriverside1@gmail.com', null, 'http://www.instagram.com/esa_ucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/esa_ucr'),
(405563, 'Elite Healthcare Hospice', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Elite Healthcare Hospice at UC Riverside fosters compassion and support for individuals and families facing end-of-life challenges through service, advocacy, and education.', 'The Elite Healthcare Hospice at UC Riverside is dedicated to providing compassionate support to individuals and families facing end-of-life challenges. Through volunteer service, advocacy, and education, we aim to foster a community of care, understanding, and respect. Our mission is to raise awareness about the importance of hospice care while equipping members with the skills to make a meaningful impact in the lives of those in need.', null, 'https://elitehpc.org/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/elitehealthcarehospice'),
(434910, 'Elites', 'Department Affiliated Organization', null, null, 'Weekly', null, 'Spirit Team', 'Spirit Team', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/elites'),
(356903, 'End Overdose UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Tuesday 8pm', 'Monthly', null, 'End Overdose is committed to preventing drug-related death through education, medical intervention, and public awareness. We connect communities with the necessary resources to fight chemical dependency. United, we can End Overdose.', null, 'ucr@endoverdose.net', 'https://endoverdose.net/', 'https://instagram.com/endoverdose.ucr?igshid=YmMyMTA2M2Y=', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/endoverdose'),
(70824, 'Engineers Without Borders at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], '5-6pm on Mondays', 'The whole club altogether (general meetings) meets 1-2 times monthly, and project subteam meetings are weekly.', null, 'Engineers Without Borders is a non-profit humanitarian organization established to partner with developing communities worldwide in order to improve their quality of life. This partnership involves the implementation of sustainable engineering projects.', 'Engineers Without Borders is a non-profit humanitarian organization established to partner with developing communities worldwide in order to improve their quality of life. This partnership involves the implementation of sustainable engineering projects, while involving and training internationally responsible engineers and engineering students.', 'alima018@ucr.edu', 'https://ewb.ucrhighlanders.org/board', 'https://instagram.com/ewb_ucr?igshid=YmMyMTA2M2Y=', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ewb'),
(104059, 'English Majors Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'weekly; varies by quarter.', 'Weekly', null, 'The English Majors Association (EMA) provides an active literary community that fosters ideas, awareness, activities and friendships at UCR. Our focus is the study of the English discipline, and we strive to make an impact through the literary discourse.', 'https://youtu.be/tDmntV68ccQ
The purpose of the English Majors Association (EMA) is a group open to all students regardless of major aiming to promote positive interactions amongst the students and faculty within the English Department, create an active literary community, and increase participation in both on-campus and off-campus English related events and activities. The English Majors Association extends its membership opportunity once per quarter in the hopes of increasing interconnectivity amongst students. With passion and dedication put forth towards the English discipline, the EMA actively seeks out substantial opportunities for student involvement and recognition amongst peers and faculty. Increased participation and influence in the English department is available to members of the EMA, as well as an open-minded environment which values individual intellect, opinion, and creativity.', 'kacos024@ucr.edu', 'http://ema.ucr.edu', 'http://instagram.com/emaatucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/englishmajorsassociation'),
(401047, 'Enlight Education', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Friday 3 pm', 'Monthly', null, 'Enlight Education has been dedicated to cultivating passion and academic excellence in STEM to empower the next generation of innovators and leaders through high-quality education.', 'Enlight Education has been dedicated to cultivating passion and academic excellence in STEM to empower the next generation of innovators and leaders through high-quality education. The school''s general science curriculum lacks the wide range of scientific knowledge many kids are curious about, and traditional science camps are out of budget for some. We at Enlight hoped to spread knowledge to the underserved youth and create a community that would allow kids to fully explore the world of STEM.
At Enlight Education, we consider every child''s passions and talents and aim to grow their knowledge through our various activities. We focus on a range of fields, including Science, Biotech, Engineering, and Computer Science. Our academic mentors create unique lesson plans, experiments, and activities to ensure not only academic improvement but also a lifelong passion for learning and STEM.', 'enlighteducation12@gmail.com', 'https://enlighteducation.net/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/enlighteducation'),
(70914, 'Entomology Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Monday 5:10-6:00 PM', 'Monthly', null, 'The primary purpose of the EGSA shall be to serve and protect the interests of current and future EGSA members and to provide a source of knowledge and service to our community at large.', 'The primary purpose of the EGSA shall be to serve and protect the interests of current and future EGSA members and to provide a source of knowledge and service to our community at large.', 'sschr015@ucr.edu', 'http://egsa.ucr.edu', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_entomology/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/egsa'),
(123163, 'Environmental Science Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Monthly', 'As an integral part of UCR''s vibrant academic community, the Environmental Sciences Club offers students - both those majoring in Environmental Science and those with a keen interest - a unique platform to explore the pragmatic implications of their studies. We strive to illuminate the practical essence of environmental science by organizing a diverse array of enriching activities.
Our club conducts immersive field trips, allowing students to observe and analyze environmental science principles in action. By visiting relevant sites, members get a first-hand experience of real-world challenges and solutions, deepening their understanding beyond textbooks and lecture halls.
Moreover, we host engaging discussions with seasoned professionals from various environmental science disciplines. These insightful dialogues provide students with an opportunity to delve into specific fields, ask pressing questions, and receive career guidance directly from industry experts.
In essence, the Environmental Sciences Club is more than just a club; it is a conduit to practical learning and professional networking, aimed at nurturing the next generation of environmental science leaders right here at UCR.', 'UCR''s Environmental Club bridges academics with reality. We host field trips, site tours, and expert talks, fostering an understanding of environmental science beyond textbooks.', 'As an integral part of UCR''s vibrant academic community, the Environmental Sciences Club offers students - both those majoring in Environmental Science and those with a keen interest - a unique platform to explore the pragmatic implications of their studies. We strive to illuminate the practical essence of environmental science by organizing a diverse array of enriching activities.
Our club conducts immersive field trips, allowing students to observe and analyze environmental science principles in action. By visiting relevant sites, members get a first-hand experience of real-world challenges and solutions, deepening their understanding beyond textbooks and lecture halls.
Moreover, we host engaging discussions with seasoned professionals from various environmental science disciplines. These insightful dialogues provide students with an opportunity to delve into specific fields, ask pressing questions, and receive career guidance directly from industry experts.
In essence, the Environmental Sciences Club is more than just a club; it is a conduit to practical learning and professional networking, aimed at nurturing the next generation of environmental science leaders right here at UCR.', 'enscclubatucr@gmail.com', null, 'http://www.instagram.com/enscclub_ucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/enscclub'),
(70813, 'Environmental Sciences mini-Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'To provide a unified voice of ENSC graduate students within the Graduate Student Association by enhancing interaction and communication among the interdisciplinary student body that makes up the ENSC department.', 'We organize and plan social events, professional development, and networking/career-building opportunities for the Environmental Sciences graduate students. We provide a unified voice of ENSC graduate students within the Graduate Student Association by enhancing interaction, inclusivity, equity, and communication among the interdisciplinary student body.', 'mreye050@ucr.edu', 'http://envisci.ucr.edu/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/environmentalsciencesmini-gsa'),
(400581, 'Ethics Bowl at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays 7-9 PM', 'Biweekly', 'We are an ethics debate club that competes in the intercollegiate ethics bowl each December. Join us if you''re interested in talking about various current ethical issues, learning about several types of ethical philosophy, or enjoy respectful and grounded debate about solutions to problems you may have personal experience with.
We meet on Tuesdays from 7pm until 9 pm, almost always in the Philosophy Library (HMNSS 1600).
Fixed discord link:
https://discord.gg/Nj5hQ3Rhhf', 'At this club we prepare for the annual Ethics Bowl by analyzing cases, developing arguments, and researching. During the off-season we house our own tournaments and continue discussing ethical dilemmas.', 'We are an ethics debate club that competes in the intercollegiate ethics bowl each December. Join us if you''re interested in talking about various current ethical issues, learning about several types of ethical philosophy, or enjoy respectful and grounded debate about solutions to problems you may have personal experience with.
We meet on Tuesdays from 7pm until 9 pm, almost always in the Philosophy Library (HMNSS 1600).
