(71130, 'Evolution, Ecology, and Organismal Biology Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Fridays - noon', 'Quarterly', null, 'To facilitate intellectual exchange and provide a forum for addressing graduate student concerns in the Biology department at UCR.', 'To facilitate the EEOB graduate student community, intellectual exchange, and provide a forum for addressing graduate student concerns in the EEOB department at UCR.', null, 'eeob.ucr.edu', 'https://instagram.com/ucr_eeob_gsa?igshid=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/eeobgsa'),
(414085, 'Exotic Animal Care Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'The Exotic Animal Care Club aims to provide educational opportunities focused on the health, behavior, and care of exotic animals. By creating a supportive learning environment, members will gain insight into species-specific needs and common health risks. The club will also maintain a weekly blog spotlighting unique exotic animals to deepen public awareness and spark curiosity. This could be a beneficial experience for those going into careers as zookeepers, wildlife researchers, activists, and veterinarians planning on specializing in exotic animals or wildlife.', 'The Exotic Animal Care Club aims to spread awareness on issues concerning exotic animals and their care, diseases affecting them and their treatments. We aim to support future zoo keepers, veterinarians specializing in exotics or wildlife, and more!', 'The Exotic Animal Care Club aims to provide educational opportunities focused on the health, behavior, and care of exotic animals. By creating a supportive learning environment, members will gain insight into species-specific needs and common health risks. The club will also maintain a weekly blog spotlighting unique exotic animals to deepen public awareness and spark curiosity. This could be a beneficial experience for those going into careers as zookeepers, wildlife researchers, activists, and veterinarians planning on specializing in exotic animals or wildlife.', 'exoticanimalcareclub@gmail.com', 'https://exoticanimalcarecl.wixsite.com/exotic-animal-care-c', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/exotic-animal-care-c'),
(418960, 'Faces of Afro-Muslims', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'FAM is a community dedicated to celebrating, uplifting, and amplifying the voices of Afro-Muslim students. We exist to create a safe space where culture and faith intersect — where we can embrace our roots an express our identities.', 'FAM (Faces of Afro-Muslims) is a community dedicated to celebrating, uplifting, and amplifying the voices of Afro-Muslim students. We exist to create a safe space where culture and faith intersect — where we can embrace our roots, express our identities freely, and connect through shared experiences.', null, 'https://linktr.ee/fam.ucr', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/fam'),
(80228, 'Fencing at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Mondays: 8:30 in SRC room B, Wednesdays: 8:30 in SRC room A', '2-3 times a week', 'Fencing at UCR aims to teach and practice the sport of Fencing at UCR. We have 2-3 practices a week in the UCR REC center, and compete in intercollegiate tournaments against UCI, UCLA, UCSB, ASU, Caltech, and more. If you are interested in joining, just stop by during practice or contact: ucrfencingclub@gmail.com
Practice: 8:30pm Mondays SRC room B and Wednesdays at SRC room A.
No experience necessary', 'Fencing at UCR aims to teach and practice the sport of Fencing at UCR. We have 2-3 practices a week in the UCR rec center, and compete intercollegiately. If you are interested in joining, just stop by during practice or contact: ucrfencingclub@gmail.com', 'Fencing at UCR aims to teach and practice the sport of Fencing at UCR. We have 2-3 practices a week in the UCR REC center, and compete in intercollegiate tournaments against UCI, UCLA, UCSB, ASU, Caltech, and more. If you are interested in joining, just stop by during practice or contact: ucrfencingclub@gmail.com
Practice: 8:30pm Mondays SRC room B and Wednesdays at SRC room A.
