(321325, 'Fight For Autism', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Thursday''s from 6-7 pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'An action and awareness organization that hosts interactive events and activities to foster inclusivity for autistic individuals and peer advocates in the Riverside community.', 'Fight For Autism (FFA) at UCR is a student-run organization that strives to advocate for those on the spectrum as well as represent and allow individuals on the spectrum to have a safe platform to freely express themselves. We host various events and activities that foster an inclusive environment for the neurodiverse community. Through our events, we hope to increase understanding and spread appreciation for autism. Our program Project L.E.A.D. grants members the opportunity to interact and bond with autistic children in local grade schools.
Fight For Autism: Tabling Video', 'ucrfightforautism@gmail.com', 'https://ucrfightforautism.wixsite.com/ucrffa', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr.ffa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ffa'),
(419064, 'Figure Skating Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Saturdays Evenings 7:45-9:45', 'Monthly', null, 'Recreational skating at Icetown Riverside — join us twice a month for fun on the ice!', 'Join us for some fun on the ice! The Figure Skating Club at UCR meets twice a month at Icetown Riverside for recreational skating sessions and social meetups. Whether you’re a beginner or an experienced skater, our club is all about enjoying the ice, learning new skills, and connecting with others who love to skate in a relaxed and supportive environment.', 'Nassa005@ucr.edu', 'https://discord.gg/6xGQEacBW', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/fsc'),
(408472, 'Filipino American Medical Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 8 PM.', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Through our passion for personal and professional growth, FAMA is dedicated to connect and empower our members by fostering a supportive community that values culture, career advancement, and community engagement.', 'Through our passion for personal and professional growth, FAMA is dedicated to connect and empower our members by fostering a supportive community that values culture, career advancement, and community engagement.', 'mguti196@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrfama'),
(400807, 'Finance and Investment Banking Association', 'Registered Student Organization', null, null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'FIBA brings together individuals passionate about investment banking, offering professional development through workshops, industry networking, hands-on experience with an investment portfolio, and competes in the National Investment Banking Competition.', 'The purpose of this organization is to bring together like-minded individuals who are keen on growing their knowledge of investment banking. Our mission is to provide members with comprehensive professional development through presentations, workshops on financial modeling, valuation techniques, and investment analysis. We aim to facilitate valuable networking opportunities with industry professionals by inviting them to give presentations on their paths to success, insights into breaking into the industry, and other relevant experiences. Additionally, FIBA is committed to preparing members for successful careers by offering resume review sessions, strategic career guidance, and real-life experience. FIBA also manages an investment portfolio, giving members hands-on experience with investment strategies and portfolio management. Furthermore, FIBA competes in the National Investment Banking Competition (NIBC), which offers members industry-level experience. Through these initiatives, FIBA seeks to equip its members with the knowledge, skills, and connections necessary to excel in the competitive world of investment banking.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/fiba'),
(281497, 'First Generation Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Varies per quater, depending on availability of board and general members. Typically Mondays or Tuesdays after 5. Follow us on IG to stay updated!', 'Weekly', null, 'FGSA hopes to empower first generation students by creating a community that promotes academic success and networking. We look to support and create unity with all of our members for success.', 'Through reaching out to first generation students on campus, we hope to cultivate personal improvement through mentorship within our members. As first generation students, the effort to break the standard can be done through a higher education, thus the establishment of this organization.
Whether you''re a first generation college student, first generation immigrant, or the first generation in your family to be born in the States, FGSA is a open and safe space to make connections and share your story. It is common for first generation students to be independent and solve issues themselves. With this space, we hope to exchange knowledge and help one another succeed.', 'firstgen.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://fgsa.carrd.co/', 'https://www.instagram.com/fgsa.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/firstgen'),
(71046, 'Flying Samaritans at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'For more information about membership, attend our meetings or join our mailing list at http://groups.google.com/group/flyingsamaritansatucr to receive updates. Head to https://flyingsamsucr0.wixsite.com/home to learn more.', 'The primary purpose of the organization is to provide health care and medication to under-served populations in Mexico. Students, physicians, physician assistants, nurses, and other caring volunteers travel monthly to medical clinics in El Hongo, Mexico to provide free health care. You will have the opportunity to learn what it is like to work in the medical field with limited resources as well as be able to work closely and shadow health professionals.', 'flyingsamsucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.flyingsamaritansatucr.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_flyingsamaritans/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/fsucr'),
(414603, 'Formula One Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Thursdays or Friday afternoon before and after and race weekend', 'Will be dependent on the F1 season schedule for meetings to take place before or after a race weekend (example: week of Las Vegas GP).', 'A community of students who are interested or love Formula One and want a space to share or learn more about the sport, its drivers, and history. We hold meetings either before or after race weekends, and discuss other items like driver drama or tech talks. We are dedicated to making a fun and positive community for F1 fans on campus and getting others into the sport!
In the Fall of 2026, we plan to incorporate other motorsports like NASCAR into the club and potentially rebrand as a Motorsports club.', 'A community of students who love Formula One and want a space to meet others who love the sport or even those who want to learn more about it.', 'A community of students who are interested or love Formula One and want a space to share or learn more about the sport, its drivers, and history. We hold meetings either before or after race weekends, and discuss other items like driver drama or tech talks. We are dedicated to making a fun and positive community for F1 fans on campus and getting others into the sport!
In the Fall of 2026, we plan to incorporate other motorsports like NASCAR into the club and potentially rebrand as a Motorsports club.', 'awu210@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/f1_ucr?igsh=MTBpeWF3cHg0d2J4eA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/f1club'),
(70977, 'Formula Society of Automotive Engineers', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 4:00pm in WCH 233 (we are in the club room daily working on the car)', 'Weekly', null, 'FSAE is a collegiate chapter of SAE International, focused on providing students with experiences you can''t get in the classroom. The Formula SAE project allows students to come together to design, build, and race a formula-style race car.', 'Please fill out this form if you''re interested: Applications will open again Fall 2026
Currently, we are mostly looking for EE/CS to build custom circuit boards and code our inverter, but we will accept all majors for either our mechanical (ME) team or our business team. We close applications 5 weeks into every quarter. We will dm you on Discord towards the end of the application period so watch out for our dm! You can join our Discord and Instagram for more information!
Since 2014, the Society of Automotive Engineers at UC Riverside has been empowering engineering students to learn and gain experience that will be used after graduation in many industries worldwide. Although traditionally thought of as a Mechanical Engineering Organization, our club has evolved into a multi-disciplinary team of engineers and business professionals throughout the years. We have several cars under our belt and have transitioned to building formula-style electric vehicles. Our alumni network includes professionals in highly competitive companies such as Tesla, Rivian, SpaceX, Anduril, etc.
Through the years of operation, our program has encouraged the growth and development of bleeding-edge technologies, including the design and development of AC Synchronous Electric Motors, Lithium-Ion battery packs, complex mechanical drivetrain systems, air intake manifolds, and so much more.
As we continue to venture forward, we expect to build the second competitive electric vehicle as a team! We travel to competition every year to compete against 75 other colleges and this year it is in Michigan.
Our sponsors include Tesla, Chicas Motorsport, SolidWorks, Hesse Mechatronics, Airtech, Ansys, Altium, IMS, Shiftclickmedia, GRI pumps, South Coast Foam, Duda, Kenny Leung, GCAPUCR, ASUCR.', 'ucrhighlanderracing@gmail.com', 'http://www.highlanderracing.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/highlanderracing', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/highlander-racing'),
(400792, 'Fostering Loving Hands', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Fostering Loving Hands aims to foster community engagement, service, and compassion. FLH aims to empower UCR students to serve and advocate for underserved populations through education and creating opportunities to directly help these communities.', 'Fostering Loving Hands aims to foster community engagement, service, and compassion. FLH strives to empower UCR students to serve and advocate for underserved populations through education about local issues and disparities and creating and connecting students to opportunities to directly help these communities.', 'ucr@fosteringlovinghands.org', 'http://fosteringlovinghands.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrflh/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/fosteringlovinghands'),
(339985, 'Friends of Médecins Sans Frontières at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'The first Wednesday of every month, from 7:00pm to 8:00pm', 'Monthly', null, 'We aim to raise awareness and knowledge about MSF’s work and about humanitarian issues taking place around the world, and support MSF in advocacy campaigns. We also aim to give back to the Inland Empire through clinical and non-clinical volunteering.', 'Doctors Without Borders/Médecins Sans Frontières (MSF) is an international medical humanitarian emergency aid and relief organization, founded in 1971, with national offices present in more than 20 countries including the United States. MSF''s national offices contribute to the operation of medical humanitaria assistance projects in more than 65 countries worldwide. In 1999, MSF received the Nobel Peace Prize. More information about MSF is available here: https://www.msf.org/who-we-are
The overarching goals of Friends of MSF at UCR is as follows:
(1) To raise awareness for MSF.
Friends of MSF York strives to raise awareness for MSF, the work of MSF in the field, the populations that MSF serves, and the humanitarian issues MSF supports.
(2) To fundraise for MSF.
Friends of MSF at UCR raises money to support MSF, its projects and campaigns.
(3) To encourage others to consider work with MSF.
Although students cannot work with MSF field missions, Friends of MSF at UCR strives to make students aware of future opportunities with MSF in the hopes that they will consider working with MSF later in their professional careers. Friends of MSF at UCR provides information on MSF, the nature of fieldwork, and emphasize that professionals from a wide range of medical and non-medical professions are needed.
(4) Form deeper roots within the Inland Empire through community service projects and fundraisers for other local non-profit organizations.
Friends of MSF at UCR do not represent the MSF organization.', 'friendsofmsf.ucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/friendsmsf_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/fomsf_ucr'),
(70814, 'Future Business Leaders of America at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays: 6:30 - 7:30 | HUB 260/269', 'Weekly', 'Meetings every Tuesday 6:30 - 7:30 PM
What makes us different? We challenge the standard in all areas:
As the largest business organization in the nation, FBLA’s mission is to develop business leaders, however, within our chapter at UC Riverside, we strive to surpass that goal. We aspire to nurture leadership within all our members, empowering them to discover their true selves, value, potential, and confidence; irrespective of their major or intended career path. We believe that preparing for a successful career transcends hard skills and professional experience; it involves being attuned with oneself and understanding their desired personal and professional growth. Our approach involves fostering a positive and welcoming environment for creativity, hands-on experience, personal development, and professional opportunities. We stand out by embracing both modern and traditional business practices to develop leaders to exceed their full potential.
No matter what age you are, your major, or interests you hold, when it comes to reaching your dreams and aspirations, every person needs the skills our organization seeks to develop and fine-tune. For this reason, we open our doors to all majors, all class levels, and all outside the community who are passionate about growth. Join us for an exciting journey of growth and achievement!
Why PBL-FBLA?
This organization takes a different approach to developing leaders. Leadership starts with understanding your purpose, strengthens with confidence, and actualizes with tangible accomplishments. As an organization, we realize that true leadership requires more than just professional skills and development. A key factor that many may overlook is the importance and value of personal development, which requires complete self awareness, elevating self confidence, overcoming self doubt, and believing in your potential. In this organization, we target growth in these two factors so that it can fuel ambition and create a hunger for taking all opportunities available to us.
An opportunity for our members to gain hands-on experience, working on projects and gaining hard skills they can utilize within their future careers.
Weekly General Meetings
Interactive workshops touching a variety of personal/professional topics, oriented to advance your growth and leadership.
State and National Conferences
Compete in events against other chapters across the state including UCSD, UC Berkeley, and more.
Always Celebrate
Whether it’s achieving goals or overcoming struggles, leaders acknowledge success and know when to celebrate them. This is why PBL-FBLA strives to not only teach professional skills, but emphasize the importance of genuine connection and fun amongst its members. From socials to retreats, there is always something fun planned to meet new people, strengthen bonds, and create an enjoyable college experience!
Are you a Vendor looking to be sponsored on campus? Email us!', 'Future Business Leaders of America at UCR - provides opportunities for students in all majors to develop skills needed for their future careers: communication, interpersonal, leadership, networking, public speaking, and resume building.', 'Meetings every Tuesday 6:30 - 7:30 PM
What makes us different? We challenge the standard in all areas:
As the largest business organization in the nation, FBLA’s mission is to develop business leaders, however, within our chapter at UC Riverside, we strive to surpass that goal. We aspire to nurture leadership within all our members, empowering them to discover their true selves, value, potential, and confidence; irrespective of their major or intended career path. We believe that preparing for a successful career transcends hard skills and professional experience; it involves being attuned with oneself and understanding their desired personal and professional growth. Our approach involves fostering a positive and welcoming environment for creativity, hands-on experience, personal development, and professional opportunities. We stand out by embracing both modern and traditional business practices to develop leaders to exceed their full potential.
No matter what age you are, your major, or interests you hold, when it comes to reaching your dreams and aspirations, every person needs the skills our organization seeks to develop and fine-tune. For this reason, we open our doors to all majors, all class levels, and all outside the community who are passionate about growth. Join us for an exciting journey of growth and achievement!
Why PBL-FBLA?
This organization takes a different approach to developing leaders. Leadership starts with understanding your purpose, strengthens with confidence, and actualizes with tangible accomplishments. As an organization, we realize that true leadership requires more than just professional skills and development. A key factor that many may overlook is the importance and value of personal development, which requires complete self awareness, elevating self confidence, overcoming self doubt, and believing in your potential. In this organization, we target growth in these two factors so that it can fuel ambition and create a hunger for taking all opportunities available to us.
How We Do It:
Unique to us is our flat organizational structure, that allows every person to voice their ideas and be heard. Additionally, UCR PBL-FBLA is an environment that is safe space for creativity with like minded individuals who help push each other towards success. This structure and environment are crucial to our organization’s culture. Collectively as fellow students, we understand how draining and demoralizing the pursuit of our ambitions may be - that rejection, fear, and struggle may derail us from our big picture goals. As difficult as the journey may be, our organization offers the care and support that of a family, but also challenges each member to to ask themselves if their actions and goals align with their idea of success - whether that means living happily, supporting a family, getting a desired job title, or working for a dream company.
What We Do:
With everything that we do at UCR PBL-FBLA, our number one goal is to help our members grow, to help you be the best version of yourself, to find and refine the leader that is already within you, and to foster your dreams into real actions. We use our “why” to design projects that are customized to benefit you, and we do so by analyzing what each member needs to be a step closer to self actualization. Here are some of the many things we do:
Committees: Programming, Outreach, and Marketing
An opportunity for our members to gain hands-on experience, working on projects and gaining hard skills they can utilize within their future careers.
Weekly General Meetings
Interactive workshops touching a variety of personal/professional topics, oriented to advance your growth and leadership.
State and National Conferences
Compete in events against other chapters across the state including UCSD, UC Berkeley, and more.
Mentor Mentee Program
Join our family and pair up with an officer/returning member for valuable insight and mentorship.
Member Development Program
A way for busier members to still gain a personalized experience by developing their skills and finding their passions.
Workshops
Not your average workshops for Networking, Resume Critiques, Elevator Pitches, LinkedIn, and more!
Professional Networking Opportunities
Quarterly Talk Shows with professionals from firms such as Goldman Sachs to share industry knowledge.
We partner with the School of Business, Career Center, and ASPB to create events like our Networking Dinner.
Values
Stride Towards Self-Actualization
To be self-actualized is to realize one’s true self: from their goals and desires to their traits and qualities. By doing so, one can gain their own sense of self and purpose. Here at PBL-FBLA, we gladly push each individual towards their own self-actualization, asking the hard, thought-provoking questions, reflecting on the difficult challenges, and allowing members to think critically about their mindsets and personal identities.
Grow Together
When one hears the word “leader”, they tend to think of one individual. However, here at PBL-FBLA, every individual is a leader in their own right, pursuing their own dreams while helping and inspiring those around them. Regardless of experience level or major, PBL-FBLA is a place where everyone can grow and push their limits to become better versions of themselves.
Produce Quality
PBL-FBLA and the Officer Team promises to ensure everything we do is up to quality standards in order to create a complete and enjoyable experience for our members. Furthermore, we promise to push our members to achieve quality within their own works and careers, providing motivation, asking the right questions, and providing them with any possible resources we can.
Always Celebrate
Whether it’s achieving goals or overcoming struggles, leaders acknowledge success and know when to celebrate them. This is why PBL-FBLA strives to not only teach professional skills, but emphasize the importance of genuine connection and fun amongst its members. From socials to retreats, there is always something fun planned to meet new people, strengthen bonds, and create an enjoyable college experience!
Are you a Vendor looking to be sponsored on campus? Email us!', 'ucrfbla@gmail.com', 'http://www.fblaucr.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrpbl.fbla', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrfbla'),
(425165, 'Future Founders', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesday 5pm', 'Weekly', 'Future Founders is an organization dedicated to creating a supportive and collaborative environment that encourages entrepreneurial growth. The organization brings together individuals who are interested in business, innovation, and investing, providing a space to exchange ideas, learn from one another, and gain real-world insight. Through discussions, workshops, guest speakers, and hands-on opportunities, members are able to explore business concepts, develop practical and transferable skills, and better understand their personal interests and strengths. Future Founders aims to help members build confidence, expand their professional network, and prepare for future academic, career, and entrepreneurial endeavors.', 'Future Founders is an organization dedicated to providing an environment that fosters entrepreneurial growth, allowing individuals to explore their business career interests and abilities.', 'Future Founders is an organization dedicated to creating a supportive and collaborative environment that encourages entrepreneurial growth. The organization brings together individuals who are interested in business, innovation, and investing, providing a space to exchange ideas, learn from one another, and gain real-world insight. Through discussions, workshops, guest speakers, and hands-on opportunities, members are able to explore business concepts, develop practical and transferable skills, and better understand their personal interests and strengths. Future Founders aims to help members build confidence, expand their professional network, and prepare for future academic, career, and entrepreneurial endeavors.', 'joel.vazquez@email.ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/futurefounders'),
(70942, 'Future Pharmacists Interested in Learning Leadership Skills', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Thursdays starting after 6:30 p.m', 'Every two weeks', 'Future Pharmacists Interested in Learning Leadership Skills.
