(301683, 'Future Teachers of Color Committed to Racial Justice+', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'We meet biweekly on Wednesdays from 6:00PM-7:00pm, join us in Sproul Hall Rm, 1215!', 'Every two weeks', 'To create a safe and welcoming space for FTOC members to discuss and share ideas on how to build racially transformative classrooms and schools.
To provide opportunities for future educators of Color to meet current educators of Color who are currently doing racial justice work in their own schools/communities through guest speakers.
To provide opportunities for community involvement and community service.
To support current teachers of Color committed to racial justice by helping in the planning and facilitation of the annual Institute for Teachers of Color (ITOC) Committed to Racial Justice conference at UCR (http://www.instituteforteachersofcolor.org/).
Mission Statement:', 'FTOC brings together racial justice-oriented students of Color from UCR who want to pursue teaching in a K-12 or higher education setting. We are a group who wants to work towards building racially transformative classrooms and schools.', 'The purpose of the FTOC Organization is:
To welcome, showcase, and build a community of future teachers of Color (both undergraduate and graduate) who are committed to racial and social justice in educational settings.
To create a safe and welcoming space for FTOC members to discuss and share ideas on how to build racially transformative classrooms and schools.
To provide opportunities for future educators of Color to meet current educators of Color who are currently doing racial justice work in their own schools/communities through guest speakers.
To provide opportunities for community involvement and community service.
To support current teachers of Color committed to racial justice by helping in the planning and facilitation of the annual Institute for Teachers of Color (ITOC) Committed to Racial Justice conference at UCR (http://www.instituteforteachersofcolor.org/).
Mission Statement:
Following the mission of the Institute for Teachers of Color (ITOC) Committed to Racial Justice (http://www.instituteforteachersofcolor.org/), the FTOC organization’s mission is to bring together racial justice-oriented students of Color from UCR who want to pursue teaching in a K-12 or higher education setting. Our main goal is to empower future educators of Color to teach for racial and social justice in order to build racially transformative classrooms and schools. We hope to do this by creating a safe space for students to critically think and talk about educational issues involving race and racism, providing volunteer opportunities in educational settings, and inviting teacher guest speakers to share their racial justice work.', 'ucr.futureteachersofcolor@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ftoc_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ftoc'),
(104235, 'Gamespawn at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'For more information, check our Discord for our weekly announcements! https://discord.gg/QXHjd4nvY6', 'Weekly', null, 'Welcome to Gamespawn, a professional engineering organization within BCOE with a focus on video game development! We host projects, events, industry speakers, and workshops in a variety of disciplines related to game design. All levels/majors welcome!', 'Hello everyone! Welcome to Gamespawn, a professional engineering organization within BCOE for UCR students who are interested in video game development. We educate students in skills related to game art, programming, writing, and sound design through interactive workshops. Our organization is here to introduce the different aspects of game development and its relation to the game industry. Every year, members pitch game ideas and form groups to develop their project pitches into playable video games! We also hold game jams for people that want to experience game development, but might not have the time commitment for a long-term project. To stay up to date on Gamespawn news and updates please join our Discord! Students with any level of interest, experience, and background are welcome to join our club and our projects :)
Join us on our Discord server here!
Looking to get involved? We''re looking for another Social Media Coordinator for the 2025-2026 academic year! Join our Discord and message Jordan or Kian to learn more!', 'gamespawn.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://gamespawn.github.io/', 'https://www.instagram.com/gamespawn.ucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gamespawn'),
(70993, 'Gamma Phi Beta Sorority', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Monday 8pm', 'Weekly', null, 'To promote the highest type of womanhood in all facets of life: mentally, spiritually, emotionally, educationally, and socially. We build confident women of character who celebrate sisterhood and make a difference in the world around us.', 'To promote the highest type of womanhood in all facets of life: mentally, spiritually, emotionally, educationally, and socially. We build confident women of character who celebrate sisterhood and make a difference in the world around us.', 'president.gphib.dl@gmail.com', 'https://www.gammaphibetaucr.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/gammaphibeta_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gammaphibeta'),
(71089, 'Gardening Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'TBA (sign up with us here on HighlanderLink and we will send you our newsletter with all meetings and events)', 'Every two weeks', null, 'An organization open to UCR and non-UCR individuals who are seeking to foster skills surrounding community gardening and to educate others about agriculture.', 'Gardening Club is a group of students who are passionate about seeking sustainable initiatives on our campus and in our communities. The role of our organization is to raise awareness of local sustainable food systems and environmental justice, while empowering students to take collaborative action! We hope to create a safe space for gardeners of all levels. Join our org to work with other students, local nonprofit organizations, and community activists in growing a community of dedicated gardeners!
Everyone is welcome and please connect to receive updates about our events!
We can''t wait to see you all!', 'ucrgardening@gmail.com', 'https://ucrgardening.wixsite.com/mysite', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrgardening/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gardenclub'),
(70963, 'Genetics, Genomics and Bioinformatics Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'The GGB GSA exists to further the goals and interests of graduate students within the Genetics, Genomics, and Bioinformatics graduate program. We  organize both scholarly and social events and discussions to benefit our overall graduate school experience', '1) To create an association that will allow students of the UCR graduate program in Genetics, Genomics, and Bioinformatics to participate in the administrative affairs of the program
