3) To provide a forum where members of the organization may voice their opinions and express their views
4) To hold events that will promote program identity and unity.', 'ethan.eurmsirilerd@email.ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ggbgsa'),
(82443, 'Geology Student Organization', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Middle of the week, 5-7 or 6-8 pm', 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose of this organization is to advocate and promote geology amongst students in the major and non-majors alike.', 'This organization strives to motivate students to learn about their surroundings and local geology regardless of major. We accomplish this goal through informative trips that unite us with nature either through hiking, rock hounding, or camping trips.
GSO is also a resource for students. Members can obtain advice on classes and even assistance on any geology related coursework. In addition, we encourage students to network with faculty, peers, and local geoscience professionals to gain insight into this underrepresented field.
If you appreciate and enjoy learning about the outdoors, then join us on our next trip! We welcome all students.', 'geostudentorg.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://earthscience.ucr.edu/gso.html', 'https://www.instagram.com/geostudentorg/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/geostudentorg'),
(361432, 'Girl Gains', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Thursdays @8pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Our mission is to promote female weight lifting and empower women to feel strong and beautiful in a judgment free community. Whether you’re a dedicated gym goer or a curious beginner, Girl Gains is a college campus-originated organization and an evolving', 'Our mission is to promote female weight lifting and empower women to feel strong and beautiful in a judgment free community. Whether you’re a dedicated gym goer or a curious beginner, Girl Gains is a college campus-originated organization and an evolving online community here to support you in every stage of your fitness journey.', 'ucriversidegirlgains@gmail.com', 'https://girlgains.co', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrgirlgains/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/girlgains'),
(71039, 'Global Medical Brigades at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Thursdays at 6pm', 'Weeks 2, 4, 8', 'Stay connected by joining our 2026 Fall Quarter General Meetings!
They will be held on Thursdays of Weeks 2, 4, and 8 from 6–7 PM
Global Brigades is the world’s largest student-led global health and sustainable development organization. Since 2004, Global Brigades has mobilized thousands of university students and professionals through nine skill-based programs that work in partnership with community members to improve quality of life in under-resourced regions while respecting local culture.
Currently, Global Brigades has ten disciplines. Medical, dental, public health, water, microfinance, business, environmental, human rights, engineering, and architecture brigades all work in rural communities and represent the holistic model that Global Brigades follows. Students can have hands-on-experience in working in communities in any of these disciplines while respecting the culture and having first-hand experience of seeing the people''s lives they change through volunteer work.
Visit our Website for additional information!', 'Global Medical Brigades has mobilized students to work alongside with professionals and community members to improve the quality of life in under-resourced communities both locally and globally in countries such as Honduras, Panama, and Nicaragua.', 'Stay connected by joining our 2026 Fall Quarter General Meetings!
They will be held on Thursdays of Weeks 2, 4, and 8 from 6–7 PM
Global Brigades is the world’s largest student-led global health and sustainable development organization. Since 2004, Global Brigades has mobilized thousands of university students and professionals through nine skill-based programs that work in partnership with community members to improve quality of life in under-resourced regions while respecting local culture.
Currently, Global Brigades has ten disciplines. Medical, dental, public health, water, microfinance, business, environmental, human rights, engineering, and architecture brigades all work in rural communities and represent the holistic model that Global Brigades follows. Students can have hands-on-experience in working in communities in any of these disciplines while respecting the culture and having first-hand experience of seeing the people''s lives they change through volunteer work.
Visit our Website for additional information!
Add to our Spotify playlist!', 'gmb.ucr@gmail.com', 'http://www.globalbrigades.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/gmb_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gmb'),
(425654, 'Global Opportunities Abroad Leaders Initiative', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The GOALies program is focused on organizing student volunteers who wish to give back to their community, fostering cultural connections formed through experiences around the world, and giving students a resource to learn more about studying abroad.', null, null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrgoalies?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/goalies'),
(76547, 'Golden ARCHES', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization','Peer Educator Group']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Golden ARCHES involves and empowers UCR students to comprehensively and effectively address a wide variety of social health, wellness and leadership issues. The organization is made up of Lead Peer Health Educators and Volunteer Health Educators.', 'Advocating Responsible Choices through Health Education and Support
Golden ARCHES is a peer health education group at UC Riverside, focused on the topics of alcohol and other drugs, safe partying, sexual health, and nutrition & fitness.
Golden ARCHES believes in providing UC Riverside’s students with accurate and honest health information, skills, and resources, so students can make informed decisions that enhance their personal health and well-being.
Golden ARCHES peers are advocates for responsible decision-making when it comes to individuals’ health, and for creating a campus community that nurtures and supports these decisions.
Golden ARCHES peer educators gain valuable experience in health education programming, and serve as positive role models for their peers.', 'goldenarches@ucr.edu', 'https://well.ucr.edu/get-involved/golden-arches', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrgoldenarches', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/goldenarches'),
(425458, 'Google Developer Group, University of California, Riverside', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], null, 'Monthly', 'Google Developer Groups at the University of California, Riverside (GDG UCR) is a student-led technology community affiliated with the global Google Developer Groups (GDG) program. The organization provides an inclusive and collaborative environment for students interested in technology, innovation, and real-world problem solving.
GDG UCR is dedicated to helping students from diverse academic backgrounds explore Google technologies, develop technical and professional skills, and apply knowledge through hands-on learning. The organization hosts workshops, technical talks, speaker events, hackathons, and project-based activities, with an emphasis on practical skill development, peer learning, and experiential education.
Through engagement with the broader GDG community, as well as collaboration with campus partners and industry professionals, GDG UCR aims to bridge academic learning with industry-relevant practice while promoting ethical technology use, leadership development, and positive community impact.', 'Google Developer Group at UC Riverside (GDG UCR) is a student-led community that empowers students to learn, build, and collaborate through hands-on workshops, speaker events, hackathons, and projects focused on Google technologies and real-world impact.', 'Google Developer Groups at the University of California, Riverside (GDG UCR) is a student-led technology community affiliated with the global Google Developer Groups (GDG) program. The organization provides an inclusive and collaborative environment for students interested in technology, innovation, and real-world problem solving.
GDG UCR is dedicated to helping students from diverse academic backgrounds explore Google technologies, develop technical and professional skills, and apply knowledge through hands-on learning. The organization hosts workshops, technical talks, speaker events, hackathons, and project-based activities, with an emphasis on practical skill development, peer learning, and experiential education.
Through engagement with the broader GDG community, as well as collaboration with campus partners and industry professionals, GDG UCR aims to bridge academic learning with industry-relevant practice while promoting ethical technology use, leadership development, and positive community impact.', 'gdgatucr@gmail.com', 'https://gdg.community.dev/gdg-on-campus-university-of-california-riverside-riverside-united-states/', 'https://www.instagram.com/gdg_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gdg-ucr'),
(364229, 'Goths and Alts of UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Fridays 5-6pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Our club exists to create an inclusive haven for the exploration of alternative and goth culture, where members can connect through music, art, and aesthetics.', 'The purpose of this organization is to foster an inclusive community dedicated to the exploration, appreciation, and expression of alternative and goth cultures. Our mission is to provide a vibrant, supportive environment where enthusiasts of all backgrounds can connect through their shared passion for diverse music, art, fashion, and aesthetics within these subcultures. We aim to introduce and educate both newcomers and seasoned followers about the depth, diversity, and history of alternative and goth cultures. By hosting events, educational sessions, and creative showcases, we aspire to encourage artistic expression, cultural engagement, and meaningful connections. Our club welcomes everyone, regardless of prior knowledge or identification with these subcultures, to join us in celebrating and understanding the rich tapestry of individuality and community that defines our shared interests.', 'gothandaltsofucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gothsandaltsofucr'),
(430442, 'Gracecity UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Thursdays @6pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Gracecity UCR is a campus ministry under Christ Embassy. We''re dedicated to raising a generation of young men and women who will fulfil God''s dream for their lives. Our mission is to take God''s divine presence to the University of California, Riverside.', 'Giving your life a meaning.', 'ookir001@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gracecityucr'),
(71042, 'GradPREP', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], null, null, null, 'GradPREP is a graduate student organization focused on professionalization. It holds a variety of workshops and seminars dedicated to improving the graduate student experience at UCR.', 'GradPREP seeks to work with the graduate student community to develop writing, teaching, and speaking skills.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gradprep'),
(70852, 'Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA','Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], 'GSC: 7pm on the first Wed of every month', 'Monthly', '-----------------------------------------------------------
Land Acknowledgement: In honor of Rupert and Jeanette Costo’s founding relationship to our campus, we would like to respectfully acknowledge and recognize our responsibility to the original and current caretakers of this land, fire, water, and air: Íviatem (Cahuilla), Máara''yam (Serrano), Tóngva, and Payómkawichum (Luiseño) peoples, and all of their descendants past, present, and future. Today this meeting place is home to many Indigenous peoples from all over the world, including UCR faculty, students, and staff, and we are grateful to have the opportunity to live and work on these homelands.', 'The Graduate Student Association exists to advance, through our advocacy and programs, the academic, social, and physical environment of current and future graduate students at the University of California, Riverside.', 'The Graduate Student Association exists to advance, through our advocacy and programs, the academic, social, and physical environment of current and future graduate students at the University of California, Riverside.
-----------------------------------------------------------
Land Acknowledgement: In honor of Rupert and Jeanette Costo’s founding relationship to our campus, we would like to respectfully acknowledge and recognize our responsibility to the original and current caretakers of this land, fire, water, and air: Íviatem (Cahuilla), Máara''yam (Serrano), Tóngva, and Payómkawichum (Luiseño) peoples, and all of their descendants past, present, and future. Today this meeting place is home to many Indigenous peoples from all over the world, including UCR faculty, students, and staff, and we are grateful to have the opportunity to live and work on these homelands.', 'gsaucr@ucr.edu', 'http://gsa.ucr.edu', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_gsa', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gsaucr'),
(70910, 'Graduate Student Association for the Graduate School of Education', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'First Fridays of the Month', 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to provide opportunities including, but not limited to, scholarship and service for graduate students and alumni of the Graduate School of Education.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to provide opportunities including, but not limited to, scholarship and service for graduate students and alumni of the Graduate School of Education. In addition, this organization shall promote the interests of graduate students within GSOE to the Graduate Student Association main council.', 'abris002@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrsoe_scholarnetwork/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gsoe-gsa'),
(79818, 'Graduate Student Association Teacher Education Program Student Representative Committee', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'Friday from 4:00pm - 5:00pm', 'Monthly', null, 'The TEP SRC provides a voice for, and advocates on behalf of the Graduate School of Education TEP''s students. We serve as a medium of communication between the UCR GSE administration, the UCR GSA, and all five cohorts within the GSE TEP.', 'This organization represents students of the Teacher Education Program at UC Riverside. Our aim is to engage in student affairs and take on leadership roles in our campus community while pursuing careers as future educators.', 'nbarr049@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tep'),
(188601, 'Graduate Student Soccer Club', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'Wednesday at 7:00PM', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to encourage and enable graduate students in the UCR campus to participate in soccer as a mean of entertainment and stress relief.', 'Graduate Student Soccer Club (GSSC) intends to regularly arrange casual and non-competitive soccer games to promote participation by graduate students in relaxing sport activities. However, anybody is welcome to participate in the club and its games.', 'tanwa001@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gssc'),
(71069, 'Graduate Students in English Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'Our primary purpose is to ensure the welfare and representation of graduate students'' concerns at all relevant levels of the English Department''s business.', 'Our primary purpose is to ensure the welfare and representation of graduate students'' concerns at all relevant levels of the English Department''s business. We organize a variety of events such as lecture series, book sales, and the occasional get-together.', 'gseaucr@gmail.com', 'http://gsea.ucr.edu', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gsea'),
(70912, 'Graduate Students of Political Science', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Monday, 12pm', 'As needed', null, 'The Graduate Students of Political Science seeks to provide all graduate students in our department with the organizational structure and support to advance their needs and experience.', 'We represent graduate students of the Department of Political Science to the external academic community. Our goals are to advance the needs of our students, provide a forum for discussion, and heighten the internal cohesion of our student body.', 'gregory.hutchins@email.ucr.edu', 'https://sites.google.com/view/ucr-polisci-gsa/graduate-students', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/gsps'),
