*Flight information:
-Airline name
-Flight #
-Date and time of arrival
-Arrival airport
-What is the last departure city before arriving in the USA?
-How many large “checked-in” bags (luggage) and how many small “carry-on” bags will you have?
*Address we will take you to (你的目的地):
-------------------------------------------------
List additional help needed after you arrive: bank account, furniture, shopping for groceries, phone SIM card, etc.
The information is strictly for airport pickup and communicating with you about the Happy English Corner.
===========', 'ScotMyhrSoCal@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/happyenglishcorner'),
(364947, 'Health Clinical & Administrative Program', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays from 7:30-8:30pm', 'Monthly', null, 'The Clinical &amp; Administrative Program has been created to provide networking opportunities, clinical experiences, and an administrative background for Pre-Health Undergraduate Students at the University of California, Riverside.', 'Our mission is to educate our interns to embrace healthcare through a holistic lens
and prepare aspiring healthcare professionals to be well-versed in both the clinical and administrative aspects of healthcare. We have a variety of opportunities for pre-health students at our
UCR Health, UCPath and UCR School of Medicine sites.', 'UCR-Health-CAP@medsch.ucr.edu', 'https://medschool.ucr.edu/ucr-health-cap', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/health-cap'),
(386036, 'Health Exploration and Rotational Training Society at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesday Biweekly at 7pm', 'Every two weeks', 'The Health Exploration and Rotational Training Society (HEARTS) at UCR is devoted to assisting undergraduates in discovering their interests through exposure to various healthcare professions. Our organization serves as a forum for enhancing student knowledge of health careers. This includes our unique rotational training practice, which helps students connect with direct physician and patient care experience, professional development skills, and opportunities for educating populations of interest. We serve to connect our members to programs and opportunities in various healthcare fields. Most importantly, we aim to create a supportive environment for future physicians and scientists while supporting our members in their journey to accomplish their future endeavors.', 'HEARTS at UCR fosters undergraduates'' healthcare exploration through diverse experiences. Our unique rotational training program offers direct exposure to healthcare opportunities. We create a supportive environment for aspiring physicians and scientists', 'The Health Exploration and Rotational Training Society (HEARTS) at UCR is devoted to assisting undergraduates in discovering their interests through exposure to various healthcare professions. Our organization serves as a forum for enhancing student knowledge of health careers. This includes our unique rotational training practice, which helps students connect with direct physician and patient care experience, professional development skills, and opportunities for educating populations of interest. We serve to connect our members to programs and opportunities in various healthcare fields. Most importantly, we aim to create a supportive environment for future physicians and scientists while supporting our members in their journey to accomplish their future endeavors.', 'ucrhearts@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrhearts/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrhearts'),
(400394, 'Health Professions Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'HPA is an organization that aims to connect the undergraduate students of UC Riverside who are interested in pursuing a career in healthcare through mentorship, social events, professional development events, and community service events.', 'HPA is a premier professional pre-health organization founded on the idea of building a community of like-minded individuals who share in interest in various health fields including medicine, dentistry, pharmacy, physical therapy, optometry, etc.
Our primary focus is to enhance the professional and academic development of our members so that they are well prepared for their respective graduate schools.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrhpa/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/healthprofessionsassociation'),
(271864, 'Health Queers', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Generally during a weekday in the afternoon depending on member availability', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Health Queers provides support for LGBTQ+ students and allies involved in healthcare fields. We provide a space for students to network with other queer pre-health students and to educate others on the health disparities that affect our community.', 'Health Queers provides support for LGBTQ+ students and allies involved in healthcare and healthcare-adjacent fields. We provide a space for students to network with other queer pre-health students and to educate others on the health disparities that affect our community.', 'nmiya007@ucr.edu', 'https://linktr.ee/healthqueers.ucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/healthqueers.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/healthqueers'),
(414051, 'Healthy Heart Nation UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Thursdays at 5:30pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Our mission is to advance cardiovascular health awareness and promote health equity on campus and in the local community by uniting students from diverse fields to engage in clinical outreach, education, and service with underserved populations.', 'Healthy Heart Nation UCR is a student chapter of Healthy Heart Nation, a national nonprofit dedicated to improving cardiovascular health in underserved populations. Through this partnership, we participate in and host events organized by Healthy Heart Nation, including clinical outreach, health screenings, and educational workshops. These events are overseen by licensed healthcare professionals to ensure safe and effective delivery of care, while also providing UCR students with meaningful volunteer opportunities and professional development. These efforts allow us to bridge gaps in care and strengthen connections between the community and future healthcare professionals.', 'feyab001@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/healthyheartnationucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/healthyheartnationucr'),
(145303, 'Healthy Hearts Student Organization at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Thursday 6pm-7pm', 'Every two weeks', 'The primary purpose(s) of this organization is to provide helpful services to the community. It shall also raise awareness of heart related illnesses and to prevent the spread of heart related illnesses by educating the public on Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) protocol, lifestyle modifications information, and stress relief techniques as well as raising awareness on this illness. Furthermore, this organization aims to provide free CPR training to students and the general public.
Check us out at UCRHealthyHearts.org and/or follow us on Instagram @ucrhealthyhearts for weekly updates', 'It shall raise awareness of heart related illnesses and to prevent the spread of heart related illnesses by educating the public on Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) protocol, lifestyle modifications information, and stress relief technique', 'The primary purpose(s) of this organization is to provide helpful services to the community. It shall also raise awareness of heart related illnesses and to prevent the spread of heart related illnesses by educating the public on Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) protocol, lifestyle modifications information, and stress relief techniques as well as raising awareness on this illness. Furthermore, this organization aims to provide free CPR training to students and the general public.
