(367698, 'Highlander Economics Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'The Highlander Economics Club is a club founded to build a community of economics majors and any students interested in economics as a whole by providing access to professors, career panels, speaker events, and research opportunities.', 'The Highlander Economics Club is a club founded to build a community of economics majors and any students interested in Economics as a whole. Our goal is to support students in creating study groups, finding necessary resources to succeed in UCR, and connecting students with professors and employers. In addition, we hope to educate members about the many facets of economics through speaker events by professors, career panels, workshops, and research opportunities.', 'highlanderecon@gmail.com', 'https://discord.gg/m4d874dpwx', 'https://www.instagram.com/hec_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/highlandereconomicsclub'),
(282496, 'Highlander EMS', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'Highlander EMS is a student-run EMS organization dedicated to providing care during emergent and non-emergent situations for the UCR campus and surrounding communities. Each care-providing member is licensed by the California EMS Authority.', 'Highlander EMS is a student-run EMS organization dedicated to providing care during emergent and non-emergent situations for the UCR campus and surrounding communities. Each care-providing member is licensed by the California EMS Authority. In addition to providing care, we help students understand how to receive EMT licensure and guide them through the process.', 'highlanderems@gmail.com', 'http://www.highlanderems.com', 'www.instagram.com/highlanderems', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/highlanderems'),
(74673, 'Highlander Gaming', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Check our socials!', 'We host one in-person general meeting per quarter as the majority of our information is delivered online through Discord.', 'Founded in April 2012, Highlander Gaming is a student organization at the University of California, Riverside dedicated to fostering community through esports, gaming, and gaming culture. We bring together students and gamers from across UCR and Southern California to compete, connect, and share their passion for gaming.
Our mission is to build a welcoming community that embraces both competition and inclusion. Whether you''re a competitive player, casual gamer, content creator, or simply looking to meet others who share your interests, Highlander Gaming provides a space to connect, grow, and belong.
Our Story
Highlander Gaming began in 2012 as Esports at UCR, founded by a small group of friends with a shared passion for gaming. At the time, the organization primarily focused on StarCraft II and sought to create a community where gamers at UCR could connect, compete, and grow together.
Since then, Highlander Gaming has grown alongside the gaming and esports industry. Today, our community connects over 3,500 gamers across UCR and beyond, with programming that spans competitive esports, casual gaming, community events, and gaming culture.', 'Welcome to Highlander Gaming! We''re here to present a social and competitive atmosphere for games such as League of Legends, Valorant, Super Smash Bros Ultimate, and everything in between! Join our Discord! https://discord.gg/mrR8GpS4mZ', '2022 HighlanderCon Recap Video
Who We Are
Founded in April 2012, Highlander Gaming is a student organization at the University of California, Riverside dedicated to fostering community through esports, gaming, and gaming culture. We bring together students and gamers from across UCR and Southern California to compete, connect, and share their passion for gaming.
Our mission is to build a welcoming community that embraces both competition and inclusion. Whether you''re a competitive player, casual gamer, content creator, or simply looking to meet others who share your interests, Highlander Gaming provides a space to connect, grow, and belong.
Our Story
Highlander Gaming began in 2012 as Esports at UCR, founded by a small group of friends with a shared passion for gaming. At the time, the organization primarily focused on StarCraft II and sought to create a community where gamers at UCR could connect, compete, and grow together.
Since then, Highlander Gaming has grown alongside the gaming and esports industry. Today, our community connects over 3,500 gamers across UCR and beyond, with programming that spans competitive esports, casual gaming, community events, and gaming culture.
We host and support a wide range of events throughout the year, including Highlander Con, which brings together gamers, creators, artists, and communities from across Southern California. Our competitive teams represent UCR across titles such as VALORANT, League of Legends, Super Smash Bros. Ultimate, Marvel Rivals, and more, competing in collegiate and national-level competition.
Our Community
Highlander Gaming is powered by a dedicated team of students who volunteer their time, creativity, and expertise to strengthen our community. Our officers, directors, managers, and members work together to create opportunities for competition, leadership, collaboration, and personal growth.
We believe gaming is more than a hobby. It is a sport, a creative medium, and a community capable of bringing people together. We are committed to creating an environment where gaming can be celebrated in all its forms while providing our members with opportunities to compete, create, and connect.
Whether you''re here to compete, attend an event, make friends, or simply find your place in the gaming community, there''s a place for you at Highlander Gaming.
Website: https://www.highlandergaming.com/
Discord: discord.gg/hlg
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/hlg_ucr/
Twitter: https://twitter.com/hlg_ucr
Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/groups/hlgucr/
Twitch: https://www.twitch.tv/hlgucr
