aim to equip members with the skills and insights necessary for success in the dynamic field of health informatics.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hhiucr'),
(414953, 'Highlander Mixed Martial Arts Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to promote a healthy environment for people to learn, share knowledge, and grow as martial artists, regardless of background.', null, 'ucrmma234@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrmma'),
(71134, 'Highlander Mock Trial', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays and Thursdays at 7:00 p.m.', 'Tuesdays and Thursdays', null, 'We are a student-run organization that enables members to train and compete in trial tournaments hosted by The American Mock Trial Association. Check out our instagram @ucrmocktrial or email us at mocktrialucr@gmail.com for more information!', 'DO YOU. . .
WANT TO BE AN ATTORNEY?
WANT TO GET BETTER AT PUBLIC SPEAKING?
WANT TO LEARN MORE ABOUT THE LAW?
JOIN THE MOCK TRIAL TEAM AT UCR!
We are a diverse group of UCR students with various interests, levels of experience, and career goals. On our team, you can be an attorney or a witness. Attorney roles are for anyone interested law, debate, or public speaking. Witness actors receive a character to personify in court- whether it be a grieving mother, a business tycoon, or the number one suspect in a murder case!
WHAT DO WE DO?
FALL: At the beginning of Fall Quarter, we recruit new members to join our team. ***No experience required.*** Together, we analyze a case given to us by The American Mock Trial Association. We then teach you everything to prepare the best case possible!
WINTER: Our team takes our case to trial! We travel to places like the University of California Los Angeles, Cal Poly San Luis Obispo, and Arizona State University to compete in huge tournaments. Each of our trials are judged by real legal professionals.
SPRING: The competitive season is over, so a second wave of recruitment allows new members to learn everything in a more relaxed environment. This gives new members a great advantage to making it onto the following year''s competitive team!', 'mocktrialucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrmocktrial?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/themocktrialteamucr'),
(234311, 'Highlander MTG', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Wednesdays 6:30 - 9:30pm', 'Weekly', 'At HMTG, we provide Commander and Modern friendly games along with occasional drafts. Our goal as a club is to reach out to any students interested or already invested in the Magic: The Gathering trading card game and wish to find other like-minded individuals that are interested in learning how to play. Something new we are trying to implement into our club are fun side events to get all of our student community involved. Join our Discord at https://discord.gg/HSPWVRHyCJ and stay connected with other magical people!
We will be sharing our new meeting place and room for next quarter, so join the Discord to stay connected!', 'Highlander MTG aims to create a safe and friendly environment for others to play Magic: The Gathering by hosting weekly meetings, drafts, and other events! Join our Discord at: https://discord.gg/HSPWVRHyCJ', 'At HMTG, we provide Commander and Modern friendly games along with occasional drafts. Our goal as a club is to reach out to any students interested or already invested in the Magic: The Gathering trading card game and wish to find other like-minded individuals that are interested in learning how to play. Something new we are trying to implement into our club are fun side events to get all of our student community involved. Join our Discord at https://discord.gg/HSPWVRHyCJ and stay connected with other magical people!
We will be sharing our new meeting place and room for next quarter, so join the Discord to stay connected!', 'bliza008@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/hmtg_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hmtg'),
(71027, 'Highlander Networking Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'HNA is a club for students at UCR of any major to meet people, build real connections, and learn things classes don''t teach. We host events with alumni and professionals to help you build a network that lasts past graduation.', 'The Highlander Networking Association (HNA) exists to make meaningful professional connections accessible to every student at UC Riverside, regardless of major, background, or intended career path. While other organizations prepare students for one career path, HNA prepares students for any of them.
HNA bridges the gap between the classroom and the professional world. The organization equips members with the readiness, resources, and real-world context that coursework alone does not provide, helping students translate what they learn in class into skills and language that carry weight beyond UCR.
HNA is built on the belief that genuine relationships are the foundation of every career, not a transactional add-on to it. The organization creates spaces, through events, workshops, and community-building, where students form authentic connections across majors, years, and interests, breaking down what often separates one department from another.
HNA serves as a pipeline to connect members with industry professionals, alumni, employers, and each other, building a network that extends beyond graduation. The organization''s goal is not only to prepare students for their first job, but to give them a lasting community during their time here at UCR, and a set of skills that serve them across every career they will hold.
Opportunity should not be limited to students who already know the right people or the right path. HNA exists to ensure every Highlander has both.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/hna_ucr?stkn=MXBoZXJ6aDhheG44cA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/networksociety'),
(387355, 'Highlander Real Estate Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays 6-7pm', 'Weekly', 'Develop your public speaking skills through direct consulting experience with investors, agents, and those in the real estate industry.
We aim to become a trusted and influential group, helping both individuals and grow by focusing the practical uses of real estate. Whether it be building wealth, a career, or a hub to network with other likeminded individuals, we hope to establish a learning initiative to help students learn about how real estate can be a career for them.', 'The Highlander Real Estate Association empowers students through hands on consulting projects that solve real world real estate challenges. Members apply classroom knowledge to create value for clients while building technical and professional skills.', 'At the Highlander Real Estate Association, our goal and mission is to provide students with real life experiences in the real estate industry. Through our hands-on Consulting program, RECRUITING IN THE FALL, we connect students to projects that impact real people and communities.
Learn how to underwrite, value, and evaluate properties through qualitative and quantitative means. Learn how to use your financial, accounting, marketing, operations, and management skills in class, and apply them here! We''re looking for those who are open minded and are committed to an environment of fast-paced development.
Develop your public speaking skills through direct consulting experience with investors, agents, and those in the real estate industry.
We aim to become a trusted and influential group, helping both individuals and grow by focusing the practical uses of real estate. Whether it be building wealth, a career, or a hub to network with other likeminded individuals, we hope to establish a learning initiative to help students learn about how real estate can be a career for them.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrrealestateclub', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/highlanderrealestate'),
(381471, 'Highlander Skunk Works', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays 11am-1pm', 'Weekly', null, 'We are a small team of dedicated engineers from various backgrounds focused on fast paced innovation and iteration. Our club holds votes at least once a year and sometimes more than once a year on what engineering project/competition to join.', 'The purpose of this organization is to provide an environment where real world design and manufacturing experience can be acquired in a variety of topics ranging from computer science, electrical engineering, as well as mechanical engineering. This will be achieved by creating an atmosphere in which fast paced design iteration and prototyping is encouraged. This organization gives opportunities to apply skills learned in class through hands-on experience. Members will decide the projects/competitions that the club undertakes based on a vote from active members that will occur every time the previous project is completed.', 'amele037@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/highlanderskunkworks'),
(156080, 'Highlander Space Program', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Meeting times varies per sub-team and per quarter', 'Weekly', 'Discord Link!!: https://discord.gg/7JF38aJ3zP
The purpose of this organization shall be to promote and advance the study and practice of aerospace engineering among students at the University of California, Riverside. HSP seeks to provide a forum for its members to explore, develop, and enhance their technical skills while fostering a culture of innovation and creativity. The club shall achieve these objectives by conducting regular meetings, work sessions, and other related activities deemed appropriate and beneficial for its members.
HSP aims to create opportunities for its members to collaborate with industry professionals and organizations, as well as engage in hands-on projects and research that are relevant to aerospace engineering. Through these activities, the club hopes to provide its members with valuable learning experiences and enhance their understanding of aerospace engineering theories and principles.
Additionally, HSP seeks to promote public awareness and interest in the field through various outreach activities, such as recorded demonstrations, tabling, and educational events. The organization also aims to inspire and encourage the next generation of scientists and engineers by actively engaging with the wider community, particularly in the STEM community.
HSP is committed to maintaining an inclusive and welcoming environment that values diversity of thought and respects the rights and dignity of all its members. HSP shall operate per the relevant laws and regulations and shall be guided by its constitution and bylaws.', 'Highlander Space Program, formerly known as Aerospace Systems, aims to promote and advance the study and practice of aerospace engineering among students of the University of California, Riverside through hands-on experience with liquid rocket projects', 'Discord Link!!: https://discord.gg/7JF38aJ3zP
The purpose of this organization shall be to promote and advance the study and practice of aerospace engineering among students at the University of California, Riverside. HSP seeks to provide a forum for its members to explore, develop, and enhance their technical skills while fostering a culture of innovation and creativity. The club shall achieve these objectives by conducting regular meetings, work sessions, and other related activities deemed appropriate and beneficial for its members.
HSP aims to create opportunities for its members to collaborate with industry professionals and organizations, as well as engage in hands-on projects and research that are relevant to aerospace engineering. Through these activities, the club hopes to provide its members with valuable learning experiences and enhance their understanding of aerospace engineering theories and principles.
