(401232, 'Highlander Sports Business Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays 7 PM', 'Every two weeks', 'HSBA is a student-run organization dedicated to empowering a network of individuals who aspire to work in the field of sports business, connecting students to the dynamic world of sports management, marketing, and entrepreneurship. Through workshops, speaker series, and hands-on experiences, we bridge the gap between academic learning and industry practice, empowering our members to shape the future of the sports business.', 'Highlander Sports Business Association (HSBA) is an organization that aims to educate and empower UCR students who plan to pursue a career in sports business through providing students with opportunities for networking and professional development.', 'HSBA is a student-run organization dedicated to empowering a network of individuals who aspire to work in the field of sports business, connecting students to the dynamic world of sports management, marketing, and entrepreneurship. Through workshops, speaker series, and hands-on experiences, we bridge the gap between academic learning and industry practice, empowering our members to shape the future of the sports business.', 'hsbaucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hsbaucr'),
(70854, 'Highlander Statistics Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Varies', 'Monthly', null, 'UCR''s premier statistics and data science student organization.', 'The Highlander Statistics Society (HiSS) hosts workshops, projects, guest speakers, and social events for students interested in statistics and data science. Ever since our founding in 2010 HiSS has been a consistent source of support and opportunity for undergraduates. We also participate in the largest data hackathon on the West Coast at UCLA — DataFest.', 'highlanderstat@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/hiss.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hiss'),
(400327, 'Highlanderettes', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Mornings and/or evenings', 'Weekly', null, 'UCR Spirit Team enhancing the fan experience through cheer and dance.', null, 'compsports@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrspiritsquad/profilecard/?igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/highlanderettes'),
(132859, 'Highlanders Against Sexual Violence Peer Education Program', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Peer Educator Group']::text[], null, null, null, 'Are you passionate about sexual violence education and prevention? Do you want to get involved on campus in a meaningful way? Help us educate the UCR community on sexual assault, dating/domestic violence, stalking, and healthy sexuality!', 'The Highlanders Against Sexual Violence (HASV) Peer Education Program at UC Riverside was launched in the spring of 2015 to raise awareness throughout the UCR community about occurrences of sexual violence. It is the program’s goal to partner with on- and off-campus community resources in an effort to educate on the topics of sexual assault, dating/domestic violence, stalking and healthy sexuality. One of the objectives of the program is to promote activities and attitudes that will contribute to the elimination of acts of violence and to foster creating a safe atmosphere for all UCR community members. Peer educators play an important role by acting as student leaders on these issues, having the unique ability to access student populations, and are dedicated to working with the student body to create a campus culture that values respect and consent.
Students who have significant leadership experience and have demonstrated a commitment to sexual violence education and prevention (typically through commitment as peer educators) may serve as a peer coordinator and work in collaboration with the assistant vice chancellor of health and wellness, the Well’s interim director, Devon Sakamoto, and other campus administrators whose work focuses on sexual violence education and prevention such as the CARE advocate, Women’s Resource Center, LGBT Resource Center and Title IX, to fulfill the program’s goals.
Highlanders Against Sexual Violence is part of a larger cohort of student leaders participating in peer education called Power of the Peers. Students in this program are exposed to a variety of topics as they interact with the Power of the Peers network and have the ability to attend workshops, speaker series, and trainings led by professionals and fellow peers.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/itsonus'),
(70859, 'Hillel at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Office Hours: 9am-12:30pm and Bagel Wednesdays from 9am-12:30pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Hillel at UCR is a Jewish cultural, social, educational and religious organization. Hillel@UCR provides an opportunity for both Jewish and non-Jewish students, faculty and staff to explore Jewish identity within the university community.', 'Hillel at UCR is a Jewish cultural, social, educational and religious organization. Hillel provides an opportunity for both Jewish and non-Jewish students, faculty and staff to explore Jewish identity within the university community.', 'evaisben@iehillel.org', 'http://www.iehillel.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_hillel/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hillelucr'),
(364401, 'Hindu YUVA at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'Hindu YUVA (Youth for Unity, Virtues, and Action) is one of the fastest-growing Hindu youth organizations across the country with over presence in over 60 different universities. At UCR, we hope to create a safe space for Hindus to freely practice their faith on campus and bring more awareness about what the Hindu faith is really about. We aim to preserve, practice, promote, and protect our Hindu dharma (way of life) by authentically celebrating festivals, hosting guest speakers, and having interactive general body meetings. We welcome everyone interested in our vision of creating awareness around the Hindu faith and a stronger presence of Hindus across UCR. We hope to see you soon!', 'Hindu YUVA is a voluntary, non-profit, socio-cultural organization that aims to organize the Hindu students on campus in order to preserve, practice and promote Hindu culture, ideals and values.', 'Hindu YUVA (Youth for Unity, Virtues, and Action) is one of the fastest-growing Hindu youth organizations across the country with over presence in over 60 different universities. At UCR, we hope to create a safe space for Hindus to freely practice their faith on campus and bring more awareness about what the Hindu faith is really about. We aim to preserve, practice, promote, and protect our Hindu dharma (way of life) by authentically celebrating festivals, hosting guest speakers, and having interactive general body meetings. We welcome everyone interested in our vision of creating awareness around the Hindu faith and a stronger presence of Hindus across UCR. We hope to see you soon!', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrhinduyuva/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hinduyuvaucr'),
(385689, 'Hispanic Student Association at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Event dates and times are announced on our social media.', 'Every two weeks', 'At HISA we aim to create an environment inclusive of all Hispanic students. By sharing our respective cultures we strive to encourage diversity and create an environment that makes everyone feel welcome. Through various culturally themed events we motivate students to engage in social life and build on campus community.
Follow us on Instagram @hisa.ucr for updates on future events and meetings.', 'HISA is a cultural association dedicated to the appreciation of the Hispanic community at UCR.', 'At HISA we aim to create an environment inclusive of all Hispanic students. By sharing our respective cultures we strive to encourage diversity and create an environment that makes everyone feel welcome. Through various culturally themed events we motivate students to engage in social life and build on campus community.
Follow us on Instagram @hisa.ucr for updates on future events and meetings.', 'HISAUCR@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/hisa.ucr?igsh=MzY1NDJmNzMyNQ==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hisa'),
(70890, 'Hispanic Studies Graduate Student Organization', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Monday 2-3 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Association of Graduate Students in Hispanic Studies seeks to promote the interests of the graduate students in the UCR Hispanic Studies Department.', 'Preamble As graduate students in the Department of Hispanic Studies at the University of California, Riverside, we recognize the need to form a cohesive association to address issues related to graduate students and to continue the growth and development of our department. We believe that all students have the right to participate in decisions that affect the conditions and quality of their education. This participation requires meaningful, active, and respectful discourse among students, as well as positive and productive interaction between students and faculty. As decisions reached by both students and faculty impact the nature of the learning environment, it is the intention of the Graduate Students of the Hispanic Studies Department at UCR to ensure that the rights and responsibilities of all persons involved in the learning environment are not abridged. The name of this organization shall be Hispanic Studies Graduate Student Organization, hereafter referred to as the HSGSA, as it will appear throughout the constitution.', 'mvisc004@ucr.edu', 'http://ucrhispanics.blogspot.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/hsgradstudents/?hl=es', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hsgsa'),
(387356, 'History Enthusiasts at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 6:30', 'Weekly', null, 'To assist students with an interest in history by promoting interactions within the History department, cultivating a vibrant historical community, and mobilizing participation both on-campus and off-campus in history-related events.', 'To assist students interested in history(regardless of major) by promoting interactions within the History department, cultivating a vibrant historical community, and mobilizing on-campus and off-campus participation in history-related events.', 'historyenthusiastsucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/he_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/historymajorsassociation'),
(71110, 'History Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Varies', 'Monthly', null, 'The History Department mini-GSA organizes and represents the needs and activities for graduate students in the Department of History.', 'The History Department mini-GSA organizes and represents the needs and activities for graduate students in the Department of History.', 'historygsa@ucr.edu', 'http://hgsa.ucr.edu', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/historyminigsa'),
(347273, 'Hmong Student Association at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Thusdays 7:00 P.M.', 'Every two weeks', null, 'HSA @ UCR is dedicated to preserving Hmong culture and fostering a welcoming, inclusive community. We strive to be a "home away from home," providing a welcoming environment for individuals from all backgrounds and identities.', 'We offer social events, cultural workshops, academic support, and outreach to create meaningful connections and lifelong friendships. Whether you''re Hmong or simply interested in learning more, HSA @ UCR is a place to grow, engage, and celebrate diversity. Join us as we continue to build a strong and vibrant community together.', 'hsaucr@gmail.com', 'https://hsa.ucrhighlanders.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/hsa.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hsaucr'),
(158410, 'Hong Kong Students Association @UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Friday 6-8PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Hong Kong Students Association (HKSA), a student-based, school&nbsp;recognized cultural organization at UCR.', 'https://youtu.be/HaxPfQGkSsA
Hong Kong Students Association (HKSA), a student-based, school recognized cultural organization at UCR. We are dedicated to gathering and creating a sense of belonging for all Hong Kong students at UCR, as well as sharing and promoting traditional Hong Kong cultural values to students who are interested.
#Culture #Friendship #Experience', 'ucrivhksa@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrhksa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrhksa'),
(334135, 'Hooks for Hope', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Varies; Usually After 4PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Hooks for Hope is an organization that aims to provide handmade crochet makes for the local community and to share the love of the craft with other students.', 'Hooks for Hope is dedicated to making handmade crochet makes for the local community by gathering UCR students who love to crochet. Each crochet item is crafted with love and is one of a kind. Our mission is to bring individuals lots of joy and show them that each of them are unique and loved in different ways, just like their plushies. Part of our mission includes fostering a sense of community for crocheters on the UCR campus. Both new and experienced crocheters are welcome to club events.', 'ucrhooksforhope@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrhooksforhope/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrhooksforhope'),
(283164, 'HOSA - Future Health Professionals', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesday and Thursdays, 6:30pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'UCR HOSA is a pre-health organization that serves students in serving UCR and the surrounding community by volunteering, networking, and socializing with students alike. We compete in leadership conferences in order to better prepare for future careers.', 'UCR HOSA is a pre-health organization that serves students in serving UCR and the surrounding community by volunteering, networking, and socializing with students alike. We compete in leadership conferences in order to better prepare for future careers.', 'ucrhosa@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrhosa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrhosa'),
(362006, 'Hungry 4 Biscuits', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'We raise awareness about food insecurity, empower students to contribute meaningfully, and offer access to resources like Basic Needs and CalFresh. Through volunteer efforts, we aim to support both the UCR campus and the greater Inland Empire community.', 'Hungry 4 Biscuits is a student-led organization committed to addressing food insecurity across UCR and the Inland Empire. We raise awareness, provide access to resources like Basic Needs and CalFresh, and offer volunteer opportunities that empower students to make a meaningful impact. Through educational initiatives, tabling events, and service projects, we aim to support our community with compassion and purpose. Follow us on Instagram (@hungry4biscuits_ucr) for updates and join anytime to be part of the movement!', 'ucr.hungry4biscuits@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/hungry4biscuits_ucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/hungry4biscuits_ucr/  https://www.instagram.com/hungry4biscuits_ucr/   Share', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/h4b'),
(101117, 'Hylander Financial Group', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays 7-9 pm', 'Weekly', 'Hylander Financial Group is UCR''s premier investment finance student organization. Our goal is to provide students with invaluable hands-on portfolio management, equity research, and investment experiences through our two student managed investment funds. Students of all disciplines and levels of financial expertise are welcome to come learn about the basics of investing and the field of finance. Through our educational, social, and career-related events along with our professional competitions and portfolio teams, HFG serves as a valuable opportunity for students to elevate their careers and financial prowess. Our general meetings are open to anyone interested and are on Mondays from 7 pm to 8 pm, followed by HSIF from 8 pm to 9 pm. We look forward to seeing you!', 'Founded in 2013, Hylander Financial Group (HFG) was established to help UCR students learn successful investing techniques, build networks in finance, and provide practical knowledge to the UCR community about the financial industry.', 'Hylander Financial Group is UCR''s premier investment finance student organization. Our goal is to provide students with invaluable hands-on portfolio management, equity research, and investment experiences through our two student managed investment funds. Students of all disciplines and levels of financial expertise are welcome to come learn about the basics of investing and the field of finance. Through our educational, social, and career-related events along with our professional competitions and portfolio teams, HFG serves as a valuable opportunity for students to elevate their careers and financial prowess. Our general meetings are open to anyone interested and are on Mondays from 7 pm to 8 pm, followed by HSIF from 8 pm to 9 pm. We look forward to seeing you!', 'hylanderfinancial@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/UCRHFG', 'https://www.instagram.com/hfgucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hylanderfinancial'),
(161799, 'Indian Students Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'First or second week of every month.', 'Monthly', null, 'The Indian Students'' Association aims at creating a common ground for all students interested in culture and traditions of India.', 'The purpose of this organization is to build a community for Indian students and people interested in Indian culture wherein they find support and a homely environment. This would also give the students a chance to celebrate their culture in a foreign country. The Indian community is full of diverse cultures wherein people from different regions bring about a conducive and cheerful atmosphere to share with everyone. The large number of Indian students in the university will be able to bond and relate with students having similar interests and share their cultural heritage.', 'isa.highlanders@gmail.com', 'https://isaucr.carrd.co/', 'https://www.instagram.com/isa.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/indianstudentsassociation'),
(321326, 'Inland Empire Street Care', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'We work to allow for more accessible healthcare, build relationships and trust, and provide resources and support for persons experiencing homelessness in our local community.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to allow for more accessible healthcare to persons experiencing homelessness in the local community. Our goal is to build relationships and trust with persons experiencing homelessness by offering access to resources and support. By building rapport with this population, we hope to foster more long-term relationships between persons experiencing homelessness and primary care clinicians in the area. Through organizing a bi-monthly clinic with local health care providers, local community organizations, and undergraduate volunteers, we can bridge the gap between the homeless population and the medical community', 'smcclinicmanager@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/inlandempirestreetmed/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/inlandempirestreetcare'),
(71587, 'Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Spring 2026 Meetings Thursday 5-6pm', 'Every two weeks', 'Micromouse
An autonomous robot built from scratch that can navigate through a 16x16 cell maze. Meetings and workshops are held once a week. The IEEE@UCR Micromouse teams compete in multiple collegiate competitions across Southern California.
Contact: ieee@ee.ucr.edu
RoboSub
UCR RoboSub is one of IEEE’s large-scale projects that consists of multidisciplinary teams composed of around 20 active members that work year-long to collaboratively create an autonomous submarine from scratch used to compete in the international RoboSub competition hosted annually by RoboNation in San Diego in the summer.', 'IEEE at UCR is an organization dedicated to providing engineers with technical, social, and professional development in the engineering field.', 'IEEE Promotional Video
What is IEEE?
IEEE stands for the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers. It is abbreviated to IEEE [ahy-trip-uhl-ee] and is officially referred to as such.
Our Mission
Our mission as the local chapter is to provide engineers with technical, social, and professional development in the engineering field. We aim to be the leading engineering organization on campus, providing more opportunities for student improvement outside the classroom. We are committed in providing engineers with career enhancement, engineering social events, and growth in their respective professions.
Projects
Our organization hosts four student projects: Micromouse, Unmanned Aerial Systems (UAS), RoboSub, and Solar Car. They are all open to everyone to participate.
Micromouse
An autonomous robot built from scratch that can navigate through a 16x16 cell maze. Meetings and workshops are held once a week. The IEEE@UCR Micromouse teams compete in multiple collegiate competitions across Southern California.
Contact: ieee@ee.ucr.edu
RoboSub
UCR RoboSub is one of IEEE’s large-scale projects that consists of multidisciplinary teams composed of around 20 active members that work year-long to collaboratively create an autonomous submarine from scratch used to compete in the international RoboSub competition hosted annually by RoboNation in San Diego in the summer.
Contact: ieee@ee.ucr.edu
Website: https://robosub.ucr.edu
Unmanned Aerial Systems
A highly motivated group of students designing, constructing and programming an autonomous aerial vehicle to compete in the annual AUVSI-SUAS competition in Maryland. Through UCR-UAS, students have the unique opportunity to hone their engineering skills and develop a product from start to finish.
Contact: ieee@ee.ucr.edu
Website: https://ucr-uas.weebly.com
Solar Car
A multidisciplinary team comprised of highly motivated undergraduate students that aim to build a solar-powered vehicle. Their mission is to promote a future of alternative energy and sustainable transportation projects at UC Riverside, contribute to Southern California’s growing technology ecosystem, and raise community awareness of the power of solar energy.
Contact: ieee@ee.ucr.edu
Website: https://ucrsolarcar.com
Come Visit Us!
Our clubroom, Solarium, is located in Winston Chung Hall, Rm. 221. It''s open 24/7 with card access. Closed during the summer.
We also have a Discord Server!', 'ieee@ee.ucr.edu', 'http://ieee.ee.ucr.edu', 'https://www.instagram.com/ieeeucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ieee'),
(403409, 'Institute of Transportation Engineers at University of California, Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'To build a community of future transportation professionals at UC Riverside, advancing sustainable solutions with CE-CERT resources. Through research, networking, and partnerships, we equip members to tackle mobility, safety, and environmental challenges', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to foster an engaged community of future transportation professionals at the University of California, Riverside, a leading institution in sustainable and intelligent transportation systems (SITS). The chapter promotes a diverse array of research projects and engineering applications, leveraging the extensive resources available within the College of Engineering’s Center for Environmental Research & Technology (CE-CERT). We will also organize workshops, guest lectures, and project activities to equip members with the skills to tackle complex transportation, air quality, energy, and climate change challenges. Additionally, we will collaborate with other ITE chapters in Southern California to provide networking opportunities for transportation engineering students across campuses. Our partnerships with CE-CERT and the regional transportation agencies will enhance the understanding of advanced mobility technologies, such as connected and automated vehicles, and transportation electrification. Ultimately, our goal is to educate and inspire the next generation of transportation engineers to create sustainable solutions focused on safety, mobility, environmental resilience, accessibility, and equity.', 'iteucr@gmail.com', 'https://discord.gg/qTupNcrMNW', 'https://www.instagram.com/ite_ucr/?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/iteatucr'),
(71068, 'Interfraternity Council (IFC)', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Thursdays at 3pm', 'Weekly', null, 'The object of this organization shall be to promote the general welfare of all member fraternities; to encourage the development and growth of the IFC at UCR members; to provide educational, social & service activities that will enhance member experienc', 'The object of this organization shall be to promote the general welfare of all member fraternities; to encourage the development and growth of the Inter-Fraternal Council at UCR members; to provide educational, social and philinthropic activities to enhance our member''s University experience.', 'ucr.ifcpresident@gmail.com', 'http://ucr-ifc.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/ifc_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ifc'),
(71152, 'InterVarsity Christian Fellowship', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Monday 7:00-9:00 pm', 'Weekly', null, 'InterVarsity at UCR is about building a joyful and authentic community for students of any ethnic, cultural background to encounter Jesus, and empowering them to boldly take risks for the Gospel on every corner of campus and beyond.', 'https://youtu.be/MHDhE1HDVkc
InterVarsity at UCR is about building a joyful and authentic community for students of any ethnic, cultural background to encounter Jesus, and empowering them to boldly take risks for the Gospel on every corner of campus and beyond.', 'csous003@ucr.edu', 'https://linktr.ee/InterVarsityUCR', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_intervarsity/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ivcf'),
(104867, 'Iranian Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'IGSA is a voluntary student organization with the objective of promoting Iranian culture by sponsoring and holding social events, and to create a platform to introduce Persian culture to the non-Persian community.', 'The Iranan Graduate Student Association (IGSA) is a non-political voluntary student organization whose objective is to sponsor Iranian social and cultural activities and events, to promote an understanding of Iranian culture, to help foster friendship among different cultural groups, and to provide a source of union and support for the Iranian community at UCR.', 'ucrigsa@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrigsa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/igsa'),
(70896, 'Iranian Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Thursday 7PM', 'Every other week', null, 'ISA is a student organization on the UCR campus dedicated to raising awareness and understanding of the Persian culture. It is open to every UCR student interested in learning more about Iran and its culture.', 'To promote unity among Iranians, discuss and advocate for common interests such as politics and national history. Considered a Social/Cultural Organization! We host events almost every week for everyone to come and enjoy.
Join us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/isaatucr/', 'ucriranianstudentassociation@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/isaatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/isa'),
(425237, 'Jesus Nights', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Once a month on Fridays around 6-7pm', 'Monthly', null, 'Jesus Nights are worship nights where we create a space for God to move and encounter us. Whether you believe in God or still on the line, you are welcome! Come find community and enjoy the music, as we praise Jesus and ask him to move in our lives.', 'Jesus Nights are worship nights where we create a speace for God to move and encounter us. Whether you believe in God or you''re still on the line, you are welcome to join us. There will be a community of believers and amazing worship with moments to share testimonies and verses in between songs. We are believing for a move of God as individuals and as a community and would love if these nights brought encouragement to you in you faith journy.', 'jesusnightsucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/jesusnights'),
(424814, 'Joining Undergraduates in Civic Enagement', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Thursdays at 5 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Create a community at UCR that supports and empowers students to address civic issues they are passionate about through community building and civic engagement.', 'JUICE Club aims to explore how participation in community service and civic engagement not only benefits the community at large, but also strengthens community, builds connections, and promotes a sense of fulfillment and belonging among student volunteers. In alignment with its community values, JUICE Club encourages and supports student members to engage with civic issues they are passionate about.', 'juiceclubucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/juiceclubucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/juiceclub'),
(380734, 'KADENCE UCR Cover Team', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Tuesdays, Thursdays from 8 pm to 10 pm', 'Weekly', null, 'A cover team based around live singing and dancing that is open to anyone who has a love for kpop, jpop, p-pop and more! While this is a cover team everyone is welcome! Officer positions are available! You don''t need to sing or dance to join!', 'https://youtube.com/shorts/L86wCr1CrJs?si=MZNeoXKfs9XRXZUS', 'kadencedanceucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://instagram.com/kadenceucr?igshid=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/kadenceucrkpopdanceteam'),
(400387, 'Kappa Alpha Pi', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesday 8:00 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose of the Kappa Alpha Pi Fraternity at the University of California, Riverside shall be
to provide students with the opportunity to learn about the Law School application process, Law
School, and the profession of law.', 'The purpose of the Kappa Alpha Pi Fraternity at the University of California, Riverside shall be to provide students with the opportunity to learn about the Law & Graduate School application process, Law School, and the profession of law. This goal will be achieved by providing the membership with the opportunity to participate in events focused on law and service designed to help the legal community. This fraternity will also provide its members access to people in the area of law and government. Above all, this fraternity and its membership will strive to create a fellowship in the form of a fraternal bond between members of the organization, thereby providing the members with personal experiences to aid their search for information about law and law-related areas.', 'presidentucrkapi@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrkapi/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrkapi'),
(158111, 'Kappa Alpha Psi Fraternity, Inc.', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'First Saturday at 9am', 'Monthly', null, 'Kappa Alpha Psi Fraternity, Incorporated was founded January 5, 1911 on the campus of Indiana University. Our Fundamental Purpose is &quot;Achievement in Every Field of Human Endeavor&quot;.', 'Kappa Alpha Psi Fraternity, Incorporated was founded January 5, 1911 on the campus of Indiana University. Our Fundamental Purpose is "Achievement in Every Field of Human Endeavor". We were found by ten illustrious founders by the names of Elder Watson Diggs, Ezra D. Alexander, Byron K. Armstrong, Henry T. Asher, Marcus P. Blakemore, Paul W. Caine, George W. Edmonds, Guy L. Grant, Edward G. Irvin, John Milton Lee.
The Eta Zeta Chapter of Kappa Alpha Psi Fraternity, Incorporated was chartered on March 22, 1974 and is a member of the Western Province.', 'kboyl008@ucr.edu', 'http://www.kappaalphapsi1911.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/hznupes/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/kappa-alpha-psi-fraternity-inc'),
(70930, 'Kappa Kappa Gamma Sorority', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Monday at 7pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Kappa Kappa Gamma is an organization of women, which seeks for every member throughout her life bonds of friendship, mutual support, opportunities for self-growth, respect for intellectual development, and an understanding of positive ethical principles.', 'Kappa Kappa Gamma is an organization of women, which seeks for every member throughout her life bonds of friendship, mutual support, opportunities for self-growth, respect for intellectual development, and an understanding of and an allegiance to positive ethical principles.', 'epsilonpi.president@gmail.com', 'http://chapters.kappakappagamma.org/epsilonpi/pages/welcome.php', 'http://www.instagram.com/kkg_ucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/kappa'),
(70918, 'Karate Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Saturdays 12:00-1:00pm', 'Weekly', null, 'The Karate Club at UCR strives to enhance lessons and knowledge of Karate-Do. It''s mission is to promote the martial art and continue the tradition of excellence at tournaments.', 'Mission
The Karate Club @ UCR helps to relieve stress and keep a healthy regime in between studies. It reviews the materials needed for an individual to compete with the karate team at local, national and international competitions.
The Karate Club @ UCR mission tri-fold:
First: To enhance the camaraderie and reinforce the lessons of karate-do on the UCR campus.
Second: To establish and maintain an organization for promoting sport karate and competition for its members.
Third: To represent UCR with excellence and integrity.', 'lmart232@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/karate'),
(420286, 'Karing Kits', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Thursdays, 7:30PM', 'Weekly', 'Our mission is to increase access to feminine hygiene products in nearby areas to homeless women. While these kits are not made exclusively of feminine hygiene products, they are directed at maintaining adequate access to these cleaning products in order to help reduce the amount of avoidable illnesses caused by lack of resources and accessibility. These illnesses include, but are not limited to, toxic shock syndrome, UTIs/RTIs, fertility issues, yeast infections, increased risk of cervical cancer, and bacterial vaginosis. While many of these illnesses are not deadly, they are avoidable when good feminine hygiene is practiced. Most local homeless shelters do not provide basic cleaning supplies for women since these are seen as “nonessential” supplies, in comparison to clothes and food. This is a precarious misconception that endangers the health, comfort, and safety of the women living in these unfavorable conditions. Our goal is to provide the items and support needed to keep these women healthy, clean, and happy while expanding and serving our community.', 'Our mission is to increase accessibility to feminine hygiene products to local homeless women. The kits are directed at maintaining adequate access to cleaning products in order to help fight period poverty and related illnesses.', 'Our mission is to increase access to feminine hygiene products in nearby areas to homeless women. While these kits are not made exclusively of feminine hygiene products, they are directed at maintaining adequate access to these cleaning products in order to help reduce the amount of avoidable illnesses caused by lack of resources and accessibility. These illnesses include, but are not limited to, toxic shock syndrome, UTIs/RTIs, fertility issues, yeast infections, increased risk of cervical cancer, and bacterial vaginosis. While many of these illnesses are not deadly, they are avoidable when good feminine hygiene is practiced. Most local homeless shelters do not provide basic cleaning supplies for women since these are seen as “nonessential” supplies, in comparison to clothes and food. This is a precarious misconception that endangers the health, comfort, and safety of the women living in these unfavorable conditions. Our goal is to provide the items and support needed to keep these women healthy, clean, and happy while expanding and serving our community.', 'our.karing.kits@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr.karing.kits?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/karingkits'),
(70957, 'Kendo Club @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesdays/Thursdays 8:30 PM-10:30 PM at Multiple Purpose Room D', '2 times a week', 'The purpose of our organization is to introduce the martial art of Kendo to UCR.
Our organization would like to find students who are interested in Kendo throughout the University. Since other UC''s have their own Kendo organizations, we are able to connect UCR to other schools through Kendo related activities. Our main goals are to practice Kendo and to teach cultural values, traditions, and the art at UCR.
We participate in multiple tournaments throughout the year such as Yuhihai at UCLA, and Shoryuhai at Harvard University. In past years, we have consistently placed highly at these tournaments. For example, at the 2018 Yuhihai Tournament, our members placed First in the Co-ed Division, Second in the Kyu Individuals Division, and Third in the Kyu Team Division.
Beginners are welcome and encouraged to come out to practice. No prior experience is necessary. Wear clothes that are easy to move around in and an open mind.
Our Current Practice times are:
Tuesday 8:30-10:30PM at MPR D at the Student Recreation Center
Thursday 8:30-10:30PM at MPR D at the Student Recreation Center
Discord Server Link:
https://discord.gg/XvrtWr9vAV
We will have all our announcements on Discord!', 'We meet and practice Kendo, no prior experience necessary.', 'The purpose of our organization is to introduce the martial art of Kendo to UCR.
Our organization would like to find students who are interested in Kendo throughout the University. Since other UC''s have their own Kendo organizations, we are able to connect UCR to other schools through Kendo related activities. Our main goals are to practice Kendo and to teach cultural values, traditions, and the art at UCR.
We participate in multiple tournaments throughout the year such as Yuhihai at UCLA, and Shoryuhai at Harvard University. In past years, we have consistently placed highly at these tournaments. For example, at the 2018 Yuhihai Tournament, our members placed First in the Co-ed Division, Second in the Kyu Individuals Division, and Third in the Kyu Team Division.
Beginners are welcome and encouraged to come out to practice. No prior experience is necessary. Wear clothes that are easy to move around in and an open mind.
Our Current Practice times are:
Tuesday 8:30-10:30PM at MPR D at the Student Recreation Center
Thursday 8:30-10:30PM at MPR D at the Student Recreation Center
Discord Server Link:
https://discord.gg/XvrtWr9vAV
We will have all our announcements on Discord!
Instagram Link:
https://www.instagram.com/kendo_ucr
Check out previous events and catch us during outreach!', 'kendo.ucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/kendo_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/kendo'),
(430992, 'Kidney Disease Screening and Awareness Program @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'KDSAP at UC Riverside empowers students to serve their community by providing kidney health education, organizing free CKD screening events, and promoting preventive healthcare through collaboration with physicians and community partners.', 'UCR KDSAP is a student-led chapter dedicated to promoting kidney health, preventive care, and early detection. We organize educational workshops, awareness campaigns, volunteer opportunities, community outreach, and free screening events under the supervision
of licensed healthcare professionals. Membership is open to students of all majors who are interested in health education, service, leadership, and improving access to preventive resources throughout Riverside and the Inland Empire.', 'ucrkdsap@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrkdsap/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrkdsap'),
(406911, 'Kindred Volunteer Collective', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Wednesdays ~7 -9 pm; Saturdays All Day', 'Weekly', null, 'Make an impact! We raise awareness among various causes & uplift student groups through philanthropy & service. Driven by inclusion, integrity, innovation, & passion, we foster a supportive community for positive change.', 'Join us in building a more inclusive and equitable future! Our organization is dedicated to bringing more attention to various causes and uplifting student groups through tangible acts of philanthropy and service. We believe in the power of collective action to create real change. We''re driven by our core values of passion, accountability, innovation, and inclusion, and we invite you to be a part of our mission to foster a supportive community where everyone thrives. Become a member and help us make a lasting impact! Please follow our IG for more info!', null, 'kindredvc.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/kindred_vc/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/kindred'),
(165296, 'Klesis Christian Fellowship', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Typical meetings will be Friday at 6:30 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'Klesis is a Christian fellowship that provides opportunities for students to explore life together, learn and live out their Christian faith in community.', 'Klesis is a Christian fellowship that provides opportunities for students to explore life together, learn and live out their Christian faith in community. Our aim is to disciple Christians to grow in connecting with God, live out a biblical community, grow in our faith, and get questions answered about the Bible or Christianity.', 'czhou092@ucr.edu', null, 'http://instagram.com/klesis_ucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/klesis'),
(70959, 'Korean American Student Association (KASA)', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Monday/Tuesday 7:00PM', 'Weekly', null, 'To promote the educational and enrichment of its members and the University community with aspects of Korean culture through involvement and participation in various social, cultural and political activities.', 'KASA is a club that not only aims to strengthen unity among the student body, but to also promote awareness of Korean/Korean American culture and serve as a channel for students with similar backgrounds to come together through various social outreach events.
On a less formal note, KASA is an all-inclusive club started to bring students with similar interests closer together by experiencing Korean and Korean American culture, as well as a “home away from home” :)', 'ucriversidekasa@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/ucriversidekasa', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrkasa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/kasa'),
(71059, 'Kristos Campus Mission', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Thursdays at 8:30 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'To be a biblical community of believers demonstrating the gospel of Christ both locally and globally to the glory of God. To fulfill the Great Commission by mobilizing and discipling collegians.', 'We aim to be a biblical community of believers demonstrating the gospel of Christ both locally and globally to the glory of God. To fulfill the Great Commission by mobilizing and discipling collegians.', 'jchoi342@ucr.edu', 'https://kcm.network/', 'https://www.instagram.com/riversidekcm?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/kcm'),
(120687, 'La Hermandad de UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 6:30', 'Weekly', null, 'La Hermandad de UCR is a healing, growing, and empowering cultural non-profit organization. Our events are open to anyone, anytime. Our efforts are focused on increasing the rates of graduation & matriculation among the Latine population.', 'La Hermandad de UCR (HUCR) is a cultural organization with the goal to create a welcoming environment where students at UCR can thrive and succeed while contributing to the Chicane/Latine community.
We focus our efforts towards increasing the matriculation, retention, and graduation rates among the Chicane/Latine student population. We will achieve this through the guidance of our three pillars: Academic Excellence, Community Service, and Social Networking.
As “La Nueva Persona”, we will strive to spread our philosophy of Hermandad as a stepping-stone towards creating a sense of familia on the UCR campus and in the (local) Riverside community. With the understanding that Chicane/Latine students traditionally face institutional, societal, and internal struggles, HUCR aims to address and surpass these historical adversities. Our mission is to impact our community and serve as leaders to incoming Chicane/Latine students. By becoming contributing members of our society, we can encourage others to follow in our footsteps.
Fuerza en La Hermandad', 'lahermandaddeucr@gmail.com', 'https://gmail.us14.list-manage.com/subscribe?u=664de2b46da1e371e3f0a14df&id=d5c1a6870a', 'https://www.instagram.com/hermandaducr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/lahermandaddeucr'),
(70869, 'La Union Estudiantil de la Raza (UER)', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Mondays, 10:00 p.m.', 'Weekly', null, '"Knowledge, Unity, Brotherhood, Raza"', 'La Unión Estudiantil de la Raza, Inc. was founded on October 6, 1992 at the University of California, Riverside by ten individuals. They had an idea that there needed to be a place where one could feel comfortable and respected without any animosity for what one thought, felt, or believed. The members analyzed the purpose and decided to create an organization that would create leaders by focusing on incorporation of ethnicity with indigenous cultures. It was decided on this day that the members would work together to incorporate in the university a Chicano-Latino/Indigenous organization that was different from the Greek system.
La Union Estudiantil de la Raza, Inc. has a distinctly different agenda that differs from the existing fraternal order. Our pledge ship is a non-hazing learning process of integration where incoming members can comfortably enter our Brotherhood. Our social atmosphere consists of recreational activities as well as scholastic and moral support. Our social activities involve unification gatherings of Chicano/Latino students, cultural trips, retreats, fundraisers, and intramural sports with other organizations on campus.
