"Que Viva UER!, Que VIVA!!!"', 'uercasadehermanos1992@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/uer_official_?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/uer'),
(400398, 'LabLink', 'Registered Student Organization', null, 'Wednesdays or Thursdays from 8-9 pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Our goal is to promote equitable research access by creating online research training modules that will better prepare students for lab research as well as improving scientific literacy and professional skills.', 'Our goal is to promote equitable research access by creating online research training modules that will better prepare students for lab research.
This club is a part of an effort to help connect students with research faculty in order to expose willing candidates to scientific (life/physical/engineering) research, while connecting faculty with UG assistants. To do this, we have partnered with Gladis Herrera-Berkowitz and the UG research office to improve the research portal and explore future collaborations to reach more students.
We aim to provide scientific literacy and improve professional skills through communication workshops, guest speakers, and resume/CV builders.
LabLink Introduction', 'lablinkucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/lablinkucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/lablinkucr'),
(402548, 'Labor Council for Latin American Advancement', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 5 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The LCLAA Student Alliance empowers college students nationwide to advocate for social justice and economic equality for the Latine community. Through campus chapters, students gain leadership, education, and advocacy skills to support Latine workers.', 'The Labor Council for Latin American Advancement (LCLAA) Student Alliance is dedicated to promoting social justice and economic equality for the Latine community in the United States. By establishing student chapters on college campuses nationwide, we empower students to become advocates in their community, fostering leadership, education, and political engagement. Our mission is to provide college students with opportunities for professional development, access to critical educational resources, and the skills needed to champion policies that benefit Latine workers and their families. Through our affiliated chapters, we aim to cultivate a new generation of informed, motivated, and socially conscious leaders committed to the principles of equality and justice.', 'ucr@lclaa.org', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucr-lclaa'),
(70955, 'Lambda Sigma Gamma', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 8pm', 'Monthly', null, 'Our organization''s objective is to instill the desire for self-improvement and to promote unity and higher education among women. We want to empower women from all different backgrounds. We believe in beauty through diversity and unity through sisterhood', 'While Lambda Sigma Gamma remains active in a wide variety of philanthropic services, the sorority’s main objective is to bring awareness and support to early Education. Their responsibility and commitment to making a meaningful difference in the lives of children continually guides our efforts. They do this by giving back to their communities via scholarships, fundraisers, donations, contributions, partnerships, volunteerism and other various philanthropic programs at each of our respective chapters.', 'scast162@ucr.edu', 'https://lambdasigmagamma.org/', 'http://instagram.com/ucr_lsg', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ipse'),
(71145, 'Lambda Theta Alpha Latin Sorority, Inc.', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Monday', 'Weekly', null, 'LTA serves as a sisterhood based on unity, love, and respect. To provide social and cultural activities and to carry on charitable and educational programs, while strengthening leadership, and ultimately maintaining high academic standards.', 'Lambda Theta Alpha serves to provide a sisterhood based on unity, love, and respect. Our goal is to provide social and cultural activities and to carry on charitable and educational programs; all while strengthening leadership, maintaining high academic standards, and ultimately serving as a voice for UCR community.
Lambda Theta Alpha Latin Sorority Inc, was established at the University of California, Riverside on May of 2001 on the basis of academia achievement with goals of community and political activism. Lambda Theta Alpha’s desire for progress, dedication to its community, and the aspiration for advancement of the Universal Women, has paved the way for many successful events in strengthening women of all creeds since its establishment here at UCR. Although we are traditionally a Latina Sorority, we do not define as so, for many independent, and strong women of all races, ethnicities, and creeds have come into our organization and succeeded as educated women.
Furthermore, amongst our many achievements we have also been recognized nationally for our philanthropy: St. Judes Research Hospital, as the Latina Sorority of the Year by NALFO, and Latinogreeks.org, and even more recently, as the winner of Voto Latino''s ''Rep Ur Letters'' Challenge by Successfully Implementing a Political Education Initiative in this past November’s Presidential Elections. Not to mention, we were the recipients of the 2011-2012, Scholarship Pillar Award in recognition of our commitment to outstanding academic achievements, at the Pillars Banquet this past year.
Ultimately as an organization, Lambda Theta Alpha thrives in its academic achievement and our annual Strong Women, Strong Minds Scholarship giveaway/banquet is our biggest and most recognized event all year. It is a way for us as women, who often times do not come into the University with all the necessary resources or financial capabilities to reach our fullest academic potential, be able to unite as an organization and give back to young ladies who are continuing their academic career into the University in order to ease their financial burden a bit, and ultimately empower the Universal Woman inside them.', 'lta.gz.president@gmail.com', 'http://lta.orgsync.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/lta_gammazeta/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/lambdaladies'),
(70829, 'Latinic Societas Unitas (LSU)', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Mondays at 8:00 pm', 'Weekly', 'Latinic Societas Unitas is a multicultural community service-based sorority at UCR. We are a small but fun-loving organization always willing to support and uplift its women!
We carry encourage and stress a unity through sisterhood. We emphasize the importance of education and acknowledge its distinct necessity. We stress and practice the need for diversity. We provide moral and academic support. We engage in our community through service. We are proud to be LSU!', 'We carry, encourage and stress a unity through sisterhood. We emphasize the importance of education and acknowledge its distinct necessity. We stress and practice the need for diversity. We provide moral and academic support.', 'Latinic Societas Unitas is a multicultural community service-based sorority at UCR. We are a small but fun-loving organization always willing to support and uplift its women!
We carry encourage and stress a unity through sisterhood. We emphasize the importance of education and acknowledge its distinct necessity. We stress and practice the need for diversity. We provide moral and academic support. We engage in our community through service. We are proud to be LSU!', 'latinicsocietasunitas92@gmail.com', 'http://lsu1992.webs.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/lsv.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/lsu'),
(71164, 'Latino Business Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Fall/Winter/Spring Quarter: Wednesday’s 7-8:30pm', 'Weekly', null, 'The Latino Business Student Association (LBSA) is an organization designed to promote professional careers to students via the incorporation of informative seminars, conferences, and speakers.', 'LBSA participates in activities that enrich members with knowledge and experience that leads them to successfully launch their careers, and ultimately become future leaders and professionals -- open to all majors and backgrounds.
Working directly with The United Latino Student Association (ULSA) also allows LBSA members to actively participate in the development of professional, social, and entrepreneurial skills, all while creating a network of opportunities for both undergraduate and graduate students to effectively communicate between CSUs, UCs, and private universities.
Our drive to pursue higher achievements as an organization lies in our values for professionalism, mentorship, knowledge, networking, and community.
For more information & org updates follow us on Instagram @lbsariverside or email us at executivead.lbsa.ucr@gmail.com -- thank you!', 'president.lbsa.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://discord.gg/pw7xNudd', 'https://www.instagram.com/lbsariverside/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/lbsa'),
(84885, 'Latino Medical Student Association +', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Days & times are picked based on student availability every quarter.', '3x per quarter', null, 'Created to support all pre-health students at UC Riverside.', 'The Latino Medical Student Association Plus (LMSA+) at UCR aims to support all pre-health students through professional and academic development experiences.
Our chapter offers various events, workshops, conferences, and more each quarter to ensure pre-health students are best prepared for their journey post-undergraduate school.
To be an active member, apply at the start of fall quarter! Active members get to know first of all the opportunities that become available and more!
Our chapter is the home of 2 mentorship programs: The Undergraduate Mentorship Program (UMP) & the Medical School Mentorship Program (MSMP). Applications open once a year in the Fall.
To learn more about our chapter, visit our website or stay up to date with our socials!', 'lmsaucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.lmsaucr.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/lmsaucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrlmsa'),
(70874, 'Latino Union', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 8PM', 'Weekly', 'Another big part of Latino Union is that we are first-generation and transfer student-friendly; we provide many on-campus resources for our members. We also provide resources that include scholarships, internships, career readiness workshops, and bring awareness to our members about campus resources. Our organization does offer a scholarship to our members called the “Latino Union Scholarship,” which is awarded to a member at our End of the Year Banquet. Our overall goal is to be a bridge to our members’ success while fostering a supportive and connected community.
Meetings are held weekly on Wednesday nights @8pm in Chung Hall 143. Contact us and join in on the fun!', 'Latino Union''s purpose is to unite Latinos at UC-Riverside through community service, and to embrace our cultures in unity. We promote higher education, and strive to build long lasting friendships through doing good in our community! Meetings Wed. @ 8pm', 'Latino Union is a student organization with a principal focus on community service, promoting higher education, and community building. Our community service ranges from, but is not limited to, local street clean-ups, food drives, and care packages to the local community. We also collaborate with different student organizations to do community service. Our organization offers members a variety of opportunities to participate in local community service events.
Latino Union is also a social organization. We hold activities for members throughout the year, which consist of events such as potlucks, bowling nights, movie nights, and the list goes on! We also have socials with other organizations on campus to get to know other organizations on campus and to make meaningful connections. As an organization, we encourage support toward other organizations'' fundraisers and activities.
Academics are crucial to the mission of Latino Union, as we believe in the advancement of our members through higher education! If a member is struggling, we have support through Library Hours and guidance. We also host guest speakers from the local community to educate our members on different career paths. We want all members to be at their best when it comes to their academic coursework!
Another big part of Latino Union is that we are first-generation and transfer student-friendly; we provide many on-campus resources for our members. We also provide resources that include scholarships, internships, career readiness workshops, and bring awareness to our members about campus resources. Our organization does offer a scholarship to our members called the “Latino Union Scholarship,” which is awarded to a member at our End of the Year Banquet. Our overall goal is to be a bridge to our members’ success while fostering a supportive and connected community.
Meetings are held weekly on Wednesday nights @8pm in Chung Hall 143. Contact us and join in on the fun!', 'latinounion588@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/latinounion/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/latinounion'),
(321855, 'Lawtinx Pre-Law Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Monday at 5:00 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'Lawtinx serves the large population of pre-law and Latinx students at UCR. Offering guidance and experience to students pursuing a career in the legal field. While the emphasis is on the Latinx community, everyone is welcomed.', 'Come join us at Lawtinx!
The Lawtinx Pre-Law Club was founded on the basis of offering representation and resources to the Hispanic/Latinx/Chicanx community at UC Riverside.
Despite making up 18% of the United States population, Latinxs makes up 4% of the legal field; our goal is to change that. We offer representation, guidance, and community to those interested in pursuing a career in the legal field by hosting speakers and offering LSAT resources amongst other cultural and professional development events. While the emphasis is on the Latinx community, all pre-law students are welcomed!
If interested feel free to contact us or visit our social media!
Instagram: @ucrlawtinx', 'ucrlawtinx@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrlawtinx/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/lawtinx'),
(71120, 'Lebanese Student Association at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'This organization usually meets anytime after 5 pm. The day is decided by the club as a whole.', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Lebanese Student Association at UCR represents individuals that come together to participate in social activities, academic workshops, & more. LSA provides opportunities to teach & enrich our community with the culture of Lebanon and the Middle East.', 'The Lebanese Student Association (LSA) at UCR is a non-religious, non-political, non-profit organization that represents a group of individuals that come together to participate in social activities, academic workshops, conventions, and more. LSA provides opportunities to teach & enrich our community with the diverse culture of Lebanon and the Middle East. While learning and connecting with one another, this club expands people''s knowledge on what Lebanese traditions and customs provide. LSA aspires toward community integration and seeks to promote an understanding of this region in the Middle East.
https://youtu.be/SokG6aVXzR0', 'lscucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_lsa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/lsa'),
(385687, 'Legal Minds Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays 5-7pm', 'Weekly', null, 'A group of UCR students whose goal is to expand the pre-law culture on campus. We aim to create a platform for pre-law students to connect and grow. We understand the challenges and opportunities in the field, and we want to make it easier for you', 'We''re a group of UCR students who want to expand the pre-law culture on campus. Our goal is to create a platform for pre-law students to connect and grow. We understand the challenges and opportunities in the field, and we want to make it easier for everyone to access the resources and support they need to succeed. By bringing together like-minded individuals, we can create a strong community that maximizes our resources and helps us all reach our full potential. Join us in building a powerful network of pre-law students at UCR!', 'ucrlegalminds@gmail.com', 'https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScNlxifFSA5Uuwd4wERh7OZC5zSj6i1P_Ol9sz_ciLGYtFZrQ/viewform?usp=sf_link', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrlms/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/lms'),
(424599, 'Legally Queer', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesdays 5pm-6pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Legally Queer is a space for queer students &amp; allies at UCR who have an interest in law or in studying queer law and history. We host a variety of events including academic, social, and mock trials for students to learn about their legal journey.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be a club specifically designed and catering to queer students at UC Riverside who have an interest in law or in studying queer law and history. We host a variety of events including academic, social, and mock trials to further enhance the experience of our queer pre-law community at UCR. We also connect queer pre-law students to advising resources through guest speaker events and campus partner relationships.', 'legallyqueerucr@gmail.com', 'https://discord.gg/7qHmgFKpsk', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/legally-queer'),
(386041, 'LEO''s Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Wednesdays @ 6:30PM', 'Monthly', null, 'The purposes of this organization shall be representing qualities of leadership, excellence, and opportunity while serving the Riverside community, alongside our student body.', 'Pre-health volunteering organization', 'leosclubatucr@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/leosclubatucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrleosclub?igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/leosclubatucr'),
(71097, 'Life', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Sundays at 10am, Mondays at 7:30pm, Wednesdays at 7:30PM and Fridays at 7:30PM', '4 times per week', 'Our mission is to show students that the Bible can be applied to everyday life and to challenge students to look further into the Bible as a wellspring of knowledge. There are several meetings during the week where students are invited to participate in Bible discussions (regardless of their religious affiliation). Personal bible studies are centered on individual schedules and are flexible for different time and location arrangements. The club centers around the Bible and active fellowship with one another to build friendships!', 'The purpose of Life is to provide students with a small group setting that is a safe place to discuss relevant topics from the Bible in an informal setting for people of all kinds of backgrounds whether Christian or not.', 'Our mission is to show students that the Bible can be applied to everyday life and to challenge students to look further into the Bible as a wellspring of knowledge. There are several meetings during the week where students are invited to participate in Bible discussions (regardless of their religious affiliation). Personal bible studies are centered on individual schedules and are flexible for different time and location arrangements. The club centers around the Bible and active fellowship with one another to build friendships!', 'William: wbruc002@ucr.edu, Yudelkis: ygonz082@ucr.edu', 'https://restoredchurchworldwide.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/lifeoncampus.ucr?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/life'),
(414591, 'Live Action at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 7:00 pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Our organization exists to unite and equip students to defend the dignity of every human life. Through education, respectful dialogue, and community outreach, we work to confront the reality of abortion, and support local families in need.', 'The purpose of this organization is to connect, educate, and empower students to stand together in defense of human life. As a unified body, we seek to raise awareness about the injustice of abortion and respond through informed dialogue, compassionate outreach, and active engagement. Our members are equipped to engage respectfully with those of differing views and to support local families in need—offering tangible help and hope in order to save lives.', 'choose.life.coalition@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/live.action.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/coalition-for-life'),
(351024, 'Loving our Emotions as Asians & Pacific Islanders', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'We encourage conversation within the Asian & Pacific Islander community of UCR. We aim to create a safe space to share, process, and acknowledge our emotions in order to normalize all aspects of working towards a healthy state of mind.', 'We are an organization at UCR that promotes mental health awareness in the Asian & Pacific Islander community by doing stress relief activities and talk circles. Through creating a safe space to share, process, and acknowledge our emotions, we aim to encourage conversations and normalize aspects of working towards a healthy state of mind.
Click here to go to our website, which has more information and upcoming events! Click here for our linktree, which has all of our socials and member applications!', 'lovingouremotions@gmail.com', 'https://leap.ucrhighlanders.org/', 'http://www.instagram.com/ucrleap', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/leap'),
(405773, 'MAES Student Chapter at UC Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Biweekly on thursday at 7pm', 'Every two weeks', 'This organization intends to cultivate and advance representation of Latinos in STEM. By hosting workshops, events, and meetings we will build a community that encourages and aids Latino leadership in STEM. We aim to help guide you in your academic and professional STEM careers by offering scholarships and internships through mymaes.org. We also plan on building a fun and welcoming social experience within stem majors!', 'The purpose of this social and academic organization shall be to promote, cultivate, and advance representation of Latino leadership and education in STEM.', 'This organization intends to cultivate and advance representation of Latinos in STEM. By hosting workshops, events, and meetings we will build a community that encourages and aids Latino leadership in STEM. We aim to help guide you in your academic and professional STEM careers by offering scholarships and internships through mymaes.org. We also plan on building a fun and welcoming social experience within stem majors!', 'ucrmaes@gmail.com', 'https://mymaes.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/maes.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/maesucr'),
(425418, 'Master of Public Health Scholars', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], null, null, null, 'This organization shall be to act as an entity that collectively represents the Master of Public Health cohorts.', 'Our mission is to serve and protect vulnerable populations with empathy, inclusiveness, and cultural sensitivity by being open to innovation, flexibility, and transparency. This includes focusing on systemic change through advocacy, infrastructure, and social justice in underserved communities. In doing so, this organization aims to provide resources, opportunities, and support to its students to achieve academic excellence and career development.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mphs'),
(420325, 'Matcha Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], '2nd Thursday of the month at 6pm', 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to create a welcoming space for students to de-stress, study, and connect with others over a shared love of matcha. The club aims to educate members about the origins and cultural significance of matcha, explore', 'Matcha Club is a student-centered organization dedicated to creating a welcoming and relaxing environment where students can de-stress, study, and build meaningful connections through a shared appreciation for matcha and Japanese tea culture. The club strives to educate members on the history, cultural significance, preparation methods, and health benefits of matcha while fostering community through social gatherings, study sessions, tasting events, workshops, and cultural activities. By combining wellness, education, and community engagement, Matcha Club aims to provide students with a supportive space that encourages cultural appreciation, friendship, and personal well being.', 'ucrmatchaclub@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/ucr.matcha.club', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrmatchaclub/?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/-'),
(81969, 'Materials Research Society at UC Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'TBD for Fall 2026', 'Every two weeks', 'Materials Research Society Chapter at UCR promotes the advancement of materials research through interdisciplinary collaboration among all majors. Our goal is to help connect students to faculty and other engineering students in order to find possible research positions and networking opportunities. We also focus on professional development workshops which feature graduate students throughout the year to sharpen our members’ skills for the engineering world. With our biweekly socials, workshops and plentiful opportunities, MRS hopes to provide the tools needed for success in the future.
If you are interested in joining our organization, please fill the Sign Up Form for updates: https://forms.gle/FtDxRdeZH6uegkbF7', 'Materials Research Society Chapter at UCR emphasizes commitment to the advancement of materials research to improve the quality of life.', 'Materials Research Society Chapter at UCR promotes the advancement of materials research through interdisciplinary collaboration among all majors. Our goal is to help connect students to faculty and other engineering students in order to find possible research positions and networking opportunities. We also focus on professional development workshops which feature graduate students throughout the year to sharpen our members’ skills for the engineering world. With our biweekly socials, workshops and plentiful opportunities, MRS hopes to provide the tools needed for success in the future.
If you are interested in joining our organization, please fill the Sign Up Form for updates: https://forms.gle/FtDxRdeZH6uegkbF7', 'ucr.mrs@gmail.com', 'https://mrsucr.carrd.co/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr.mrs/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mrsucr'),
(414864, 'Materials Science and Mechanical Engineering Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Tuesdays at noon', null, null, 'The MSMEGSA supports graduate students in Materials Science and Mechanical Engineering through professional development, networking, and social events, fostering a strong, collaborative community and advocating for student interests within the department', 'The Materials Science and Mechanical Engineering Graduate Student Association (MSME GSA) is a student-led organization dedicated to fostering a strong academic, professional, and social community among graduate students within the fields of Materials Science and Mechanical Engineering. Our mission is to support the personal and professional development of our members through a variety of initiatives, including research symposia, career development workshops, networking events, and social gatherings.
MSME GSA serves as a platform for graduate students to connect with peers, faculty, alumni, and industry professionals, while also acting as a collective voice to advocate for student interests within the department and the broader university community. By promoting interdisciplinary collaboration, leadership opportunities, and community engagement, MSME GSA strives to enrich the graduate experience and empower students to succeed in their academic and professional pursuits.', 'MSMEGSA@email.ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/msmegsa?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/msme-gsa'),
(420034, 'Math Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'The goal of the club is to give undergraduates a community with others who enjoy math and to participate in mathematical discussion in an environment that is more relaxed than other mathematical settings.', null, null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mathclub'),
(123318, 'Math Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Visit the MathGSA website, or email one of the officers to see if a meeting is currently being planned', 'Monthly', 'The MathGSA represents the interests of the mathematics graduate students at UCR. We want to provide a forum to discuss ways that we can work together to improve the department, and we also aim to create a sense of community among the math graduate students. Meetings are usually held monthly, first Friday @ 2pm in Skye Hall 284.
For organization details, proceedings, and a list of helpful links for math graduate students, visit https://mathgsa.github.io/. Feel free to reach out by email.', 'Graduate Student Association for the Department of Mathematics', 'The MathGSA represents the interests of the mathematics graduate students at UCR. We want to provide a forum to discuss ways that we can work together to improve the department, and we also aim to create a sense of community among the math graduate students. Meetings are usually held monthly, first Friday @ 2pm in Skye Hall 284.
For organization details, proceedings, and a list of helpful links for math graduate students, visit https://mathgsa.github.io/. Feel free to reach out by email.', 'mfred010@ucr.edu', 'https://ucrmath.github.io/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mathgsa'),
(414359, 'Med X Clinical Research Initiative at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'UCR Med X empowers undergraduates to bring their clinical research ideas to life by providing resources, mentorship, and hands-on instruction in research design, ethics, and implementation.', 'Students in UCR Med X will collaborate in research teams to explore clinically relevant topics of their choice. The organization provides guidance, instruction, and resources to support every step of their research journey, from idea to execution.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrmedx'),
(180887, 'Medical Emergency Education Project', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Wednesday 8pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Medical Emergency Education Project provides the Inland Empire community the knowledge and skills to be utilized in medical emergencies by offering Basic Life Support and First Aid classes and the opportunity for UCR students to become an instructor!', 'The Medical Emergency Education Project strives to help alleviate health issues by equipping UC Riverside students, faculty, and staff, as well as the Inland Empire community, with the necessary resources for medical emergencies. We offer Basic Life Support and First Aid certification classes in an effort to increase the awareness and knowledge of emergency skills and techniques that could help save a life. Our organization grants the leadership opportunity to become an instructor to continue spreading the knowledge of Basic Life Support and First Aid. This not only helps students pursue potential routes to emergency medicine or emergency medical services but also help them apply the knowledge to serve underserved communities within the Inland Empire and wherever their future may take them!
Follow us on Instagram @ucrmeep for updates!', 'ucrmeep@gmail.com', 'https://www.ucrmeep.com/home', 'http://www.instagram.com/ucrmeep/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrmeep'),
(405662, 'Medics in Armenia at UC Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Medics in Armenia is an organization dedicated to educating and providing valuable experiences for incoming medical professionals. Students participate in shadowing opportunities, volunteer work, and local services applicable to the medical field.', null, null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/mia_ucr?igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/medicsinarmenia_ucr'),
(401287, 'Melody Maker at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'We will provide instruments, such as ocarina and ukulele, and learn how to play it as a club. Our goal is to create a community that focuses on sharing and embracing music for anyone who is looking for a place to both practice and have fun at UCR.', 'As students, we understand how school can be stressful, but we also recognize the healing and stress-relieving power of music. Our goal is to offer an avenue for students to embrace music as a way to unwind and connect. Through learning and playing together, students will not only develop musical skills but also create lasting memories and build a supportive community.', 'schin065@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/melodymakeratucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/melodymakeratucr'),
(70840, 'Men''s Club Soccer at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'M & W : 6:45-9:00pm', 'Weekly', null, 'This club is for students still looking to play intercollegiate soccer without having to be consumed by the competitive soccer lifestyle that is D1.', 'To provide a competitive soccer team to students and college athletes, and to develop talented soccer players, skills, and abilities. We compete in the SoCal Premier Division where we play against other schools across Southern California.
Follow our Instagram to keep up with IMPORTANT DATES & TRYOUTS!', 'bhom009@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrmensclubsoccer/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/msc'),
(71090, 'Men''s Club Volleyball at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesdays @ 8:30-10:30pm & Sundays @ 4-6pm', '2-3 times a week', 'In recent years, the volleyball community at UCR has grown. This club is designed to provide a competitive environment for students in the sport of Volleyball. The club provides a space to meet people with the common interest of volleyball, provide opportunity for community service, compete against other club teams, enjoy recreational volleyball, teach comradery, and more.
Please follow our Instagram for more info about tryouts, tournaments, and open gyms: @ucrmensclubvb', 'Men''s Volleyball Club at UCR is designed to provide a competitive volleyball environment for students. 

Follow our Instagram for more info about tryouts, tournaments, and open gyms: @ucrmensclubvb', 'In recent years, the volleyball community at UCR has grown. This club is designed to provide a competitive environment for students in the sport of Volleyball. The club provides a space to meet people with the common interest of volleyball, provide opportunity for community service, compete against other club teams, enjoy recreational volleyball, teach comradery, and more.
Please follow our Instagram for more info about tryouts, tournaments, and open gyms: @ucrmensclubvb', 'ucrmensvb@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrmensclubvb/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mensvolleyball'),
(118262, 'Men''s Club Water Polo at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Monday and Wednesday (8:00-10:00pm)', 'Weekly', 'We practice every Monday and Wednesday (8:00-10 PM) @ the UCR Student Recreation Center Lap Pool.
To join, show up at the pool and fill out DoSportsEasy. Everyone is welcome, no prior experience required.
To reach out via instagram dm our account @ucrwaterpolo
Tournaments guaranteed every quarter, scrimmage to learn, focus on fundamentals and bring a smile!', 'Compete and practice water polo at UCR !

Active on Instagram @ucrwaterpolo
DM us!', 'We practice every Monday and Wednesday (8:00-10 PM) @ the UCR Student Recreation Center Lap Pool.
To join, show up at the pool and fill out DoSportsEasy. Everyone is welcome, no prior experience required.
To reach out via instagram dm our account @ucrwaterpolo
Tournaments guaranteed every quarter, scrimmage to learn, focus on fundamentals and bring a smile!', 'echav115@ucr.edu', 'https://ucr.dserec.com/online/clubsports/club/9/registration', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrwaterpolo', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mcwp'),
(71055, 'Microbiology Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'One 2 hour meeting during the second week of every month between 5-7pm', 'Monthly', null, 'MicroGSA is dedicated to fostering a collaborative and supportive community for current and future graduate students within the Microbiology Graduate Program.', 'The Microbiology Graduate Student Association (Microbiology GSA) is dedicated to fostering a collaborative and supportive community for current and future graduate students within the Microbiology Graduate Program. Our mission is to cultivate an inclusive and supportive environment to enhance both academic and professional growth.
The Microbiology GSA serves as a representative body, providing a voice for microbiology graduate students within the department and broader university community. We are committed to advocating for student needs, and organizing events that enrich the graduate experience including workshops, outreach events, and socials.', 'ucrmicrogsa@gmail.com', 'https://microbiology.ucr.edu/microbiology-graduate-student-association-mini-gsa', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_mcbl?igsh=OGQ5ZDc2ODk2ZA%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/microgsa'),
(425199, 'Military Medical Community', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'MMC connects students interested in military medicine with recruiters, HPSP students, and other medical personnel of their interest through mentorship, networking, and national events.', null, 'ucrmmc@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrmmc/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/militarymedicalcommunity'),
(400156, 'Mindbody at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The primary purpose of Mindbody is to promote awareness of mental and physical health strategies, such as the effects of sleep, nutrition, and exercise.', 'Our mission is to research, share, and apply evidence-based strategies to enhance physical and mental well-being.
Journal Club – We analyze research articles, discuss key findings, and explore real-world applications. Each session, we present 1–2 articles from psychology, biology, or medicine (or any article related to physical or mental health). We also help students get involved in research labs.
Socials – We host fun activities like board game night, giving members a chance to connect and unwind.
Education Committee – Every other week, we create a slideshow for our Instagram page on a condition or disease related to sports or nutrition. We also plan to visit high schools in the Riverside Unified School District (RUSD) to present current research.', 'marcus.yan@email.ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mindbody'),
(224494, 'Minority Association of Pre-Medical Students', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'MAPS members are considered National Associate members and make up about one third of SNMA''s membership. This initiative of the Student National Medical Association (SNMA) represents future underrepresented medical students.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to provide underrepresented pre-medical students with knowledge, skills, and experience that are both prerequisite and concomitant to professional participation in health care fields. MAPS also serves to improve minority matriculation into all professional health related programs, with an emphasis on medicine.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/maps'),
(70897, 'Model United Nations (MUN) at UC Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'General Meetings: Tuesdays & Wednesdays 7:30-8:30pm starting Week 2', 'Weekly', null, 'To educate students regarding international relations and international politics as well as promote diplomatic cooperation, public speaking, and collective problem solving through emulating the procedures and function of the United Nations.', 'To educate students regarding international relations and international politics as well as promote diplomatic cooperation, public speaking, and collective problem solving through emulating the procedures and function of the United Nations.', 'ucr.mun@gmail.com', 'http://www.munucr.org/home', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrmun/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/munatucr'),
(405163, 'Moot Court Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays and Thursdays 6:30-7:30pm', 'Twice a week', null, 'The Moot Court Club simulates appellate court advocacy, helping students develop skills in legal analysis, oral argument, and critical thinking. We foster teamwork, leadership, and confidence through workshops, mock trials, and competitions.', 'The Moot Court Club is a student-led organization dedicated to fostering skills in legal analysis, oral advocacy, and critical thinking through the simulation of appellate court proceedings. Our members engage in thought-provoking debates, analyze real-world legal issues, and compete in local and national Moot Court competitions.
Through workshops, mock trials, and mentoring, we create a supportive environment where students can develop essential skills for law school, careers in law, and beyond. Open to students of all backgrounds, the club aims to empower members to advocate confidently, think critically, and lead effectively.', 'eraul002@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mootcourt'),
(70983, 'Movimiento Estudiantil Chicanx de Aztlan (MECHA)', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 6:30PM', 'Weekly', 'Please visit our instagram @MECHADEUCR for the latest.
We meet on Tuesdays from 6:30 pm - 7:30 pm. Location announced on our Instagram.', 'MECHA is a student organization that promotes higher education, culture, and history. MECHA was founded on the principles of self-determination and education for the liberation of our people. To get involved visit our Instagram: @mechadeucr', 'MEChA is a student organization that promotes higher education, cultura, and historia. MEChA was founded on the principles of self-determination and liberation for Chicanx commuity and has evolved to promote healing, education, and unity for all Latinxs. We believe that political involvement and education is the avenue for change in our society. MEChA is grounded in a philosophy, not a nationality. It is a movement, working with all those who acknowledge and work towards the betterment of our communities, regardless of ethnicity.
Please visit our instagram @MECHADEUCR for the latest.
We meet on Tuesdays from 6:30 pm - 7:30 pm. Location announced on our Instagram.', 'mechadeucr2019@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/mechadeucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mechadeucr'),
(71000, 'Mu Sigma Rho at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Honors']::text[], 'Depends on quarter schedule - usually afternoons', 'Once a year.', null, 'The local chapter of Mu Sigma Rho at UCR. Mu Sigma Rho is the National Statistics Honorary Society. Our purpose is the promotion and encouragement of scholarly activity in statistics, and the recognition of outstanding achievement among our students.', 'Mu Sigma Rho is a nonsecret organization whose purpose is the promotion and encouragement of scholarly activity in statistics and the recognition of worth-while achievement among the staff and students in eligible academic and nonacademic institutions. It aims to do this by:1. electing members according to their academic achievement, especially in the field of statistics;2. engaging in activities designed to promote the statistical and general scholarly development of its members;3. encouraging participation in the various professional statistical societies and associations.', 'msr.ucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/msr'),
(350894, 'Mujeres Activas en Letras y Cambio Social', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Join us via Highlander Link to receive meeting information', 'Monthly', null, 'Creating a safe space for womxn to speak out on issues affecting them on campus and within the communities, navigate academia and prepare for graduate school, and represent UCR at the annual national MALCS Summer Institute (held during the Summer).', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to create a comfortable space where women can empower each other, speak on the issues affecting women on campus, coordinate with on-campus centers such as the Chicano Student Program (CSP) and the Women’s Resource Center (WRC), engage with our communities through workshops and outreach, help Active Members prepare and navigate academia, and represent UC Riverside at the annual national MALCS’ Summer Institute.', 'UCRMALCS@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/malcs'),
(71044, 'Music Changing Lives at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Music Changing Lives at UCR was established to spread joy through arts, academics, music, and volunteering in the community.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization is to spread joy by volunteering and bringing music, arts and education to those in the community. The outcomes of this organization are the hopes of reduced crime rate, reduced drop-out rates, increased family and community engagement, and increased participation in higher education. The members of this program shall use their acquired knowledge to enrich the lives of children.
Find more information about the non-profit organization at https://www.musicchanginglives.org/
Our Instagram is at https://www.instagram.com/musicchanginglives/?hl=en and Discord at https://discord.com/invite/nRSJCwJxed
You can also find our Facebook group at https://www.facebook.com/MusicChangingLivesIE/', 'musicchanginglivesucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.musicchanginglives.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/mcl_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mclatucr'),
(344514, 'Music Enthusiasts Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Wednesdays 8pm to 10pm at Watkins 1111', 'Weekly', 'Join the discord!
We meet every Wednesday at Watkins 1111 from 8PM to 10PM', 'The Music Enthusiasts Society is a club for appreciating and sharing of alternative music and its many underground genres.', 'The Music Enthusiast Society is a place for all music lovers, creators, and collectors to share their interest and appreciation for music and its many genres.
Whether you''re looking to find new music or make friends with similar taste, Music Enthusiast society is the place for you.
Join the discord!
We meet every Wednesday at Watkins 1111 from 8PM to 10PM', 'musicenthusiastsucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://instagram.com/mes.ucr?igshid=YmMyMTA2M2Y=', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/musicethusiastsociety'),
(71115, 'Music Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Wednesdays @ 2pm', 'Quarterly', null, 'The purposes of this organization shall be: a) to serve as a medium of communication between members of the MGSA, the GSA, and the Music Department; b) to promote and coordinate the interests of the members of the MGSA; c) to facilitate valuable intellect', 'The purposes of this organization shall be: a) to serve as a medium of communication between members of the MGSA, the GSA, and the Music Department; b) to promote and coordinate the interests of the members of the MGSA; c) to facilitate valuable intellectual exchange.', 'ucrmgsa@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/musicgrads'),
(420124, 'Music Undergraduate Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesday at 1pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be for potential and enrolled Music undergraduate students interested in pursuing a career in Music and beyond to network and support each other''s goals and interests. We’ll strive on being the bridge for career', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be for potential and enrolled Music undergraduate students interested in pursuing a career in Music and beyond to network and support each other''s goals and interests. We’ll strive on being the bridge for career readiness incorporating all our Music Undergraduate scholars pursuing the depths of Music Industry, Music Education and more. Our purpose is to also advocate for all Music Undergraduates by making this organization a safe place where they can bring their concerns and have a voice in their education.', 'gvasq042@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/musa'),
(70871, 'Muslim Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 5pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Muslim Student Association at UC Riverside', 'Asalamu Alaikum, Peace and Blessings upon all of those who read this message. Muslim Student Association (MSA) is a religious organization devoted to strengthening the Muslim community through service and activism, educating both Muslims and people of other faiths about the religion of Islam, and facilitating a better environment for Muslim students on campus. MSA aims to serve Muslim students during their university careers by creating a strong, diverse network of students who are conscious of their Islamic identity and committed to serving Islam.', 'msa.riverside@gmail.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/msaucr/', 'https://www.instagram.com/msaucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/msa'),
(404505, 'Muslim Tech Collaborative', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Thursdays 5-6pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'MTC UCR is dedicated to creating a space for Muslims in tech to come together as a professional and spiritual community, showcasing Islamic excellence by leveraging our talents and creating positive tangible impacts on the world.', null, null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/mtc'),
(402632, 'National Arab American Medical Association NextGen Chapter at University of California, Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'Our chapter also emphasizes the importance of understanding diverse backgrounds in healthcare and encourages all students to consider how social, cultural, and historical factors shape patient care and community health outcomes. Through our events and workshops, we aim to cultivate cultural competence and empathy in healthcare, recognizing the vital role these skills play in effectively serving a diverse population.
NAAMA NextGen at UCR is more than just a student organization; it is a network of future healthcare leaders committed to excellence, inclusivity, and the advancement of health and well-being for all communities. By bringing together students and seasoned healthcare professionals in a supportive environment, we are laying the groundwork for a new generation of healthcare providers who are prepared to meet the challenges of tomorrow with compassion, knowledge, and an unwavering commitment to making a positive impact in their communities.', 'NAAMA NextGen at UCR empowers students from all backgrounds pursuing healthcare careers. Through mentorship, networking, and events with renowned Arab American professionals, we foster leadership, inclusivity, and a commitment to advancing health for all', 'The NAAMA NextGen chapter at UCR is dedicated to empowering students of all backgrounds who are passionate about pursuing careers in healthcare. Our chapter’s mission centers on fostering a supportive and inclusive community where students can access vital resources that promote healthcare advocacy, professional growth, and meaningful community service. Through a combination of mentorship programs, networking events, skill-building workshops, and leadership opportunities, we provide our members with the essential tools they need for career development and a smooth transition into the healthcare field.
One of the distinctive aspects of NAAMA NextGen at UCR is our focus on connecting students with renowned Arab American healthcare professionals from across various specialties. These accomplished professionals, who have made significant contributions to healthcare, bring a wealth of knowledge, experience, and inspiration to our community. We invite these leaders to campus for exclusive guest lectures, panel discussions, and interactive networking events where students can gain valuable insights, ask questions, and engage in meaningful conversations. This direct access to industry leaders offers students the chance to learn not only about the challenges and successes these professionals have encountered but also about the unique perspectives and resilience they bring to their work.
Our chapter also emphasizes the importance of understanding diverse backgrounds in healthcare and encourages all students to consider how social, cultural, and historical factors shape patient care and community health outcomes. Through our events and workshops, we aim to cultivate cultural competence and empathy in healthcare, recognizing the vital role these skills play in effectively serving a diverse population.
NAAMA NextGen at UCR is more than just a student organization; it is a network of future healthcare leaders committed to excellence, inclusivity, and the advancement of health and well-being for all communities. By bringing together students and seasoned healthcare professionals in a supportive environment, we are laying the groundwork for a new generation of healthcare providers who are prepared to meet the challenges of tomorrow with compassion, knowledge, and an unwavering commitment to making a positive impact in their communities.', 'naamaucr@gmail.com', 'https://naama.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/naamaucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/naamanextgenatucr'),
(120334, 'National Black Law Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesday 6:30 - 9:00 pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Established to unite students with their peers who have a similar interest in the legal field, to provide students a better understanding of careers within the legal field, and to give opportunities for mentorship with current practitioners in law.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to provide community support for students who desire to obtain a deeper understanding of the legal field through various services such as mentorship opportunities with a local bar association, the opportunity to shadow practitioners of the law who encourage academic excellence, as well as to provide the essential tools needed to assist students in their advancements into the professional community. This club is not limited to those that are in pursuit of a J.D., but for everyone intrested in law and related fields.', 'ucrnblsa@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/nblsa_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/nblsa'),
(70915, 'National Pan-Hellenic Council (NPHC)', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Thursdays at 8PM', 'Every two weeks', 'In alignment with its mission, the National Pan-Hellenic Council (NPHC) at UCR is dedicated to advancing the well-being of its affiliated fraternities and sororities through leadership and professional development opportunities for its members.
To further its mission, the NPHC at UCR has identified the following objectives which are: serving as a communication conduit between constituent fraternities and sororities, facilitating the coordination of workshops and national meetings, conducting regular workshops and training sessions, collaborating with various community groups and organizations, promote unity and economic empowerment among member organizations, and fulfill additional coordinating functions as outlined in the NPHC Constitution and Bylaws or directed by the NPHC Executive Board.', 'In alignment with its mission, the National Pan-Hellenic Council (NPHC) at UCR is dedicated to advancing the well-being of its affiliated fraternities and sororities through leadership and professional development opportunities for its members.', 'In alignment with its mission, the National Pan-Hellenic Council (NPHC) at UCR is dedicated to advancing the well-being of its affiliated fraternities and sororities through leadership and professional development opportunities for its members.
To further its mission, the NPHC at UCR has identified the following objectives which are: serving as a communication conduit between constituent fraternities and sororities, facilitating the coordination of workshops and national meetings, conducting regular workshops and training sessions, collaborating with various community groups and organizations, promote unity and economic empowerment among member organizations, and fulfill additional coordinating functions as outlined in the NPHC Constitution and Bylaws or directed by the NPHC Executive Board.', 'ucrnphc@gmail.com', 'https://www.nphchq.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_nphc/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrnphc'),
(71066, 'National Residence Hall Honorary', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], 'Monday 8-9PM At the Dundee MPR', 'Weekly', null, 'To aid the development and maintenance of a strong, diverse and academically successful residential community within the UCR Residence Halls.', 'Our mission as the National Residence Hall Honorary at the University of California, Riverside is to aid the development and maintenance of a strong, diverse and academically successful residential community within the UCR Residence Halls. We believe that in order to accomplish this we must do the following:
Maximize opportunities for residents to become leaders and explore their unique leadership styles.
Create and support initiatives that focus on diversity awareness, tolerance and celebration.
Develop effective educational and social programs.
Encourage academic excellence through role modeling and the development of academic initiatives.
Recognize resident leaders for their service to the residence hall community.
Find and direct residents to appropriate resources and leadership opportunities in Housing Services, on campus and in the surrounding community.
Find and direct residents to appropriate resources and leadership opportunities in Housing Services, on campus and in the surrounding community.
Be a channel through which recognition of the Residence Halls is known on a local, regional and national level.', 'ucr.nrhh@gmail.com', 'http://ucrnrhh.wordpress.com', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/nrhh'),
(70926, 'National Society of Black Engineers', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'One dedicated mentor, matched to your major and goals
Bi-weekly programs with the full cohort
Academic guidance, resume reviews, and interview prep
Access to NSBE events, industry tours, and alumni networks
A real community of people who get it
K-12 Outreach: We partner with the Society of Women Engineers, 100 Black Men of the Inland Empire, and local schools to give K-12 students hands-on STEM exposure.
General Meetings: Held every two weeks. A mix of professional development, community, and chapter business.
MEMBERSHIP
Membership is open to all UCR students. No experience, background, or specific major required, just a willingness to grow and contribute to the community.
General NSBE membership: ucrnsbe@ucr.edu
Instagram: @nsbe_ucr
Meeting Frequency: Every two weeks
Location: UC Riverside, Bourns College of Engineering', 'UCR''s chapter of the National Society of Black Engineers, BCOE''s most awarded student org. Our mission: increasing the number of culturally responsible Black engineers who excel academically, succeed professionally, and positively impact the community.', 'ABOUT US
The National Society of Black Engineers at UC Riverside exists for one reason: to make sure Black engineers at UCR have every resource, connection, and opportunity they need to thrive, not just survive.
We''re 100+ members strong, hold an average chapter GPA of 3.0, and we''re the first student organization at UCR to establish an endowment fund. Last year in 2025-2026 alone, our members toured Google, Google, NASA JPL, the DIII-D National Fusion Facility, and the IEUA Water Reclamation Plant. We''ve had engineers from Meta, Boeing, and Karma Automotive come speak directly to our chapter. Eight of our members attended national engineering conferences and came home with four internships secured on the spot.
We''re not just a club. We''re a launchpad.
Awards & Recognition:
Outstanding Student Organization of the Year, UCR Student Life
Best Organization of the Year, African Student Programs
Best Outstanding K-12 Outreach Award (2024-2025)
Social Justice Activist of the Year
First UCR student org to establish an endowment fund
PASSING THE TORCH: PEER MENTORSHIP PROGRAM
If you''re a Black first-year or transfer student coming into the Bourns College of Engineering, this program was built for you.
Passing the Torch pairs you 1-on-1 with an upperclassman mentor who''s already navigated what you''re about to face: the hard classes, the internship grind, the figuring-it-all-out phase. They''ve been there. now they''re here for you.
What mentees get:
One dedicated mentor, matched to your major and goals
Bi-weekly programs with the full cohort
Academic guidance, resume reviews, and interview prep
Access to NSBE events, industry tours, and alumni networks
A real community of people who get it
This program is completely free. Priority is given to incoming first-year and transfer engineering students, but any student wanting mentorship is welcome to apply.
Ready to join? Fill out the membership form here!
WHAT WE DO
Beyond Passing the Torch, NSBE UCR runs programs all year for all members:
Conferences: We send members to NSBE Nationals, the Fall Regional Conference, AfroTech, BEYA, and more. These aren''t just trips; they''re career accelerators with recruiting fairs and networking built in.
Industry Tours: Past tours include Google, NASA JPL, DIII-D National Fusion Facility, and the IEUA Water Reclamation Plant. Real access to real places.
Guest Speaker Panels: Engineers from Meta, Boeing, Karma Automotive, and others have come to speak directly with our chapter.
K-12 Outreach: We partner with the Society of Women Engineers, 100 Black Men of the Inland Empire, and local schools to give K-12 students hands-on STEM exposure.
General Meetings: Held every two weeks. A mix of professional development, community, and chapter business.
MEMBERSHIP
Membership is open to all UCR students. No experience, background, or specific major required, just a willingness to grow and contribute to the community.
General NSBE membership: ucrnsbe@ucr.edu
Passing the Torch mentorship sign-up: passingthetorch@ucr.edu
CONTACT & SOCIAL
Email: passingthetorch@ucr.edu (mentorship) | ucrnsbe@ucr.edu (general)
Instagram: @nsbe_ucr
Meeting Frequency: Every two weeks
Location: UC Riverside, Bourns College of Engineering', 'ucrnsbepres@gmail.com', 'http://www.engr.ucr.edu/~nsbe/', 'https://www.instagram.com/nsbe_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/nsbe'),
(71075, 'Native American Student Association (NASA)', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Meetings are held once a week on Monday at 6:00pm in the Native American Student Programs office, located at Costo Hall 229. We also have a zoom option available.', 'Weekly', null, 'Native American Student Association', 'Maintain a strong network with neighboring Native communities, increasing the number of Native students at UCR and providing a space for our Native students to promote cultural awareness of the various tribes to the campus.', 'aparr064@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/nasaucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/nasa'),
(187430, 'Natural History Museum Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Same day every week, usually in the afternoons, but changes each quarter', 'Weekly', null, 'The Natural History Museum Club is a local group in the Natural History Collections Care Network. Our goals are to expose students to museum studies and increase appreciation for natural history through volunteering, discussions, trips, and projects.', 'The Natural History Museum Club at UCR is a local branch of the Natural History Collections Care Network. Our activities include volunteering in collections on campus (such as the geology collection, entomology museum, and herbarium), museum science workshops, and tours and/or field trips to museums on and off-campus.
The purposes of the Natural History Museum Club at UCR organization shall be:
I. To provide multidisciplinary education, training, access, and opportunities for museum work to students which would otherwise be inaccessible or limited in scope
II. To interface with a nationwide network of like clubs on other university campuses
III. To facilitate interactions between undergraduates, graduates, staff, and faculty in fields utilizing natural history collections
IV. To further the goals of campus natural history museums
*Updated April 2026', 'nhmc.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://thenhccn.wixsite.com/nhccn/university-of-california-riverside-1#!', 'https://www.instagram.com/nhmc_at_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/nhmc'),
(70980, 'Navigators at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Wednesday, 7:00pm - 9:30pm', 'Every two weeks', 'The Navigators is an interdenominational, student, Christian organization seeking to meet the spiritual needs of students. We are a people growing in our faith through deep relationship and the Bible.
Our mission is "To know Christ, make Him known, and help others do the same."', 'We are a people growing in our faith through deep relationship and the Bible. We meet weekly as an organization, provide bible studies and opportunities for Christian discipleship', 'The Navigators is an interdenominational, student, Christian organization seeking to meet the spiritual needs of students. We are a people growing in our faith through deep relationship and the Bible.
Our mission is "To know Christ, make Him known, and help others do the same."', 'tobie.owl@navigators.org', 'https://linktr.ee/ucrnavs', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrnavs/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/navigators'),
(425073, 'NeuroPsychology Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays at 5pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Build bridges between the neuroscience and psychology field.', 'Build bridges between the neuroscience and psychology field by bringing people interested in the brain’s structure, mental processes, and development, through fun activities and learning experiences.', 'neuropsychology.ucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/neuropsychatucr/?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/neuropsych'),
(222305, 'Neuroscience Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'FAQ
When do you meet?
-- We meet every other week throughout the quarter from 7-8 pm with occasional socials or lab tours on off weeks.
Where do you meet?
-- We meet in the Student Success Center Multi Purpose Room 1 (MPR 1).
What do you do in your meetings?
--In our meetings, we explore topics related to the brain, including brain structure, brain chemistry, and brain function, as well as their applications to fields such as psychology and child development. We also host engaging socials, fun activities, interactive workshops, and other events that foster connection, collaboration, and professional growth.', 'This club is meant for people with a common interest in the brain, its fuctions, and affect on thought and behavior. We hope to provide a place to discuss our common interest and provide a more interactive, fun resource for learning about the brain.', 'Thank you for your interest in UCR''s Neuroscience Club. This club is for people with a common interest in the brain, its functions, and its effect on thought and behavior. Anyone is free to join regardless of what major you''re in. There is no knowledge requirement or an expectation that you have taken any neuroscience classes at UCR. We hope we can provide you with a place to discuss our common interest as well as provide a more interactive and fun resource for learning about the brain.
FAQ
When do you meet?
-- We meet every other week throughout the quarter from 7-8 pm with occasional socials or lab tours on off weeks.
Where do you meet?
-- We meet in the Student Success Center Multi Purpose Room 1 (MPR 1).
What do you do in your meetings?
--In our meetings, we explore topics related to the brain, including brain structure, brain chemistry, and brain function, as well as their applications to fields such as psychology and child development. We also host engaging socials, fun activities, interactive workshops, and other events that foster connection, collaboration, and professional growth.', 'neuroclub1000@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrneuroclub/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/neuroclub'),
(70891, 'Neuroscience Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Friday 12PM-1PM', 'Monthly', null, 'We vow to be an academic/social organization, with its own independent finances, empowered to represent graduate students, and to affect academic program policy.', 'We vow to be an academic/social organization, with its own independent finances, empowered to represent graduate students, and to affect academic program policy. The purposes of this organization shall be: To create an association that will allow students of the UCR graduate program in Neuroscience to participate in the administrative affairs of the program; To foster an open atmosphere conducive towards the advancement of the students higher education; To provide a forum where members of the organization may voice their opinions and express their views; and To hold events that will promote program identity and unity.', 'iwarr004@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrneuro/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ngsa'),
(71010, 'Nigerian Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'To spread and share Nigerian culture, provide a network from students to others, and increase awareness of Nigerian students presence.', 'To spread and share Nigerian culture, provide a network from students to others, and increase awareness of Nigerian students presence.', 'ucriversidensa@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrnsa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/nsa'),
(70831, 'Nikkei Student Union', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Thursday 8:00 PM', 'Every two weeks', 'Nikkei Student Union (NSU) is an socio-cultural organization devoted to promoting, preserving, and educating the surrounding community and college-aged youth about the history of Japanese and Japanese Americans through cultural events and social activities.
We host bi-weekly General Meetings where our NSU community gather to learn more about Japanese American Culture, participate in engaging games and icebreaker activities, as well as hear more about upcoming events open to General Members.
If you''d like to learn more about the club or keep up to date with our events, follow us @ucrnsu on Instagram.
Check our linktree for additional resources if you don''t have/use Instagram', 'Japanese-American Social and Cultural Club', 'Nikkei Student Union (NSU) is an socio-cultural organization devoted to promoting, preserving, and educating the surrounding community and college-aged youth about the history of Japanese and Japanese Americans through cultural events and social activities.
We host bi-weekly General Meetings where our NSU community gather to learn more about Japanese American Culture, participate in engaging games and icebreaker activities, as well as hear more about upcoming events open to General Members.
If you''d like to learn more about the club or keep up to date with our events, follow us @ucrnsu on Instagram.
Check our linktree for additional resources if you don''t have/use Instagram', 'ucr.nsu@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/ucrnsu', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrnsu/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/nsu'),
(70812, 'Oasis Christian Fellowship', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Weekly - Friday, 7:00 PM to 9:00 PM @ Dundee A1003', 'Weekly', 'Oasis Christian Fellowship (OCF) is a Christian organization on campus that exists to help students find life, community, and faith in Jesus. Inspired by the idea of an oasis in the desert, we aim to be a place of refreshment in the midst of college life, where students can feel supported, known, and spiritually encouraged.
We meet weekly to study the Bible, grow in our faith, and build meaningful relationships. Throughout the week, we also spend time hanging out, studying together, and creating fun and memorable experiences as a community. Whether you are a Christian looking to grow deeper in your faith or someone who is simply curious and exploring, Oasis is a welcoming space for you to ask questions and walk alongside others.
If you would like to get in contact with us, feel free to message us or fill out our interest form. For the most up-to-date information on upcoming events, check out our website and events page.
If you would like to get in contact with us, feel free to message us and/or fill out this form.
