(347179, 'Omega Psi Phi Fraternity, Inc', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'First Friday of the Month', 'Monthly', null, 'Omega Psi Phi Fraternity, Inc. is a brotherhood founded on the Cardinal Principles of Manhood, Scholarship, Perseverance, and Uplift.', 'Since its humble beginnings on the Howard University campus, the Omega Psi Phi Fraternity continues to be on the front line, leveraging its power, influence and more than 100 years of commitment to the uplift of our people and our communities.', 'Sigmaeta76@gmail.com', 'oppf12d.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/sigmaeta1976/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sigmaeta76'),
(71126, 'Order of Omega', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'To recognize greeks that have attained a high standard of leadership in inter-greek activities, to encourage them to continue along this line, and to inspire others to strive for similar conspicuous attainment.', 'To recognize members of the greek community that have embody the values of the FSIC and have attained a high standard of leadership in inter-greek activities to encourage them to continue along this line, and to inspire others to strive for similar conspicuous attainment.', 'ka.orderofomega@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ka.orderofomega/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/orderofomega'),
(414087, 'Our Protectors of Animal Wellbeing and Safety', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose of this organization is to provide hands-on animal volunteer experience, spread animal care awareness, create a space for animal lovers to gather, and overall contribute to the well-being of animals.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to provide hands-on animal volunteer experience, spread animal care awareness, create a space for animal lovers to gather, and overall contribute to the well-being of animals.', 'rp.a.w.s.ucrboard@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/rpawsucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/r_p.a.w.s._ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rpaws'),
(71041, 'Pacific Islander Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'WELCOME TO PISA! 

Follow us on Instagram for the latest updates!
Instagram: @pisa_ucr', 'Pacific Islander Student Association (PISA) is an organization that will thrive on enhancing the experience of Pacific Islanders on-campus and off-campus. PISA seeks to provide a space for its members to articulate their experiences and share their individual cultures with each other and the larger university and community populations. This in turn, will serve as an avenue to promote and establish cultural solidarity, leadership, diversity, tolerance and respect. The students and associates of the Pacific Islander Student Association want to promote both Pacific Islander culture and Pacific Islander unity in the community. For instance, hosting a Pacific Islander High School Conference will help promote the benefits of higher education.', 'pisaucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/pisa_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pisaatucr'),
(70860, 'Pakistani Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Thursday', 'Every two weeks', null, 'We are a student organization open to all undergraduate & graduate students, staff, and faculty. We seek to bring together those members of the community that share our interest in the social, cultural, and political milieu of Pakistan.', 'This is a student group open to all undergraduate & graduate students, staff, and faculty. We seek to bring together those members of the community that share our interest in the social, cultural, and political milieu of Pakistan and Central & South Asia. The club was founded with hopes of fostering diversity and understanding amongst the campus. Follow us on our social media accounts for updates and events -- Instagram: @psaucr', 'ucriversidepsa@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/psaucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/psaucr'),
(333446, 'Partners in Health Engage at UC Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Thursdays 7-8', 'Every two weeks', null, '"Health care is a human right. At PIH, this core belief drives everything we do—from hospital bedsides to the streets. Join us in our fight." - Partners in Health', '"Health care is a human right. At PIH, this core belief drives everything we do—from hospital bedsides to the streets. Injustice has a cure. Join us in our fight." - Partners in Health
At Partners In Health we hold fundraising events to raise money to help those in third world countries or who are struggling to obtain healthcare. We also hold Advocacy events, calls, and emails, where we speak to Members of Congress and House of Representative Members to pass more legislation, advocating for equal healthcare for all. And Lastly, we create Community Engagement events where we go to placed in the community, explain our mission, and pass out resources to those who need healthcare.', 'partnersinhealthucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.pih.org/organize', 'https://instagram.com/pihengage_ucr?igshid=1cfcnqvb0a5yd', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pihengageucr'),
(425265, 'Pediatric Hope Project', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Pediatric Hope Project provides a free tutoring program connecting K-12th-grade pediatric patients with volunteer college students. The aim is to supply educational support during treatment.', 'The Pediatric Hope Project provides a free tutoring program connecting K-12th-grade pediatric patients with volunteer college students. The aim is to supply educational support during treatment.', 'pediatrichopeproject@gmail.com', 'https://www.pediatrichopeproject.com/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/thepediatrichopeprojectucr'),
(180867, 'PERIOD. @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Subject to change every quarter', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The mission of PERIOD@UCR is to celebrate and promote menstrual health through advocacy, education, and service.', 'The mission of PERIOD@UCR is to celebrate and promote menstrual health through advocacy, education, and service. We host period packaging events, educational workshops, and work on campus policy to eliminate period poverty and normalize conversations about periods.', 'period.ucr@gmail.com', 'http://periodatucr.weebly.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/period.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/periodatucr'),
(71139, 'Phi Alpha Delta Pre-Law Fraternity', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays, 8-9 PM: Active Members & Wednesdays, 8-9PM: New Members', 'Weekly', null, 'Phi Alpha Delta Law Fraternity, International is a professional law fraternity
advancing integrity, compassion and courage through service to the student, the school,
the profession and the community.', 'MISSION
Phi Alpha Delta Law Fraternity, International is a professional pre-law fraternity
advancing integrity, compassion and courage through service to the student, the school,
the profession and the community.
VISION
We are the preeminent law fraternity promoting the bonds of fraternalism and we are the
leader in the development and advancement of professional ideals.
CORE VALUES
Bound together by tradition and our common interest in the law, we share these core values:
Integrity, Compassion, Courage, Professionalism, Service, Diversity, and Innovation.
DECLARATION OF PURPOSE
The purpose of this Fraternity shall be to form a strong bond uniting students and teachers of the law
with members of the Bench and Bar in a fraternal fellowship designed to advance the ideals of liberty
and equal justice under law; to stimulate excellence in scholarship; to inspire the virtues of compassion
and courage; to foster integrity and professional competence; to promote the welfare of its members;
and to encourage their moral, intellectual, and cultural advancement; so that each member may enjoy a
lifetime of honorable professional and public service.
tion to professional advancements. We host an annual Lawyer Banquet in the Fall, which allows new and active members exposure to speak and network with lawyers. In Winter, we have winter retreat (a small trip we take to bond with one another)! Then, we have Spring formals and Alumni Networking in the Spring! These main events are hosted in conjunction to smaller events that help to provide students with career opportunities and professional development. The difference between Phi Alpha Delta and other pre-law organizations is our preeminent role in creating strong networks and relationships; we have a mentor mentee program, similar to a big/little program that establishes lifelong relationships with other students who are entering the legal profession as well. This dynamic may help to provide employment and internship opportunities, in addition to advice in every aspect. Many mentor mentee relationships help towards assimilating into university life and into the legal community in terms of law school or gap year opportunities. With this in mind, Phi Alpha Delta is the perfect place to begin learning about law! By providing members with events and resources, as well as individual experiences, Phi Alpha Delta is a diversified organization that provides opportunities in every aspect!', 'president@ucrpad.org', 'https://pad.ucrhighlanders.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrphialphadelta/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pad-prelaw-fraternity'),
(102180, 'Phi Beta Kappa', 'Department Affiliated Organization', null, null, null, null, 'please update', null, null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/phibettakappa'),
(330729, 'Phi Beta Sigma Fraternity, Inc.', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'From its inception, the Founders conceived Phi Beta Sigma as a mechanism to deliver services to the general community.', 'Phi Beta Sigma Fraternity was founded at Howard University in Washington, D.C., January 9, 1914, by three young African-American male students. The Founders, Honorable A. Langston Taylor, Honorable Leonard F. Morse, and Honorable Charles I. Brown, wanted to organize a Greek letter fraternity that would truly exemplify the ideals of brotherhood, scholarship, and service. From its inception, the Founders also conceived Phi Beta Sigma as a mechanism to deliver services to the general community. Rather than gaining skills to be utilized exclusively for themselves and their immediate families, the founders of Phi Beta Sigma held a deep conviction that they should return their newly acquired skills to the communities from which they had come. This deep conviction was mirrored in the Fraternity''s motto, "Culture For Service and Service For Humanity."', 'phibetasigma.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.ucrsigmas.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrsigmas/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/phibetasigmafraternityinc'),
(138489, 'Phi Chi Theta', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Thursdays at 8pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Phi Chi Theta at UCR is a co-educational business and fraternity dedicated to creating well-balanced leaders through involvement, empowerment, and philanthropy. We are committed to building the next generation of business leaders.', 'Phi Chi Theta at UCR is a co-educational business and economics fraternity dedicated to creating well-balanced leaders through involvement, empowerment, and philanthropy. We are committed to building the next generation of business leaders.
https://ucrpct.com/
Follow our Instagram for more: @ucrpct', 'ucrpct@gmail.com', 'https://www.ucrpct.com/', 'http://www.instagram.com/ucrpct', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrpct'),
(71196, 'Phi Delta Epsilon International Medical Fraternity', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Sunday at 7:00 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Phi Delta Epsilon is an International Co-Educational Medical Fraternity. We pride ourselves in our motto, "Facta Non-Verba, Deeds Not Words."', 'Phi Delta Epsilon International Medical Fraternity creates physicians of integrity with a lifelong commitment to our guiding principles of philanthropy, deity, and education through fellowship, service, mentoring, and formal training in leadership, science, and ethics. As UC Riverside''s only co-educational medical fraternity, we take pride in our close camaraderie and unparalleled diversity.
UC Riverside''s pre-medical chapter, formally known as the California Delta Chapter, was officially chartered in the spring of 2013. UC Riverside students with the aspiration to one day become physicians now have the opportunity to become part of a network of prestigious undergraduate universities and medical schools all over the globe. CA Delta is eagerly awaiting the chance to welcome new brothers and sisters into our fraternity so that we may build new traditions together that will last for the remainder of UC Riverside''s history.
If you are interested in more information about Phi Delta Epsilon, our California Delta Chapter, or joining our family, please feel free to contact us through our email since we limit our HighlanderLink roster to active members only.', 'phideucr@gmail.com', 'http://phideucr.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/phideucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/phide'),
(104149, 'Physician Associates of Tomorrow', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesday-Thursday 7-8 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose of this organization is to educate students about the role of Physician Assistants (PA) in the medical field and the requirements for PA schools.  We aim to bring students closer to becoming a Physician Assistant.', 'The purpose of this organization is to educate students about the role of Physician Assistants (PA) in the medical field and the requirements for PA schools. We guide and prepare students to become better PA school applicants by providing information, networking and volunteer opportunities. Our goal is to bring students closer to becoming a Physician Assistant.
Please follow our instagram for regular updates about events and opportunities: @PATATUCR', 'patatucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/patatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pat'),
(70927, 'Pi Beta Phi Fraternity for Women', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Monday @ 8:00pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Pi Beta Phi Fraternity is an organization for women, which seeks to promote friendship, development women of intellect and integrity, cultivate leadership potential and enrich lives through community service.', 'Pi Beta Phi is a women’s organization dedicated to friendship, leadership, personal growth, and academic excellence. Founded in 1867 as the first national fraternity for women, it fosters a supportive community where members are encouraged to lead with integrity and make a positive impact.
Through leadership opportunities and its philanthropic initiative, Read > Lead > Achieve, Pi Beta Phi promotes service, educational access, and lifelong connections among its members.
These relationships help members adapt to college life by providing a sense of mutual support and guidance. But, finding a place to belong on campus is only the beginning. Pi Beta Phi’s many programs offer a variety of services and benefits to its members including a lifetime of sisterhood, personal development, philanthropic service, leadership opportunities, mentor relationships and networking.
MISSION
The mission of Pi Beta Phi Fraternity for Women is to promote friendship, develop women of intellect and integrity, cultivate leadership potential and enrich lives through community service.
VISION
The vision of Pi Beta Phi Fraternity for Women is to be recognized as a premier organization for women by providing lifelong enrichment to its members and contributing to the betterment of society.
CORE VALUES
•Integrity
•Lifelong Commitment
•Honor and Respect
•Personal and Intellectual Growth
•Philanthropic Service to Others
•Sincere Friendship
READ. LEAD. ACHIEVE.
Today, the Fraternity continues to be a vehicle for serving others in the field of literacy. Pi Beta Phi’s 100-year literacy vision reads: Pi Beta Phi leads the way to a more literate society. The vision is supported by our Read. Lead. Achieve.® literacy platform, which includes the following initiatives:
• Champions are Readers (CAR): Pi Phi’s hands-on program, CAR is a monthlong reading enrichment program for third-grade elementary students. CAR encourages students to develop daily reading habits and provides Fraternity members with an easy-to-implement program encouraging family literacy.
• First Book: Pi Phi is proud of its corporate partnership with First Book, an international nonprofit organization founded in 1992 with a single mission: to give children from low-income families the opportunity to read and own their first new books. In five years, Pi Phi and First Book donated nearly 3 million brand-new books to children who would otherwise not have a book of their own.
• Fraternity Day of Service: Pi Beta Phi celebrates Fraternity Day of Service in an effort to advance literacy on or around March 2 in honor of Dr. Seuss’® birthday. Every year, Pi Beta Phi sponsors a Fraternity-wide event in order to achieve maximum impact in fundraising and awareness.
• Arrow in the Arctic: Pi Phi’s Canadian philanthropy, Arrow in the Arctic, supports literacy in Canada’s Northern library systems: the Yukon, Northwest Territories and Nunavut. Arrow in the Arctic also helps to preserve the language and culture of the north’s Inuit and First Nations. Pi Beta Phi is the only National Panhellenic Conference (NPC) group to have its own Canadian philanthropy.
• Local Literacy Initiatives and Service: Local literacy initiatives promote and improve literacy in Pi Phi communities, reaffirm the Fraternity’s commitment to and impact on youth education, and provide an opportunity for Pi Beta Phi chapters and alumnae organizations to see the direct impact of their work how it affects children in their communities.
If you are interested in learning more about this Fraternity, please visit our National website at pibetaphi.org.
If you wish to contact our national headquarters, please see the information below:
Pi Beta Phi Headquarters
1154 Town & Country Commons Drive
Town & Country, Missouri 63017
PH: (636) 256–0680
FAX: (636) 256–8095', 'cp.calambda@gmail.com', 'http://www.pibetaphi.org/ucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrpiphi', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pibetaphi'),
(412120, 'Pi Kappa Phi', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Monday 9pm', 'Weekly', null, 'Pi Kappa Phi was founded by exceptional men who chose to lead. For more than a century, we have stayed true to our roots, developing the next generation of servant leaders who put service before self and work to improve the world around them.', 'Our Mission :
To create an uncommon and lifelong brotherhood that develops leaders and encourages service to others for the betterment of our communities.
Our Vision:
A future where every Pi Kappa Phi embraces his role as a leader, puts service before self and improves the world around him.
Our Public Values:
Common Loyalty, Personal Responsibility, Achievement, Accountability, Campus Involvement, Responsible Citizenship, Lifelong Commitment.', 'archon.ucrpikapps@gmail.com', 'https://pikapp.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/pikappucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pikappaphi'),
(365506, 'Pi Sigma Alpha', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Honors']::text[], 'Weekday Evenings', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to stimulate scholarship and interest in Political Science by providing tangible recognition to students who have excelled in the field.', 'Pi Sigma Alpha is the National Political Science Honor Society. It is the only honor society at UCR that recognizes and promotes the high academic achievement in those who are pursing in the field of political science. With specialized events, activities,
and membership opportunities offered for those apart, we seek to help the future leaders in this field grow. Be apart for your hard work and get the recognition you deserve.', 'ucrpsahonors@gmail.com', 'https://politicalscience.ucr.edu/psa', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr.psa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/psa'),
(385324, 'Pi Sigma Epsilon', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesdays', 'Weekly', null, 'An organization dedicated to preparing the emerging workforce with the core competencies necessary for success.', 'PSE is a dynamic organization dedicated to fostering professional development, particularly in the realms of sales, marketing, and management. It offers a unique platform for students to enhance their skills, engage in real-world business scenarios, and build a supportive network with an emphasis on leadership, ethical conduct, and teamwork.', 'pres.pseatucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrpse?igsh=MW5vMGJzZTkyZzFtYw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pse'),
(381973, 'Pickleball Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Mondays 8-10 PM and Wednesdays 8-10 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'Welcome to the Pickleball Club at UCR!  We invite you to join us to learn, improve, and enjoy the game of pickleball.  Open to all, beginner friendly!', 'Welcome to the Pickleball Club at the University of California, Riverside! We offer recreational pickleball for students, staff, and faculty. Join us to improve your pickleball skills, enjoy social events, and make new connections. Open to all skill levels!
How to register:
Step 1: Sign up on the SRC''s Do Sports Easy Website - https://recreation.ucr.edu/competitive-sports/sport-clubs
Click on the link above and scroll down to the Pickleball Club, then click "Registration". Follow the steps on the website to officially register through the club (this is a separate process from Highlander Link because we are an SRC-affiliated organization).
Step 2: Bring your Student ID card whenever you attend one of our open plays. THIS IS IMPORTANT. Without your Student ID, the SRC employees cannot check you into the club.
Step 3: Have Fun! See you out there Highlanders!', 'pickleballclubatucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/pickleballclubatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pickleball'),
(382009, 'Planned Parenthood Generation Action at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Tuesdays 6:30', 'Every two weeks', null, 'We aspire to mobilize advocacy efforts at UR surrounding sexual and reproductive health and justice, educate student body, and create lasting change on and off campus.', 'We aspire to mobilize advocacy efforts at UCR surrounding sexual and reproductive health and justice, educate student body, and create lasting change on and off campus.', 'ppgaatucr@gmail.com', 'https://ppgaatucr.weebly.com', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ppgaucr'),
(76127, 'Plant Pathology Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Thursdays 1-2 pm', 'Monthly', null, 'The goal of the PLPA GSA is form a community for the graduate students in the Plant Pathology department.', 'The goal of the PLPA GSA is form a community for the graduate students in the Plant Pathology department to encourage student excellence and success.', 'vvale009@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/plpagsa'),
(430921, 'Pokemon Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Our first meeting of the year is October 14th from 6-7 PM in OLMH 1136', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to serve as a welcoming community for UCR students, both graduate and undergraduate, and faculty to congregate together to discuss and play Pokémon.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to serve as a welcoming community for UCR students, both graduate and undergraduate, and faculty to congregate together to discuss and play Pokémon. The club’s values are to be inclusive and mindful, while considering all aspects of the hobby equally.', 'cmoni005@ucr.edu', 'https://discord.gg/aVggevbmdk', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pokemonclubucr'),
(70868, 'Pre-Dental Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'We have events at least once a week, including 3 general meetings per quarter typically on Tuesday evenings. We will always announce our meeting times on our Instagram page and Google Calendar.', 'Weekly', null, 'Pre-Dental Society is a pre-dental organization at UCR that offers dental exposure and leadership opportunities for undergraduate students who are passionate about dentistry.', 'Pre-Dental Society at UCR (est. 2010) offers dental exposure and leadership/mentorship opportunities for undergraduate students who are passionate about dentistry. Students will have the opportunity to go on dental school tours, volunteer at the Riverside Free Clinic for hands-on dental experience, join our mentorship program, learn more about the dental school application process, and participate in other volunteer opportunities within our community. Our PDS family offers a supportive community open to all. Sign up for 2026-2027 membership here!', 'ucrpredentalsociety@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrpds/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pds'),
(425058, 'Pre-Student Osteopathic Medical Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Monthly', 'Pre-SOMA is the undergraduate branch of the Student Osteopathic Medical Association (SOMA). It allows pre-medical students to explore osteopathic medicine, connect with DO students and physicians, and decide if the DO path is right for them. The Pre-SOMA Committee promotes osteopathic medicine, supports aspiring DOs, and provides networking and educational opportunities.
A DO (Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine) is a fully licensed physician who can practice all areas of medicine, including surgery. DOs receive additional training in osteopathic manipulative medicine and focus on whole-person, patient-centered care.
SOMA, founded in 1970, is the largest osteopathic medical student organization with over 15,000 members. It supports osteopathic medical students, represents their voices within the American Osteopathic Association, and helps shape the future of osteopathic medicine. SOMA is student-run at both local and national levels.', 'The purpose of this organization is to increase the awareness about osteopathic medicine, provide interested students resources and information about osteopathic medicine, and help others in the community through service.', 'Pre-SOMA is the undergraduate branch of the Student Osteopathic Medical Association (SOMA). It allows pre-medical students to explore osteopathic medicine, connect with DO students and physicians, and decide if the DO path is right for them. The Pre-SOMA Committee promotes osteopathic medicine, supports aspiring DOs, and provides networking and educational opportunities.
A DO (Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine) is a fully licensed physician who can practice all areas of medicine, including surgery. DOs receive additional training in osteopathic manipulative medicine and focus on whole-person, patient-centered care.
SOMA, founded in 1970, is the largest osteopathic medical student organization with over 15,000 members. It supports osteopathic medical students, represents their voices within the American Osteopathic Association, and helps shape the future of osteopathic medicine. SOMA is student-run at both local and national levels.', null, 'studentdo.org/pre-soma/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrpresoma?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrpresoma'),
(385055, 'Pre-Therapy Student Organization', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays 7-8pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to inform students about career path options in therapy and learn more about how to get into a therapy program. This organization aims to provide resources for students who have interests in a therapy career.', 'The purpose of this organization is to inform students about career path options in therapy and learn more about some requirements for certain therapy programs. This organization aims to provide resources for students who have interests in a therapy career (including but not limited to: physical, occupational, counseling, etc) by bringing in professionals in the field, touring therapy schools, etc.', 'mrami332@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_ptso?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pretherapystudentorg'),
