Stay up to date on our meeting times and volunteer opportunities by contacting us to be added to our groupme and discord or visiting our website!', 'ucrpreveterinaryclub@gmail.com', 'http://ucrprevetclub.weebly.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrpreveterinaryclub/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pvc'),
(71149, 'Precision For Vision', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays 6:30PM-7:30PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'To provide members with the opportunity to network with fellow Pre-Optometry students, eye care professionals (OD), and optometry school deans & admissions staff, to volunteer in various community health initiatives for the underserved, and more!', 'Precision for Vision is a pre-optometry organization at UCR dedicated to uniting and supporting pre-optometry students. Our mission is to provide guidance to members related to the pathway and overall journey to becoming future ODs (Doctors of Optometry). Members are provided with further knowledge regarding the pathway, volunteering/hands-on experience, and networking opportunities.
PFV hosts optometry students, optometrists, graduate school deans and admissions, and more! Members broaden their knowledge of graduate programs as well as what it takes to be a competitive professional school applicant. Members are given the opportunity to network and connect with fellow pre-optometry and optometry people. Members can gain hands-on experience and volunteering through community service events.
Follow us for updates!
IG: https://www.instagram.com/precisionforvision
Website: http://precisionforvision.wix.com/ucrpfv
Email: precisionforvision@gmaill.com', 'precisionforvision@gmail.com', 'http://precisionforvision.wix.com/ucrpfv', 'https://www.instagram.com/precisionforvision/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pfv'),
(402926, 'Product Management Club', 'Registered Student Organization', null, 'Wednesday evenings', 'Weekly', 'The Product Management Consulting (PMC) Club is a student-led organization dedicated to empowering students with hands-on experience in product management and technology entrepreneurship. Our mission is to provide students with the knowledge, tools, and
resources needed to bring tech startup ideas to life. Through collaboration, mentorship, and practical experience, we aim to foster a supportive environment where students can develop and test innovative ideas, ultimately equipping them with the skills to
lead or participate in tech-driven projects or startups.', 'The Product Management Club (PMC) is a student-led organization dedicated to empowering students with hands-on experience in product management and technology entrepreneurship through projects, lessons, and competitive events.', 'The Product Management Consulting (PMC) Club is a student-led organization dedicated to empowering students with hands-on experience in product management and technology entrepreneurship. Our mission is to provide students with the knowledge, tools, and
resources needed to bring tech startup ideas to life. Through collaboration, mentorship, and practical experience, we aim to foster a supportive environment where students can develop and test innovative ideas, ultimately equipping them with the skills to
lead or participate in tech-driven projects or startups.', 'spale009@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/productmanagementclub'),
(431040, 'Professionals in Political Science', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to facilitate and foster a safe space for all individuals including but not limited to public policy and political science majors seeking non-law specific career advice, development, and opportunities.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to facilitate and foster a safe space for all individuals, including but not limited to Public Policy and Political Science majors, seeking career advice, professional development, and opportunities to explore the diverse career paths available within the fields of government, public policy, public administration, nonprofit organizations, advocacy, international affairs, research, diplomacy, public service, and other careers within the political science and public policy field', 'professionalsinpolisci@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pips'),
(345158, 'Programming Club at UCR', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'Monday 3:30pm', 'Weekly', null, 'The Programming Club at UCR is a graduate student organization created to help fellow graduate students learn finance and information system industry-specific programs.', 'The Programming Club at UCR is a graduate student organization created to help fellow graduate students learn finance and information system industry-specific programs. We explore the fundamentals of multiple programs each year and use a student-teach student method to really bring connectivity within the club. The students decide what to learn as a group, as well as how fast they want to learn and who will teach it. By doing this we are bringing the positive experiences that every student has to offer, and if you are brand new to these programs you can start from the beginning at a good pace, and one day help teach others!', 'amalh017@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/programmingclubatucr'),
(425056, 'Project 70mm', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Friday 8pm', 'Every two weeks', 'Project 70mm is a Student Led Organization at the University of California, Riverside dedicated to inspiring interest and awareness for the beauty of South Asian films in all genres and languages. Our organization''s goal is to create an inclusive space for exploring and celebrating cinema through regular screenings, discussions, and themed events.
We meet biweekly, and have plenty of events, snacks, and debates in store! Join our HighlanderLink to receive updates on our meeting times and check out our Instagram @Project70mm', 'Showcasing films of all genres and languages to create interest and awareness for South Asian film culture', 'Project 70mm is a Student Led Organization at the University of California, Riverside dedicated to inspiring interest and awareness for the beauty of South Asian films in all genres and languages. Our organization''s goal is to create an inclusive space for exploring and celebrating cinema through regular screenings, discussions, and themed events.
We meet biweekly, and have plenty of events, snacks, and debates in store! Join our HighlanderLink to receive updates on our meeting times and check out our Instagram @Project70mm', 'project70mm.ucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/project70mm'),
(425363, 'Project Forget Me Knot at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional','Service']::text[], 'Tuesdays at 5PM', 'Weekly', null, 'To provide high quality emotional support and care for senior residents of the Inland Empire and other underserved communities in California through volunteer-led recreational, musical, and social interaction-oriented service events.', 'Project Forget Me Knot is a non-profit student-led organization committed to providing high quality emotional support and care for senior residents of the Inland Empire and other underserved communities in California through volunteer-led recreational, musical, and social interaction-oriented service events. We aim to raise awareness and combat mistreatment while also bringing comfort to individuals residing in senior living and assisted care facilities.
Our volunteering opportunities are perfect for pre-health and pre-med students! If you are interested in learning more, check out our socials @fmkucr on Instagram for a sneak peek of what we''re up to. Drop us a DM or email with any questions and we can''t wait to see you at our events!', 'fmkucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/fmkucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/fmkucr'),
(382939, 'Project Lux', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Sunday Night', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Project Lux is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit student-run organization dedicated to bridging the gap between healthcare and houselessness. Our chapter is primarily focused on health insurance enrollment, community service and advocacy.', 'Project Lux is an organization committed to health equity.
We work toward achieving this goal through enrolling individuals experiencing houselessness in health insurance programs, such as Medical, and helping these individuals with other basic health care needs.
Additionally, we work with student volunteers whom we hope to inspire to continue to create change in their communities. We aim to help these volunteers recognize this broad issue and give them a platform through which they can make a tangible impact. We envision a world in which no individual is discouraged from receiving medical aid due to unaffordable services.', 'ucr@projectluxnp.org', 'https://www.theprojectlux.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/projectluxucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/projectlux'),
(425459, 'Project Pulmonary Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 7pm', 'Monthly', null, 'PPM Riverside is a community-based organization established for the purpose of promoting public awareness regarding the harmful effects of carcinogen exposure and other wildfire-related hazards on firefighters and other first-responders.', 'This organization is dedicated to advancing lung health and safety through awareness, advocacy, and direct service. Its mission includes, but is not limited to, collaborating with municipal and regional fire departments, providing financial and material assistance such as donations, organizing educational and community outreach programs, conducting public awareness campaigns, and advocating for improved protective policies, safety standards, and PPE equipment.
PPM hopes to support lung health in any way whether that is through education campaigns, volunteering, lung cancer research, or public health endeavors.
Project Pulmonary Riverside stands with the key values of honor, accountability, service, and collaboration. This organization is committed to maintaining transparency, integrity, and professionalism while serving its community. Through partnerships and community service, PPM Riverside seeks to strengthen the health and well-being of firefighters and others who face lung disease while promoting improvements in pulmonary healthcare and rehabilitation.', 'projectpulmonaryriverside@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/projectpulmonaryriverside'),
(99659, 'Project RISHI at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'We are a national non-profit organization that works to promote the sustainable growth and development of rural Indian villages.', 'In partnership with local community members and social enterprises, we identify issues that are central to the villages we support and then provide the resources to implement solutions. We do this by fundraising throughout the year in hopes of being able to afford important supplies for the village and by taking trips as a group every summer to first-hand offer help, deliver supplies, and implement new helpful systems. UCR''s chapter of the organization works specifically with a village Uttarakhand. Every year we continue to build off of our efforts in hopes of one day bringing this village to a place where they can support themselves
Project RISHI', 'ucriverside@projectrishi.org', 'http://www.projectrishi.org/ucriverside/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrprishi/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/projectrishi'),
(175661, 'Project Sunshine at University of California Riverside School of Medicine Chapter', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'We meet biweekly on varying days in the evening, in the HUB. See our Instagram for up-to-date information!', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Project Sunshine is a nonprofit organization that provides free educational, recreational, and social programs to children and families living with medical challenges.', 'Bringing joy and play to pediatric patients!
Project Sunshine is a nonprofit organization that provides free educational, recreational, and social programs to children and families living with medical challenges. We offer volunteering experiences both in-person and on Zoom.
"Project Sunshine brings volunteer-led programming to pediatric patients and their families in a variety of medical settings. We recognize the tremendous weight of managing a child’s illness or injury, whether it requires short-term or long-term care. Every child with a medical challenge is unique, and our programs seek to adapt to the individual needs of each child."
https://projectsunshine.org/?hsLang=en', 'projectsunshineucriverside@gmail.com', 'http://www.projectsunshine.org', 'https://www.instagram.com/psucriverside/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/projectsunshine'),
(408655, 'PROsthetics Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to promote student exposure to the varying applications of prosthetics, engaging students from all engineering and CNAS backgrounds with an emphasis on medicinal applications I.E. creating mock prosthetics.', null, null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/prosthetics_club'),
(71146, 'Providing Opportunities Dreams and Education in Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Mondays 6-7pm for Spring 2026!', 'Weekly', null, 'Established in 2008, PODER seeks to provide assistance to undocumented students through mentorship, financial assistance, and community building.', 'Our Mission:
Established in 2008, PODER seeks to provide assistance to undocumented students through mentorship, financial assistance, and community building. PODER is aware that the Riverside community lacks such resources for the immigrant population; therefore PODER serves as a pipeline of information for those in need.
Goals of PODER:
Provide a safe environment where undocumented students can feel at home with a group of people who understand similar struggles.
Educate the community about Assembly Bill 540, CA DREAM Act, Deferred Action, and immigration reform.
Assist undocumented students in the transition from high school or community college and provide mentorship.
Provide financial assistance through scholarships and/or other resources.
Advocate for the rights of all undocumented immigrants.
What We Do:
Annual Events:
“Dreaming of a Higher Education” Conference: Our annual conference brings students from the Inland Empire and Coachella Valley to UC Riverside for a day of workshops and presentations regarding AB540, CA Dream Act, DACA, Access to Higher Education, immigration policy updates, among other topics that are crucial to immigrant communities!
Immigrant Awareness Week: We dedicated a whole week to bring awareness to UC Riverside about immigrant communities and their intersectional identities.
Coming Out of the Shadows: During Immigrant Awareness Week, PODER hosts “Coming Out of the Shadows” event at the Bell Tower. Students have the safe space to come out publicly as undocumented and share their stories. On April 3rd, 2014 PODER hosted the first “Coming Out of the Shadows” event at UC Riverside to empower our undocumented peers to be “Unafraid and Unashamed”.
“Investing in the Dream” Fundraiser Banquet: Our annual banquet helps raise scholarship funds for undocumented students.
Other Work:
Workshops/ Presentations: PODER provides presentations on DACA, AB 540, CA DREAM Act and the experience of undocumented students at high schools and other community events.
Advocate for undocumented Students: PODER advocates for equal opportunities and resources for undocumented students. In October 2013, we were able to get ASUCR to pass a resolution in support of undocumented students. PODER also advocates for undocumented students at the University of California Office of the President through their student representative. As part of a UC wide undocumented student coalition, UC Riverside and other UC campus were allocated $5 million to support undocumented students.', 'PODERatUCR@Gmail.com', 'http://usp.ucr.edu/poder', 'https://www.instagram.com/poderatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/poder'),
(71108, 'Psi Chi Psychology Honor Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Honors']::text[], 'Evenings during the week', 'Every two weeks', 'Our general meetings are typically held every other week of the quarter. For more information on becoming a member and other frequently asked questions, please visit our website.
____________________________
With over 1,000 chapters in U.S. colleges and universities, Psi Chi is the National Honor Society for Psychology. It was founded in 1929 for graduate and undergraduate students who strive to maintain academic excellence and advance the science of Psychology.
Psi Chi is a purely academic honors society based on academic merit and scholastic achievement. Psi Chi is not a fraternity or sorority. We are the primary psychology organization on campus and we provide numerous opportunities for professional development, networking, and leadership experience through our general meetings, workshops, socials, and volunteering events throughout the year.
Psi Chi is known for hosting the Fall Lab Fair, the new Psychology Winter Camp, and R’PSYC Undergraduate Research Conference, which are some of the ways we prepare our members to succeed in research, graduate school, and future careers.
If you want to make new friends with similar academic and professional interests, Psi Chi is the right place for you to find a safe and supportive community at UCR!
The scholarship of all Psi Chi members is valued. An official membership card and certificate are awarded to each member. Medals, honor cords, and stoles can be purchased to wear at graduation.
Dr. Hendley, a professor in the area of Psychology, is our faculty advisor. She provides many useful resources for students preparing for graduate school and exploring opportunities in psychology on campus.
Our Psi Chi chapter hosts many events to better equip students for success. Professors, graduate students, Clinical Psychologists, and guidance counselors from the Career Center represent some of the talented speakers who share their knowledge at Psi Chi events. In addition, we host numerous socials, volunteer events, and general meetings.', '“The purposes of Psi Chi shall be to encourage, stimulate, and maintain excellence in scholarship of the individual members in all fields, particularly in psychology, and to advance the science of psychology.”', 'Our general meetings are typically held every other week of the quarter. For more information on becoming a member and other frequently asked questions, please visit our website.
____________________________
