(70997, 'Psychology Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'As needed', 'As needed to address department and organization issues.', null, 'We, the members of this organization shall be the Psychology Graduate Student Association at UCR, established to facilitate intellectual exchange and provide a forum for addressing psychology graduate student concerns.', 'We, the members of this organization, shall be the Psychology Graduate Student Association of the University of California, Riverside, established to facilitate intellectual exchange and provide a forum for addressing psychology graduate student concerns.', 'psychgradreps@gmail.com', 'https://psychology.ucr.edu/graduate-study/current-graduate-students/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/pgsa'),
(71166, 'Queer & Trans People of Color', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'General meetings/events tend to be on Wednesdays. Check our Instagram @qtpoc.ucr for the most up-to-date information!', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Queer & Trans People of Color is an organization that brings together people from different intersections of our members'' lives and communities as queer & trans* people of color and allies.', 'The establishment of Queer & Trans People of Color Organization is rooted in the struggle against racism and prejudices prevalent in the Queer community. We are committed to activism-- to recognizing and highlighting not only the unique intersections of our identities, but also the social justice movements that fight the unique oppression and prejudice that QTPOC experience. We promote inclusivity by creating space for Queers of Color socially, politically, culturally and environmentally.', 'ucrqtpoc@gmail.com', null, 'https://instagram.com/qtpoc.ucr?igshid=8tos26988hy4', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/qtpoc'),
(71058, 'Queer Alliance', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Check our Instagram for the meeting day/time! We announce it for every quarter. The location is always the LGBT Resource Center (located at 245 Costo Hall)', 'Weekly', null, 'Queer Alliance aims to create inclusive spaces that empower the LGBTQIA+ community at UCR and youth of the surrounding area, and to promote the acceptance of diverse sexual and gender identities through advocacy and education', 'Welcome to Queer Alliance!
Our mission is to create inclusive, safe spaces on campus that empower UCR''s queer LGBTQIA+ community, and to promote the acceptance of diverse identities (relating to sexuality and gender) and intersectionalities through advocacy and education.
We organize large-scale queer events on campus that include:
The Coming Out Dance (a safe interactive space where people of all orientations and identities can mingle and let loose), The Coming Out Monologues (an educational and empowering performative program speaking on the experiences of UCR''s queer population), The Dragalicious Drag Ball (our largest program offering an evening of drag performance entertainment and a chance for student to participate), and Pride Prom (an outreach event geared towards creating a safe and inclusive version of Prom that queer youth in the surrounding area can enjoy and be themselves).
Members can engage either actively through the organization, planning, and execution of the listed events, or more passively by enjoying regular socials and outings with other members and queer people on campus.', 'qa.ucriverside@gmail.com', 'https://groupme.com/join_group/25306145/fZcpWQUO', 'https://www.instagram.com/qa_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/queeralliance'),
(158768, 'Queer Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'Fall quarter biweekly meetings, beginning November!', 'Every two weeks', null, 'This organization is a safe haven for queer and gender queer graduate students to connect, educate, and support one another throughout our graduate school journey.', 'QGSA is meant to represent a diverse community and promote inclusivity and equity within UCR. This organization is for queer and genderqueer identified graduate students to discuss campus concerns related to LGBTQIA2S+ issues, hang out, and ultimately foster a sense of community and activism!', 'qgsa.ucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/qgsa'),
(400894, 'Queer Leadership Council', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Biweekly on Tuesday from 4pm-5pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Queer Leadership Council (QLC) at UCR is dedicated to supporting and empowering LGBTQ+ organizations and individuals on campus. We provide essential resources, emergency relief, and advocacy', null, 'sedre001@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/qlc'),
(420733, 'Queer South Asian & South West Asian Student Org', 'Registered Student Organization', null, null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Queer South Asian and South-West Asian &amp; North African (QSSWANA) is focused on bringing a community together, allies included, where we can address the lived experiences of our Queer SSWANA students within our created safe space.', 'Our mission is to establish a safe and inclusive space while advocating for Queer SSWANA students who encounter social injustice, such as homophobia, racism, and any kind of discrimination. Those lived experiences must bring attention and be heard. Through our organization, we will ensure to share and learn from one another. As we grow bigger, we hope to work on projects that would support us to make a huge positive impact on campus. Anyone is welcome to join, allies included.', 'qsswana@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/qsswana.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/qsswana'),
(405780, 'Quranic Studies UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Monday 4-5pm', 'Weekly', null, 'A Quranic Studies Club focused on teaching Tajwid (Quranic recitation), Tafsir (interpretation), translation, and memorization in a supportive environment, fostering spiritual growth and deepening understanding of Quranic teachings.', 'The Quran Club is a learning group focused on fostering a deeper connection with the Quran. It offers participants the opportunity to learn proper Tajweed (Quranic recitation), understand the Tafsir (interpretation) of verses, explore translation for better comprehension, and work on memorization of Quranic passages. This supportive environment is designed to empower women in their spiritual growth and enhance their knowledge of Quranic teachings.', 'Quranicstudies@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/qs.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/quranicstudies'),
(400590, 'R'' Karters', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesday''s and Thursday''s from 8PM-10PM', 'Weekly', 'The Mario Kart Club is a space for Mario Kart lovers to come together and play Mario Kart. Meetings involve playing on one or two large servers as a group with the rest of the club. There is also the opportunity to win prizes via monthly and quarterly tournaments.', 'A safe space for Mario Kart lovers to come together and play Mario Kart.', 'The Mario Kart Club is a space for Mario Kart lovers to come together and play Mario Kart. Meetings involve playing on one or two large servers as a group with the rest of the club. There is also the opportunity to win prizes via monthly and quarterly tournaments.', 'ucrkarters@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rkarters'),
(293650, 'R''Brains and Behavior', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesday; 5pm-6pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'We are a Psychology Club! Our purpose is to establish resources, such as networking opportunities, educational advancement, and professional development, in addition creating a community for young professionals within the field of psychology.', 'R''Brains and Behavior is a student-led psychology club dedicated to creating an inclusive environment for anyone interested in psychology. We provide a space to explore diverse topics, engage in related activities, and connect with like-minded individuals. Our mission is to support members'' educational, professional, and personal growth by offering networking opportunities, career development, and resources. Through events with UCR staff and alumni, we aim to foster a strong community and help members discover and expand their focus within the field of psychology.', 'rbrainsandbehavior@gmail.com', 'https://rbrains.ucrhighlanders.org', 'http://instagram.com/rbrainsatucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rbrains'),
(303251, 'R''Cycle Co-op', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Wednesdays 10:00AM', 'Weekly', 'Participation is open to all UCR affiliated individuals: Undergraduate students, Graduate students, Staff and Faculty. Please go to our Instagram to get started with the club!
All club participants are welcome to attend the general meetings. Section meetings will be held for each of the three communities of members: Undergrads, Graduate students, and Staff/Faculty. These meetings include group rides, lunch hours, and more.
One of the ultimate goals of the R''Cycle Co-op is to secure a physical facility on campus where the UCR community can have access to:
Inexpensive second-hand replacement parts
Affordable used bikes', 'The R''Cycle Co-op is a student org focused on building up the cycling community at UCR. The goal of the Co-op is to promote Sustainability, Community, Safety Education and Training, and Advocacy for alternative transportation on campus.', 'The R''Cycle Co-op is a student org focused on building up the cycling community at UCR. The goal of the Co-op is to promote Sustainability, Community, Safety Education and Training, and Advocacy for alternative transportation on campus.
Participation is open to all UCR affiliated individuals: Undergraduate students, Graduate students, Staff and Faculty. Please go to our Instagram to get started with the club!
All club participants are welcome to attend the general meetings. Section meetings will be held for each of the three communities of members: Undergrads, Graduate students, and Staff/Faculty. These meetings include group rides, lunch hours, and more.
One of the ultimate goals of the R''Cycle Co-op is to secure a physical facility on campus where the UCR community can have access to:
Inexpensive second-hand replacement parts
Affordable used bikes
Discounted new parts
A library of loaner tools
Technical assistance and training
The R''Cycle Co-op is also invested in promoting the use of alternative transportation beyond the boundaries of UCR through advocacy at the local, state and federal level.
We hope that you will join our community to help make our campus and world a better place, one bike-ride at a time!', 'rcyclecoop@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/rcycle_coop/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rcycleco-op'),
(406666, 'R''LING', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesdays; 4-5pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'R''LING is a linguistics-focused club organization that offers various opportunities to network and collaborate with related departments, as well as formally discuss the studies of language and other related fields.', 'R''LING is a student led linguistics-focused organization that strives to offer and create meaningful opportunities for students interested in linguistics or its related fields. Through various panels, guest speakers and workshops, the organization provides academic guidance and community structure to foster students'' interests in the linguistics field. We hope to inform and educate students on the diversity within the study of linguistics and the various career opportunities it offers.', 'ucriverside.linguists@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/rling.ucr?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rlingucr'),
(164861, 'R''shorts', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Every other Wednesday at 6:30pm in Humanities 411', 'Every two weeks', 'R''Shorts is a filmmaking club that helps facilitate the development of different skills such as: screenwriting, videography and/or cinematography, directing, acting, postproduction, etc. This also includes the different practices (location scouting, acting rehearsals, etc.) involved in making a short film. Members will get the opportunity to exercise their creativity, hone their crafts, network, build their portfolios, gain exposure, and make new friends. Being surrounded by like-minded, passionate people allows members to create new content, be alerted to new production opportunities, and improve skills that open doors into careers within the filmmaking and content creation industries.', 'Film club at the University of California Riverside that allows students to develop and explore their creative skills through the film process.', 'R''Shorts is a filmmaking club that helps facilitate the development of different skills such as: screenwriting, videography and/or cinematography, directing, acting, postproduction, etc. This also includes the different practices (location scouting, acting rehearsals, etc.) involved in making a short film. Members will get the opportunity to exercise their creativity, hone their crafts, network, build their portfolios, gain exposure, and make new friends. Being surrounded by like-minded, passionate people allows members to create new content, be alerted to new production opportunities, and improve skills that open doors into careers within the filmmaking and content creation industries.', 'ucr.rshorts@gmail.com', 'https://ucrrshorts0.wixsite.com/rshorts', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr.rshorts/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rshorts'),
(104326, 'R''Stage Productions', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Tuesdays around 5-7pm', null, null, 'R''Stage Productions aims to showcase student work and provide a means for artistic collaboration between students. Student actors, directors, writers, stage managers, and designers of all majors are welcome.', 'R''Stage Productions is an organization dedicated to helping students of all majors create a theatrical production. Actors, directors, writers, stage managers, and designers can all find a home here. Students of all backgrounds are welcome to build new relationships and are provided with a means for artistic collaboration, as well as professional experience in the realm of theatre.', 'rstageproductionsucr@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/rstageucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/rstageucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rstage-productions'),
(385473, 'R''TimeinaFlash', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Fridays, 3-5pm.  Subject to change.', 'Every two weeks', 'The purpose of our club is to provide a welcoming environment for photographers, ranging from any skill type or medium. Film, Digital, and Phone photography is welcome. If you simply like photos, this is the club for you. We will learn not only the technical aspects needed to achieve certain looks but participate in biweekly challenges to practice the techniques. We hope to learn and grow together, and most importantly, have fun doing so!', 'A club for any photographer, of any skill level.  Whether you''re a beginner or expert, whether you shoot film or digital.  We are dedicated to helping photographers grasp the technical aspects of photography through the use of biweekly challenges and fun!', 'The purpose of our club is to provide a welcoming environment for photographers, ranging from any skill type or medium. Film, Digital, and Phone photography is welcome. If you simply like photos, this is the club for you. We will learn not only the technical aspects needed to achieve certain looks but participate in biweekly challenges to practice the techniques. We hope to learn and grow together, and most importantly, have fun doing so!', null, null, 'http://instagram.com/rtimeinaflash', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rtimeinaflash'),
(400223, 'Racquetball Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesdays and Thursdays 6:00pm-8:00pm. Join our Discord as throughout the semester we decide to hold more or less practices: https://discord.gg/ssaZRaT', 'Weekly', 'Our club’s all about building a welcoming racquetball community at UCR, where students can play, learn, and talk about the sport—whether you’re brand new or competitive. We run regular practices focused on improving skills, having fun, and enjoying friendly matches. Plus, we’re passionate about introducing racquetball to more people around campus and our community through events and outreach that invite everyone to discover and enjoy the game. Currently we boast about 30 members, and have players of all skill levels involved. Join our discord to learn more about when we hold our practices as our events may not up to date: https://discord.gg/wrSedXB.', 'UCR''s first dedicated Racquetball Club!

Open to everyone, whether you’re brand new to the sport, experienced on the court, or just curious about racquetball. Join us to play, learn, and connect—no experience needed!', 'Our club’s all about building a welcoming racquetball community at UCR, where students can play, learn, and talk about the sport—whether you’re brand new or competitive. We run regular practices focused on improving skills, having fun, and enjoying friendly matches. Plus, we’re passionate about introducing racquetball to more people around campus and our community through events and outreach that invite everyone to discover and enjoy the game. Currently we boast about 30 members, and have players of all skill levels involved. Join our discord to learn more about when we hold our practices as our events may not up to date: https://discord.gg/wrSedXB.', 'rbeoh001@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_racquetball/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/racquetballatucr'),
(430991, 'RAZA Assembly', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Raza Assembly de UCR is an organization that provides unity amongst all Raza organizations and promotes educational and cultural awareness within the campus Latinx community.', 'As RAZA Assembly de UCR, our purpose is to enhance communication and unity amongst the organizations comprising Latinx and the surrounding community. As well as promoting education and cultural awareness within the Latinx community. And support the enhancement
of the organizations represented within Raza Assembly.', 'razaassemblydeucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/raza_assembly'),
(402276, 'Real Estate Careers and Horizons', 'Registered Student Organization', null, null, 'Monthly', null, 'REACH is dedicated to helping students get educated about the different career opportunities in the real estate industry through mentorship &amp; training to acquire the skills necessary to break into the industry, whether an internship or full-time job.', null, 'reach.ucr@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/reach.ucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/reach1'),
(418587, 'redefineD at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Tuesday 7pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Through service, learning, and real-world experience, we aim to help marginalized populations redefine their lives while inspiring students.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization is to educate students about street medicine and the needs of underserved communities. By working closely with our parent organization, we provide members not only with knowledge but also with the opportunity to participate in hands-on fieldwork opportunities. Through service, learning, and real-world experience, we aim to help marginalized populations redefine their lives while inspiring students.', 'ucrredefined@gmail.com', 'redefined.ucrhighlanders.org', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/redefined-at-ucr'),
(82957, 'Residence Hall Association', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], 'Mondays at 9pm', 'Weekly', 'Residence Halls Association (RHA) is a student run organization that operates under Resident Life and Housing Services at UCR. RHA works closely with both of these departments to ensure that the greater needs and desires of the residents are heard and communicated by the organization to the respective department. We are the voice of the residents, and work in many areas to fulfill that responsibility. Most members describe RHA as the student govenment within the Residence Halls. Our goal is to make the residents’ stay here comfortable, fun, and memorable. Whether it is by hosting numerous social and educational events, granting residents their facility needs, or even lending a helping hand to the individual or other organizations, we are glad to do it. Joining RHA is easy. All you have to do is come to a RHA senate meeting that happens once a week in your residence hall. Just click on the Residence Halls tab above to find out when your RHA senate meetings is happening in your residence hall. We look foward to seeing you at our next meeting!', 'Residence Halls Association (RHA) is a student run organization that operates under Resident Life and Housing Services at UCR. RHA works closely with both of these departments to ensure that the greater needs and desires of the residents are heard.', 'Residence Halls Association (RHA) is a student run organization that operates under Resident Life and Housing Services at UCR. RHA works closely with both of these departments to ensure that the greater needs and desires of the residents are heard and communicated by the organization to the respective department. We are the voice of the residents, and work in many areas to fulfill that responsibility. Most members describe RHA as the student govenment within the Residence Halls. Our goal is to make the residents’ stay here comfortable, fun, and memorable. Whether it is by hosting numerous social and educational events, granting residents their facility needs, or even lending a helping hand to the individual or other organizations, we are glad to do it. Joining RHA is easy. All you have to do is come to a RHA senate meeting that happens once a week in your residence hall. Just click on the Residence Halls tab above to find out when your RHA senate meetings is happening in your residence hall. We look foward to seeing you at our next meeting!', 'rhaucr1954@gmail.com', 'https://ucrrha.com', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rha'),
(430886, 'Revolutionary Communists of America at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to organize a new generation of class fighters, educate students in Marxist theory, and build a revolutionary presence on campus.', null, 'kkrag002@ucr.edu', 'https://communistusa.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ie.communists/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rca_ucr'),
(420791, 'Rhythm Gaming Club @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'End of week afternoons.', 'Monthly', 'Our goal here at RGC@UCR is to create a welcoming community where players of all skill levels can connect, improve, and share their passion for rhythm gaming. We host casual meetups, tournaments, and arcade outings! Whether you’re starting out or chasing full combos, our club is the right place to hit buttons to the beat, make new rhythm gamer friends, and enjoy rhythm gaming together!
Make sure to join our discord to talk amongst fellow rhythm gamers, share your scores, and keep up with club updates such as tabling, arcade meetups, meetings, and game nights!
Discord: https://discord.gg/9AWWcMVnB9', 'Here at the RGC@UCR, our clubs purpose is to bring together and foster a community of students that enjoy rhythm games. Whether you’re a seasoned pro or a total beginner, our club welcomes everyone regardless of their rhythm game background.', 'We are the Rhythm Gaming Club @ UCR, a community for students, by students, who love rhythm games of all kinds! From classics such as Dance Dance Revolution and Pump It Up, to modern titles such as maimai, Sound Voltex and Chunithm, to non-arcade titles like osu! and Project Sekai, and many many more, there is something for you here.
Our goal here at RGC@UCR is to create a welcoming community where players of all skill levels can connect, improve, and share their passion for rhythm gaming. We host casual meetups, tournaments, and arcade outings! Whether you’re starting out or chasing full combos, our club is the right place to hit buttons to the beat, make new rhythm gamer friends, and enjoy rhythm gaming together!
Make sure to join our discord to talk amongst fellow rhythm gamers, share your scores, and keep up with club updates such as tabling, arcade meetups, meetings, and game nights!
Discord: https://discord.gg/9AWWcMVnB9', 'ucrrgc@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rgcatucr'),
(346547, 'Rides @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'Rides @ UCR is a car club social organization that brings together all those interested in the modification, appreciation, and passion for vehicles. Everyone is welcome to our events whether you have a vehicle or not!', 'Rides@UCR is a car club & social organization that unites all those interested in the modification and passion for vehicles and driving. Everyone is welcome to our meets, even if you don''t own a vehicle yourself. For the latest information on our events, check our Instagram @ridesucr.', 'ridesucr@gmail.com', null, 'http://www.instagram.com/ridesucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ridesatucr'),
(180110, 'Riverside Bhangra', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], null, 'Weekly', 'We are a diverse cultural dance team that is dedicated to Bhangra, a folk dance originating from Punjab. We love to dance, expand our team, meet new people, compete, and hold workshops.', 'We are a diverse cultural dance team that is dedicated to Bhangra, a folk dance originating from Punjab. We love to dance, expand our team, meet new people, compete, and hold workshops.', 'We are a diverse cultural dance team that is dedicated to Bhangra, a folk dance originating from Punjab. We love to dance, expand our team, meet new people, compete, and hold workshops.', 'riversidebhangra@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/rside_bhangra_/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/riversidebhangra'),
(70836, 'Riverside Free Clinic at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Every other Wednesday at 4:30 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Student Run Health Clinic began in 2005, growing from the collaborative concerns of students and doctors disturbed by the number of Riverside locals without basic healthcare.', 'At RFC, we strive to provide free interdisciplinary health and wellness care to the underserved population of the Inland Empire while also providing an effective training environment for future healthcare professionals and leaders dedicated to serving the Inland Empire. Our undergraduate volunteers work with medical students, various healthcare professionals from numerous programs & universities, and faculty from the UCR School of Medicine to provide basic healthcare to the underserved population of Riverside.
This group was formally known as the Student Run Health Clinic and is now known as the Riverside Free Clinic.
Applications come out in the Spring, so if you''re interested, please visit our website in May!', 'clinicmonitor@riversidesrhc.com', 'http://riversidefreeclinic.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrrfc/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rfc'),
(222300, 'Riverside Giddhe di Raunak', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Days and times vary.', 'Weekly', 'Riverside Giddhe Di Raunak is a Punjabi folk dance team focused on providing people the chance to experience the rich culture of Punjab. We provide competitive and non-competitive performance opportunities. No experience is necessary (everyone is welcome) and the basics of giddha will be taught. We hold weekly practices and workshops. Please contact us if you are interested in attending a practice or joining the team! RGDR is a family and not just a team!', 'Riverside Giddhe di Raunak is focused on providing people the chance to experience the rich culture of Punjab through the region''s traditional folk dance called Giddha. The various techniques and forms used in Giddha will be taught and performed.', 'Riverside Giddhe Di Raunak is a Punjabi folk dance team focused on providing people the chance to experience the rich culture of Punjab. We provide competitive and non-competitive performance opportunities. No experience is necessary (everyone is welcome) and the basics of giddha will be taught. We hold weekly practices and workshops. Please contact us if you are interested in attending a practice or joining the team! RGDR is a family and not just a team!', 'giddhaucr@gmail.com', null, 'http://instagram.com/giddhaucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/giddhaatucr'),
(71151, 'Riverside Surging Dragons Dragon Boat Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Saturdays and Sundays at 8:30 am at lot 15.', 'Weekly', null, 'Our clubs aims to help people make friends at UCR through the sport of dragonboat!', 'Our family''s motto is to instill discipline, hardwork, passion, and focus while stimulating the growth of our hearts and minds. More than a group of paddlers - we strive to push beyond our limits and be the best that we can be.
You do not need to have prior experience nor any fitness experience, we will help you grow! This is a great place to find friends and to have an unforgettable experience.', 'rsd.dragonboat@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/rsd_dragonboat', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rsd'),
(234322, 'Riverside X Dance', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Mondays, 7:00-9:00pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Riverside x Dance is a beginner-friendly K-pop dance team at UCR. With workshops, socials, and performances, RxD is dedicated to embracing a community that’s bringing back fun to 3rd gen kpop. Bringing back K-pop in style, The RxD Team ♡ ⋆.˚ ᡣ𐭩 .𖥔˚', 'Riverside x Dance is a beginner-friendly K-pop dance team at UCR. With workshops, socials, and performances, RxD is dedicated to embracing a community that’s bringing back fun to kpop. With rolling auditions per quarter, we welcome all students to apply and join the team! Bringing back K-pop in style, The RxD Team ♡ ⋆.˚ ᡣ𐭩 .𖥔˚', 'riversidexdance@gmail.com', 'https://riversidexdance.carrd.co', 'https://www.instagram.com/rxducr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rxd'),
(71019, 'Rugby Football Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesday and Thursday, 7:00 to 9:00 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose of this organization is to teach and improve rugby skills to players, promote team spirit through competitive games with other rugby clubs, and provide athletic conditioning.', 'The purpose of this organization is to teach and improve rugby skills to players, promote team spirit through competitive games with other rugby clubs, provide athletic conditioning, enact positive sportsmanship on and off the field, and to recognize and promote the national growth and interest of students'' rugby.
If interested in playing, look us up on our Instagram account and send us a text with any questions you may have!
(@ucr_rugby)', 'Rbozz002@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_rugby', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rfcatucr'),
(70893, 'Running Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], '5:00pm Fall & Spring Quarter, 4:00pm Winter Quarter outside the SRC', 'Monday through Friday every week', 'We’re a casual, social, running club based at UCR, open to anyone regardless of experience level! Our goal is to provide a friendly, welcoming, and safe environment for everyone. We host casual practices on tested routes around the surrounding area, offer opportunities to participate in competitive races throughout the year, and organize social events/collaborations. Our Runs are held Monday through Friday at 5 PM (or 4 PM during winter daylight savings) outside the SRC at the tables near the north entrance. Join us whenever you can—we’d love to see you often!
If you''d like to learn more about the club or keep up to date with our events, follow us @runningclubatucr on Instagram.
OR check out our Discord or our email list by clicking join from this page.
Our website: runningclubatucr.wordpress.com', 'We’re a casual, social, running club based at UCR, open to anyone regardless of experience level! Providing a friendly, welcoming, and safe environment for everyone. Join us outside the SRC at 5pm Mon-Fri, no commitment required!', 'We’re a casual, social, running club based at UCR, open to anyone regardless of experience level! Our goal is to provide a friendly, welcoming, and safe environment for everyone. We host casual practices on tested routes around the surrounding area, offer opportunities to participate in competitive races throughout the year, and organize social events/collaborations. Our Runs are held Monday through Friday at 5 PM (or 4 PM during winter daylight savings) outside the SRC at the tables near the north entrance. Join us whenever you can—we’d love to see you often!
If you''d like to learn more about the club or keep up to date with our events, follow us @runningclubatucr on Instagram.
OR check out our Discord or our email list by clicking join from this page.
Our website: runningclubatucr.wordpress.com', 'runningclubatucr@gmail.com', 'http://runningclubatucr.wordpress.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/runningclubatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/runningclubatucr'),
(401849, 'Russian-Speaking Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], null, 'Every other week and on traditional holidays.', null, 'The Russian-Speaking Student Association is founded on a commitment to celebrating, understanding, and sharing the Russian Language among the members of the post-Soviet Diaspora and language learners and enthusiasts.', null, 'rssaatucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/rssa.ucr?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rssa'),
(71086, 'Sakura-bu', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Creatr Lab @Orbach Library 5pm-6:30pm (3/27/25-6/6/25)', 'Weekly', null, 'Japanese Culture, Language Education, and Exchange Organization', 'Purpose
Sakura-bu is an organization at UCR where domestic and international students from Japan exchange cultural ideas and languages.
Aim
Sakura-bu aims to welcome incoming exchange students from Japan, connecting them with UCR students.
Proposal
Sakura-bu proposes allowing international students to make new friends and precious memories.
Environment
Sakura-bu fosters an everlasting acquisition of Japanese culture and language for UCR students.
Intention
Sakura-bu intends to bring students from a diverse subset of backgrounds to immerse themselves in different cultures.
Contact
- Instagram
- Discord
- Facebook
- Twitter', 'sakurabu300@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/sakurabu_ucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sakura-bu'),
(431116, 'Sandals International Table', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Saturdays at 3:30pm', 'Weekly', 'connected students feel known, supported, and at home during their time at UCR. Members and
community partners gather regularly to build cross-cultural relationships, practice everyday
conversational skills, and create a consistent, welcoming space for students far from home.', 'The purpose of this organization is to create a welcoming table where international students and scholars at UCR can build genuine friendships with members of the surrounding community.', 'The purpose of this organization is to create a welcoming table where international students and
scholars at UCR can build genuine friendships with members of the surrounding community. SIT
is hosted in partnership with Sandals Church''s Hunter Park campus, extending an established
community hospitality ministry to UCR''s international student population.
Through shared meals, conversation, and cultural exchange, SIT exists to help internationally
connected students feel known, supported, and at home during their time at UCR. Members and
community partners gather regularly to build cross-cultural relationships, practice everyday
conversational skills, and create a consistent, welcoming space for students far from home.', 'bguer033@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sandalschurchcom'),
(351363, 'School of Business Leadership Council at UC Riverside', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], null, null, null, 'To increase collaboration among School of Business student organizations and the school administration to deliver excellence to the UCR School of Business community.', 'The School of Business Leadership Council is dedicated to establishing a council of UCR School of Business student leaders to increase collaboration and facilitate resources among School of Business student members, student
organizations, and faculty to deliver excellence to the community.', 'sblcucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/sblcucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sblc'),
(166762, 'School of Medicine Medical Student Council', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Once/month after the monthly GSA meeting', 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to establish an association in full support of representing the School of Medicine student body and interest group organizations.', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to establish an association in full support of representing the School of Medicine student body and interest group organizations, while ensuring adequate funds to be allocated upon application submission/review for student activities, research, presentation, conference or academic enrichment opportunities for the M.D. Students of the School of Medicine. The UCR SOM MSC will ensure complete transparency, easy communication, and fair allocation of funds and resources to the M.D. student body.', 'ecasi005@medsch.ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sommsc'),
(419620, 'School on Wheels at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'School on Wheels is a nonprofit organization that provides free one-on-one tutoring, mentorship, and academic support to children experiencing homelessness with the mission of helping these students succeed despite the challenges of housing insecurity.', null, 'ucrsow@gmail.com', 'https://schoolonwheels.org/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrsow'),
(293992, 'SciComm @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'First Tuesday of the month', 'Monthly', 'We practice creative and community-building science communication to the general public through events and multimedia projects. Additionally, we organize an annual workshops about the practice of science communication.', 'We practice creative communication of science to the general public through events and multimedia projects. Additionally, we organize an annual workshop about the practice of science communication.', 'We practice creative and community-building science communication to the general public through events and multimedia projects. Additionally, we organize an annual workshops about the practice of science communication.', 'scicommucr@gmail.com', 'http://scicommucr.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/scicommucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/scicommucr'),
(196635, 'Science Policy Graduate Student Association', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], null, 'Monthly', 'The Science Policy GSA bridges the gap between scientists and the general public, allowing STEM students to see their importance in the policy process. We practice communication skills, advocate for science, promote scientific collaboration, and create opportunities
for students to connect with elected officials. We also educate students on the importance of the political process with respect to science and technology policy. We strive to allow students to see that their voice, vote, and expertise matter in the community,
both local and national, and not just in academia.
We are the sister organization to the Science to Policy Program. To find out more visit s2p.ucr.edu', 'This organization is for all students interested in STEM''s role in policy, bettering scientific communication, and for connecting with local representatives.', 'The Science Policy GSA bridges the gap between scientists and the general public, allowing STEM students to see their importance in the policy process. We practice communication skills, advocate for science, promote scientific collaboration, and create opportunities
for students to connect with elected officials. We also educate students on the importance of the political process with respect to science and technology policy. We strive to allow students to see that their voice, vote, and expertise matter in the community,
both local and national, and not just in academia.
We are the sister organization to the Science to Policy Program. To find out more visit s2p.ucr.edu', 's2p@ucr.edu', 'http://s2p.ucr.edu', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrs2p/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sciencepolicy'),
(385313, 'Scotty''s Final Call', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Campus Department','Department Affiliated Organization','Department Program']::text[], null, null, null, 'Stay in the loop about free well-being events on campus! You''ll get updates about programs that offer free food and health-promoting supplies. Plus, we’ll let you know when there''s leftover food available for pickup

Easy Steps: “SIGN IN” and select “', 'Stay connected to free well-being events, resources, and food opportunities across campus! This email service is open to all UCR students, staff, and faculty.
By joining, you’ll receive real-time email alerts about:
Well-being events offering free resources: Learn about events hosted or promoted by The Well, Basic Needs, and other campus departments where participants may receive free food or health-promoting supplies. Participation in the event or activity is required, so we kindly ask that attendees not stop by only to pick up items.
Leftover food available on campus: Receive alerts when food is left over from campus events or conferences and is available for pickup. These opportunities are offered on a first-come, first-served basis.
Each email will include important details, such as the location, availability, participation expectations, and pickup instructions.
Ready to join? Select “SIGN IN,” then “JOIN” to subscribe.
If you no longer wish to receive these emails, you may unsubscribe at any time using the unsubscribe option provided. Due to the large number of subscribers, we’re unable to process individual unsubscribe requests, but you can easily manage your subscription directly.', 'thewell@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/hws'),
(430877, 'Scotty''s Launch Squad', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to open more opportunities for students to engage in rocketry and aerospace learning, to gain experience with STEM, and to participate in yearly competitions while creating lasting connections.', 'Our team is dedicated to extending more opportunities for rocketry and aerospace learning at the University of California, Riverside. We will do this by developing a rocket that meets the NASA Student Launch Program 2026-2027 requirements while sharing industry experience and engaging with passionate students, experts, and rocket enthusiasts.', 'scottyslaunchsquad@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/scottyslaunchsquad/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sls_rocketry'),
(104148, 'Secret Swords and Sorcery Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Look at our description for meeting information.', 'Twice, weekly.', 'This is a group for people who want to play roleplaying games, like Dungeons and Dragons, Shadowrun, Pathfinder, and Warhammer 40k. Our club provides a space for both new and veteran players to come together and group up for sessions, and offers a place to exchange new and creative ideas for the tabletop community. For more information, feel free to email our president, Kieran Tsim, at ''ktsim001@ucr.edu''. If you don''t receive a response in 8 hours, feel free to send another.
Meeting Times Spring 2026: 6:00pm at HUB 260 Tuesdays and Fridays. Check the club''s discord for updates on each quarter.
https://discord.gg/zduVcpz
Currently, the club offers existing games of Dungeons and Dragons 5th Edition, Middle Earth Roleplaying, Shadowrun, World/Chronicles of Darkness (Vampire the Masquerade/Requiem, Werewolf the Apocalypse/Forsaken, Mage the Ascension/Awakening, etc) and the Warhammer 40k War-game (Deathwatch and More). We''re always looking to try new systems amidst our various groups, so if you''ve got a fun and interesting idea and the desire to run or play in a game, feel free to come on by and join us!', 'The purpose of this group is to organize tabletop and live role playing games such as D&D.

As of Spring 2024, 
Meetings Times: 6:00pm to 10:00pm Tuesdays and Fridays
Place: Hub 265

Check out our Discord for more info!
 https://discord.gg/53Sp6Qz', 'This is a group for people who want to play roleplaying games, like Dungeons and Dragons, Shadowrun, Pathfinder, and Warhammer 40k. Our club provides a space for both new and veteran players to come together and group up for sessions, and offers a place to exchange new and creative ideas for the tabletop community. For more information, feel free to email our president, Kieran Tsim, at ''ktsim001@ucr.edu''. If you don''t receive a response in 8 hours, feel free to send another.
Meeting Times Spring 2026: 6:00pm at HUB 260 Tuesdays and Fridays. Check the club''s discord for updates on each quarter.
https://discord.gg/zduVcpz
Currently, the club offers existing games of Dungeons and Dragons 5th Edition, Middle Earth Roleplaying, Shadowrun, World/Chronicles of Darkness (Vampire the Masquerade/Requiem, Werewolf the Apocalypse/Forsaken, Mage the Ascension/Awakening, etc) and the Warhammer 40k War-game (Deathwatch and More). We''re always looking to try new systems amidst our various groups, so if you''ve got a fun and interesting idea and the desire to run or play in a game, feel free to come on by and join us!', 'ktsim001@ucr.edu', 'https://discord.gg/HG84rdQ', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_s4/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ssandss'),
(71005, 'Senryu Taiko', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Mondays and Wednesdays 6:30-9:00 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'Self-taught and self-sustained, Senryu Taiko continues the tradition of kumidaiko by writing music together, teaching incoming members, and forming ties with other collegiate taiko groups across the nation.', 'Making noise since 1998, Senryu Taiko is one of the earliest intercollegiate taiko groups to ever form in the United States. Self-taught and self-sustained, Senryu Taiko continues the tradition of kumidaiko by writing music together, teaching incoming members, and forming ties with other collegiate taiko groups across the nation.', 'senryutaiko@gmail.com', 'https://senryutaiko.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/senryutaiko/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/senryutaiko'),
(384955, 'She Means Business', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Thursday nights', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose is to principles for the professional advancement of its members, stress the principles of equality and respectability for all members, and provide a forum for the interchange between members of this organization and other UCR students.', 'The purpose of this Organization is to provide an effective, cohesive forum to educate, promote, and uphold the principles, ideals, and precepts of She Means Business, an undergraduate-focused women in business organization. It shall promote the principles for the professional advancement of its members; stress the principles of equality and respectability for all members; provide a forum for the interchange between members of this organization and the other members of other UCR organizations; and develop an understanding of professional work ethic, critical thinking, general professionalism among its members.', 'ftong003@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/shemeansbusiness'),
(71138, 'Sigma Gamma Rho Sorority Inc.- Xi Rho Chapter', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Sigma Gamma Rho Sorority''s aim is to enhance the quality of life within the community. Public service, leadership development and education of youth are the hallmark of the organizations, programs and activities.', 'Sigma Gamma Rho Sorority''s aim is to enhance the quality of life within the community. Public service, leadership development and education of youth are the hallmark of the organizations, programs and activities. Sigma Gamma Rho addresses concerns that impact society educationally, civically, and economically. Soaring To Greater Heights Of Attainment Around The World, Sigma Gamma Rho Sorority, Inc., as a leading national service organization, has met the challenges of the day and continues to grow through Sisterhood, Scholarship and Service. Look for updates on our facebook page and our instagram page @xirhopoodles', 'ucrsgrho@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/xirhopoodles/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sgrho'),
(70865, 'Sigma Kappa Sorority', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], 'Monday, 8pm', 'Weekly', null, 'The women of Sigma Kappa strive to trust and empower our sisterhood to achieve success in unity, learning, and involvement. We exercise the rights of good citizens and the support of worthwhile civic, social, and philanthropic projects.', 'Consistent with our Founders’ thoughts in 1874, our primary purpose is to create an environment for our members in which lasting friendships and our values of sisterhood emanate all aspects of our organization. We encourage an atmosphere which will foster high ideals of friendship among college women, promote their educational and cultural interests, create in them a true sense of social responsibility and develop in them high qualities of character.', 'tesigmakappapresident@gmail.com', 'http://ucr.sigmakappa.org/', 'http://www.instagram.com/ucrsigmakappa', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sigmakappasorority'),
(70858, 'Sigma Pi Alpha Sorority, Inc.', 'Fraternities and Sororities', array['Fraternity/Sorority']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'To create a close network of Latinas who want to make a difference in their community. We address the academic, cultural, communal and social needs of our members. We are Chicana/Latina based but we do consider ourselves to be multicultural.', 'Sigma Pi Alpha Sorority was founded on May 2nd, 1996 by nine women at the University of California, Berkeley. They found the need to create a close network of Latinas who wanted to make a difference in their community by beginning with themselves. Beta chapter, at UC Riverside has been making strives on campus since June 2001. Although we use Greek letters, we are not affiliated with the Greek system. The Greek letters have been selected by our founding mothers to symbolize our Chicana/Latina heritage by spelling Ella, meaning she/her in the Spanish language. The sorority is Chicana/Latina based but we do consider ourselves to be multicultural. We have three pillars that we pride ourselves on. They are campus involvement, community service, and sisterhood. Lastly, if you are interested in joining, we would like you to know that we do not rush! We have a motto that says “you choose us, we don’t choose you!”', 'betachapterpresident01@gmail.com', 'http://www.sigmapialpha.org/', 'http://www.instagram.com/beta_ellas', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ellas'),
(386311, 'Sikh Collegiate Federation', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Tuesdays 8:30-9:30pm', 'will meet every Tuesdays from 8:30-9:30pm in the HUB room 367. If any meetings postponed those updates can be found on our instagram page or groupme.', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to forge a Gurmat-inspired generation through creative leadership development, community organizing, and social activism. Our mission is to build a Sikh political campus voice by strengthening the power of Sikhs.', null, 'ucr@jakara.org', 'https://www.jakara.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/scf.ucr?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/scf'),
(74688, 'Sikh Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Every Thursday at 6 PM unless specified otherwise (times may change every quarter depending on scheduling, check instagram)', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The goal of our organization is to create a safe and empowering space for Sikh Students at UCR by hosting various community-building events, discussion nights to address social issues affecting our community, and tabling events to connect with our peers.', 'Waheguru Ji Ka Khalsa, Waheguru Ji Ki Fateh.
The Sikh Student Association (SSA) at University of California, Riverside (UCR) is an organization to create a safe and empowering space for Sikh and non-Sikh Students at UCR. We get together for sangat (company), seva (selfless service), simran (meditation) and academics. The Sikh Student Association at UCR welcomes all students from various backgrounds and makes a positive impact on its members that lasts a life time.', 'ssa.ucriverside@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ssa_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrssa'),
(405091, 'Sisters Affirming our Social-cultural Identities', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Fridays, 2 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose of this organization shall be to provide a safe space for black women. S.A.S.I. aspires to do this through programming, outreach, meetings, events, and any other means to ensure the protection of black women on campus.', 'Sisters Affirming our Social-Cultural Identities (S.A.S.I.) was established as a cultural enrichment and advocacy group driven towards the advancement of Black women everywhere. S.A.S.I. is intended to center those who identify as Black women and address their unique intersectional oppressions. We are here to empower, support and advocate on behalf of Black women across the African diaspora, spiritually and emotionally, mentally and physically.
On the campus of University of California, Riverside, S.A.S.I. will serve as an organization that seeks to encourage women to work towards their own personal self-development by providing a healthy space that promotes vulnerability and growth. S.A.S.I. will use its platform to discuss, dissect issues that are relevant and directly affect women of color, black women and the black community overall.
S.A.S.I. is an organization that is intended for the growth of women of color. We will stand in alliance and solidarity with our male counterparts. We will work to strengthen and foster a healthy relationship within our community amongst the men and women on this campus.', 'ucriversidesasi@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr.sasi/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sasiatucr'),
(368821, 'SKY Campus', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Meetings are generally every other Thursday from 4-5pm', 'Every two weeks', 'Our goal is to create a space where students can have fun and meet new people while experimenting with meditation and breathwork as ways to increase energy levels and focus while reducing stress.', 'There are many different activities people engage in to relieve stress, like art, spending time in nature, etc. The purpose of SKY is to create a community on campus where people can experiment with meditation and breathwork as forms of stress reduction.', 'Our goal is to create a space where students can have fun and meet new people while experimenting with meditation and breathwork as ways to increase energy levels and focus while reducing stress.', 'jsama031@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/skyatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sky'),
(405730, 'Smile Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Thursday at 7 PM', 'Weekly', 'Smile Society is a student-led organization that brings together individuals passionate about health equity, with a specific focus on oral health. Our activities are centered around education, advocacy, and fundraising. We educate members and the broader community about the significance of oral health, advocate for increased awareness and better hygiene practices, and organize fundraising events to support non-profits and NGOs that provide dental supplies and educational programs to underprivileged communities.', 'Smile Society promotes oral health through education, advocacy, and fundraising, supporting underprivileged communities with dental supplies and hygiene awareness.', 'Smile Society is a student-led organization that brings together individuals passionate about health equity, with a specific focus on oral health. Our activities are centered around education, advocacy, and fundraising. We educate members and the broader community about the significance of oral health, advocate for increased awareness and better hygiene practices, and organize fundraising events to support non-profits and NGOs that provide dental supplies and educational programs to underprivileged communities.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrsmilesociety?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/smilesociety'),
(300540, 'Society for Anthropological Students', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'We meet once weekly, depending on member availability.', 'Weekly', null, 'We aim to create a space for those who have a passion for any of the subfields of Anthropology. We provide any and all necessary resources at our disposal for our community and strive to promote anthropological knowledge.', 'We aim to create a space for those who have a passion for any subfield of Anthropology. We provide any and all necessary resources at our disposal for our community. This can be through hosting workshops, sharing opportunities and resources, and working alongside the Anthropology Department.
To be involved, please use our HOME PAGE to follow our socials and join our Discord for more updates on all things SAUS.', 'ucr.anthropology@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/ucrsaus', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrsaus/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/saus'),
(425225, 'Society of Cosmetic Chemists', 'Registered Student Organization', null, null, 'Weekly', null, 'The Cosmetic Chemist Society supports students interested in cosmetic chemistry and medicine by exploring the intersection of chemistry, beauty, and biology through workshops, speakers, and hands-on-learning that prepares members for their professions.', 'The Society of Cosmetic Chemists is a student-run, career-focused organization established in 2026 that aims to support students interested in the cosmetic chemist profession, medicine, and/or both with exposure to the field(s) formulation workshops, guest-speakers, and interactive socials to make meaningful connections. SCC aims to help interested students broaden their general related knowledge, connect with industry professionals to gain insight into the field(s), and learn about common chemical ingredients and their interactions in personal care products.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/scc_ucr'),
(71081, 'Society of Hispanic Professional Engineers', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesday bi-weekly, even weeks, 5:00PM-6:00PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'We obtain excellence through integrity, empowerment, achievement, diversity, and continuous improvement. We are the leading social-technical organization whose primary function is to enhance and achieve the potential of Hispanics in STEM.', 'We are brought together by heritage, social responsibility and desire to improve the equality of all people through the use of science and technology. We value excellence in education, professional pursuits, and leadership. We obtain excellence through integrity, empowerment, achievement, diversity, and continuous improvement. SHPE is a national organization whose primary function is to cultivate the potential of the Hispanic community through technology, engineering, math, and science. We will fulfill our mission by increasing educational opportunities, promoting professional and personal growth, and reinforcing our reputation as a vital Hispanic organization.
To learn more, follow us on Instagram @shpeucr and join our discord at https://discord.gg/5EXaCJz for updates.', 'shpe.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://shpeucr.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/shpeucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/shpe'),
(71135, 'Society of Women Engineers', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Friday 2-3pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'SWE at UCR is a professional engineering organization specializing in professional and academic development, increasing the female presence in BCOE, and outreach opportunities by encouraging young students to pursue STEM fields.', 'SWE at UCR is a professional engineering organization specializing in professional and academic development, open to all genders, and outreach opportunities by encouraging young students to pursue STEM fields. We also frequently collaborate with other engineering organizations to help expand students'' professional networks. Three of our larger annual events are as follows:
Bourns Science and Engineering Day is the largest engineering outreach event at UCR. This past year, over 2500 children, parents, and teachers registered to participate in an all-day event with a distinguished keynote speaker, tours of the college, and exciting, interactive STEM-related activities/experiments showing students and their parents the importance of math and science.
Evening With Industry is a professional development event where company representatives and recruiters dine with students to share their experiences, provide industry insight, and discuss possible job/internship opportunities.
Research Networking Night is an academic development event where distinguished engineering professors and graduate students dine with students to discuss their research, open undergraduate research positions, and their experiences.
If you have any questions, please feel free to contact us, and we will be happy to provide you with more information!
Facebook Group: www.facebook.com/groups/5046061607
Instagram: swe.ucr', 'swe.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://ucrswe.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/swe.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/swe'),
(70864, 'Sociology Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Tuesday, late afternoon/early evening', 'Monthly', null, 'The mission of the SGSA is to serve as a resource and aid for the successful development of graduate students within the sociology department at UCR.', 'The mission of the SGSA is to serve as a resource and aid for the successful development of graduate students within the sociology department at UCR. SGSA seeks to accomplish this mission by making students aware of the different facets of the sociological discipline and through active involvement in the educational experience of students in our department. By bringing together individuals from different backgrounds, experiences and values, who share a commitment to serve their society, SGSA serves as a learning experience that challenges students to continuously respond to a basic underlying question: How can we as individuals and scholars contribute to a better understanding of our society?', 'tcohe008@ucr.edu, shami032@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sgsa'),
(419624, 'Somethin'' Sweet', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Weeks 1,3,5, and 7 ~ Friday, 6-7 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Somethin'' Sweet at UCR offers current students to be able to learn how to bake while creating connections with other members that will be cherished. It focuses on spreading the love and joy that comes with baking.', null, 'smthnsweetucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/smthnsweet'),
(71084, 'SOON Movement Global', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Tuesday 8:00 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose of SOON Movement Global is to fulfill the Great Commission at UCR and to all parts of the world.', 'The purpose of SOON Movement Global is to help fulfill the Great Commission at UCR and to all parts of the world. Our vision is for everyone in UCR to know at least one person who truly follows Christ. We want to share the good news of Jesus Christ to our community and campus and build a community of passionate followers of Christ.', 'llee153@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/sm.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/soonmovementglobal'),
(139291, 'South Asian Federation - SAF', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Depends on the quarter', 'Weekly Board Meetings + 3-5 General Membership Events per quarter', null, 'The purpose of South Asian Federation is to culturally, socially, and philanthropically unite the South Asian student population at UC Riverside. We aim to be safe space for all those who identify as South Asian, in hopes to create a stronger community.', 'The purpose of South Asian Federation is to culturally, socially, and philanthropically unite the South Asian student population at UC Riverside. We aim to be safe space for all those who identify as South Asian, in hopes to create a stronger community. We hope to one day have a South Asian Costo Hall center to help our community feel more represented here. We are mainly socially and culturally oriented, striving to have the South Asian student population celebrate the many different cultures represented through festivals and inclusive religious events. Additionally we are philanthropically associated as well, providing resources and opportunities for students here on campus year round.', 'safucr@gmail.com', 'http://ucrsaf.com', 'http://instagram.com/ucrsaf', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/saf'),
(415000, 'South Asian InterVarsity', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Spiritual/Religious/Atheist']::text[], 'Tuesday 7-10 p.m., Thursday 6-8 p.m.', 'Weekly', null, 'SAIV is about building a joyful and authentic community for students of South Asian background to encounter Jesus, and empowering them to boldly take risks for the Gospel on every corner of campus and beyond.', 'SAIV is about building a joyful and authentic community for students of South Asian background to encounter Jesus, and empowering them to boldly take risks for the Gospel on every corner of campus and beyond.', 'ucrsaivoffical@ucr.edu', 'https://linktr.ee/ucr_saiv', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr.saiv', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucr_saiv'),
(218605, 'Southeast Asian Studies Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'Thursday/Friday (10:00am-12:00nn)', 'Once every quarter, during bi-monthly events, and whenever there is a need to convene as an organization.', null, 'SEASGRAD is an association of graduate students affiliated with the Southeast Asian Studies program (SEATRiP) at UC Riverside. Our mission is to build an inclusive, empowered and professional community of scholars in Southeast Asian Studies.', 'The Southeast Asian Studies Graduate Student Association (SEASGRAD) is an association of MA and PhD students affiliated with UC Riverside’s Southeast Asian Studies Program, SEATRiP (Southeast Asia: Text, Ritual and Performance.) SEATRiP brings together faculty and students who share an interest in the arts and humanities and are actively engaged with the languages and expressive cultures of Southeast Asia. Work within SEATRiP addresses regionally-specific texts, rituals and performances across time and space. The interdisciplinary program was founded in 2002 by scholars in the Ethnomusicology, Anthropology, and Comparative Literatures and Languages departments.
SEASGRAD’s mission is to build an inclusive, empowered and professional community of scholars in Southeast Asian Studies.
This is an interdisciplinary group comprised of members enrolled in Master and Doctoral programs at UCR who are also associated with the SEATRiP M.A. and SEATRiP Designated Emphasis programs, or otherwise affiliated with SEATRiP and Southeast Asian Studies generally. The purposes of SEASGRAD shall be:
-We contribute to scholarship on Southeast Asia, its people, and its diasporas.
-We promote interdisciplinary dialogues among scholars of Southeast Asian studies.
-We nurture communication between our graduate students, faculty members, and undergraduate students.
-We gather and disperse integral funding and educational information.
-We seek to heighten university and public awareness of the program of Southeast Asian Studies at UCR through events and outreach projects, such as our annual conference.', null, 'https://seasgrad.ucr.edu/', 'https://www.instagram.com/seasgraducr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/seasgrad'),
(425113, 'Special Olympics - UC Riverside Chapter', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'This is UCR''s campus-based club of the Special Olympics program. Our goal is to connect college students and community members with Special Olympics athletes to create an inclusive community. Our focus is on increasing inclusion and campus impact!', 'We are a campus-based club of the Special Olympics program here at UC Riverside.
Our goal is to connect college students with Special Olympics athletes to create an inclusive community.
Club focus:
Inclusion: athletes are teammates, and we all work together
Continuity: consistent engagement with athletes and dedication to volunteering
Campus impact: Educate and involve the college community', 'ucrspecialolympics@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrspecialolympics'),
(420278, 'Sport Medicine Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Biweekly Thursdays', 'Monthly', null, 'Our mission is to educate students on the fundamentals of sports medicine, injury prevention, rehabilitation, and performance optimization through workshops, guest speakers, and volunteer opportunities.', null, null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sportsmedclub'),
(222269, 'STAGE: Chinese Performing Arts Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Weekdays at 8:00pm', 'Weekly', null, 'STAGE is an organization that students could learn about Chinese performing arts such as Chinese drama.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to let more students get to learn about Chinese performing arts such as Chinese drama. STAGE would conduct at least one Chinese play in an academic year. STAGE gives students chances to be involved at school. It also provides opportunities for students to know more about Chinese culture. STAGE is the first Chinese drama club at UCR. It enriches students’ lives and offers more opportunities to express students’ talents. It is also helpful to enhance intercultural communication on campus.', 'qshao008@ucr.edu', null, 'https://instagram.com/stage_ucr?igshid=da084bhso3za', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/stage'),
(379591, 'Star Wars Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'We hold our general meetings/lightsaber trainings every other week. Check out our Instagram (@starwarsucr) for more information!', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to spread the Star Wars fan base across campus and to provide a school-affiliated Star Wars community through related activities.', null, 'Ucrstarwarsclub@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/starwarsucr?igsh=YzVkODRmOTdmMw%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/starwarsclubatucr'),
(77168, 'Starving Artists', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Weekly! Join our Discord and Instagram for up-to-date information on meeting times and locations.', 'Weekly', null, 'We at Starving Artists are an organization dedicated to providing a forum, a space for students to come together and get involved in art related activities. Whether that may be through drawing or painting, we are open to all visual art mediums.', 'ABOUT US
Starving Artists is a club at UC Riverside that seeks to develop an open arena to both artists and non-artists in creating a collective that is centered on exchanging ideas, collaboration, networking, and developing skills. We seek to provide an environment of free artistic speech and expression through, but not limited to, the visual and performing arts. In addition, our goal is to service the community that exemplifies art in a socially responsible way.
CONTACT
StarvingArtistsUCR@gmail.com
SOCIAL MEDIA
Instagram: @starvingartistsucr
Discord: https://discord.gg/starvingartistsucr
Highlander Link: https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/starvingartists
CABINET
Co-President: Anna Medvedeva
Vice President: Aru Lopez
Secretary: Kelly Luu
Treasurer: Neil
Public Relations Director: Ro Zheng', 'StarvingArtistsUCR@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/starvingartistsucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/starvingartists'),
(179267, 'Statistics Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'The official GSA of the Statistics Department''s graduate program.', 'We aim to advance the academic, professional, and social lives of current and future statistics graduate students at UC Riverside, and to encourage collaboration on research with students that are both within and outside of the statistics department.', 'ucr.grad.stat@gmail.com', 'https://statistics.ucr.edu/graduate-program/mini-gsa', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/stats'),
(99795, 'STEM Connections Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Varies with schedule', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The mission of the STEM Connections Club is to foster academic excellence, community, and professional growth among STEM students, with a particular focus on supporting community college transfer students within the CNAS.', 'Mission:
The mission of the STEM Connections Club is to support, engage, and empower STEM students—particularly community college transfer students within the College of Natural and Agricultural Sciences (CNAS)—by fostering academic success, meaningful connections, and a strong sense of belonging at UC Riverside.
Through peer mentorship, academic and professional development programming, and community-building initiatives, STEM Connections promotes student retention, leadership development, and interdisciplinary collaboration within the STEM community.
Vision:
STEM Connections Club envisions an inclusive and connected STEM community at UC Riverside where all students—especially transfer students—are supported in their academic journeys, empowered to pursue leadership and research opportunities, and equipped to thrive as future professionals and change-makers in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics.
Values:
Inclusion
We are committed to cultivating an inclusive environment that embraces diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, ensuring all STEM students feel welcomed, valued, and supported.
Academic Excellence:
We promote rigorous learning, intellectual curiosity, and academic engagement by encouraging collaboration, skill-building, and continuous growth.
Community & Belonging:
We believe student success is strengthened through connection. We foster camaraderie, peer support, and meaningful relationships across STEM disciplines.
Leadership & Empowerment:
We empower students to develop leadership skills, pursue research and professional opportunities, and become advocates for themselves and their communities.
Collaboration & Service:
We value collaboration with faculty, campus partners, and student organizations to enhance access to resources and create impactful programming that supports student success.', 'stemconnections4@gmail.com', 'https://cnastransfer.ucr.edu/', 'https://www.instagram.com/stem_connections_club/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/stemclub'),
(384866, 'STEMivate', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Monday 4PM', 'Weekly', null, 'STEMivate is an organization founded in 2023 by students at the University of California, Riverside. This organization was built on the foundation of motivating students across Riverside county to pursue a passion in STEM.', 'This organization aims to inspire students in Riverside and the greater Inland Empire to pursue interests in STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics) and attain excellence in these fields. The organization facilitates engagement with college-level peers through peer mentorship, integrating STEM learning into classrooms. STEMivate focuses on promoting academic excellence and outreach by delivering college-level material in an accessible and enjoyable manner through college student mentors with expertise in STEM subjects. The primary goal is to help students succeed and excel in STEM-related subjects through a faster and more engaging learning experience.', 'stemivateriverside@gmail.com', 'https://stemivateriverside.wixsite.com/stemivate', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/stemivate'),
(431154, 'STEMsters', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'STEMsters is a student-led service organization that connects UCR students with opportunities to teach fun, hands-on STEM activities to K–8 students. Members gain experience in mentorship, leadership, and science while inspiring the next generation!', null, 'tterr007@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/stemsters'),
(414975, 'Stratos Associates', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 7 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'Stratos Associates is a student business club focused on leadership, entrepreneurship, and career growth through events and real-world projects.', 'Stratos Associates is a student-led professional development organization focused on helping business students across all concentrations gain access to internships, professional opportunities, leadership development, and real-world experience. Stratos works to create a collaborative and supportive environment where students can build confidence, develop professional skills, connect with opportunities, and grow within their respective career interests. Through internships, professional workshops, networking opportunities, certifications, collaborations, and hands-on leadership experience, Stratos aims to make career growth and professional development more accessible for students across fields such as finance, marketing, accounting, business analytics, management, entrepreneurship, operations, and strategy.', 'msutt012@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrstratos/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/stratosassociates'),
(82105, 'Stress Busters Peer Educators', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], null, 'Varies over course of the academic year', null, 'When stress strikes, call the StressBusters! We are available to present workshops on stress management, relaxation, time management, and sleep hygiene for your campus org. To schedule a presentation, email your request to ccpeers@ucr.edu.', 'The Stressbusters are undergraduate students trained by the UCR Counseling and Psychological Services to provide stress and time management, relaxation,and sleep hygiene workshops, as well as tabling events, to the campus community. The workshops are fun, interactive, and relaxing. Our services are available for FREE to any group on campus, including clubs and organizations, residential halls, fraternities/sororities, among others. You are welcome to contact us at Ccpeers@ucr.edu or visit our website below for more information on requesting a workshop or tabling event for your group. We look forward to hearing from you!
Please visit our website: http://counseling.ucr.edu/education-training/Pages/StressBusterPeerEducators.aspx.', 'ccpeers@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/stressbusters'),
(70887, 'Student Affiliates in School Psychology', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], 'Thursday afternoons', 'Monthly', null, 'Student Affiliates in School Psychology', 'The purposes of SASP are to:
encourage and promote collaboration and community among school psychology students and faculty, the UCR community, and other school psychology programs and organizations, both locally and nationally
provide opportunities for networking and additional training in the field of school psychology
encourage and promote participation in research that increases the educational and psychological well-being of children and youth
promote the field of school psychology and the doctoral program in school psychology at UCR
provide a forum for the identification and discussion of current and future student needs, both professionally and academically', 'vnguy275@ucr.edu', 'http://www.apadivisions.org/division-16/students/index.aspx', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sasp'),
(71056, 'Student Athlete Advisory Committee', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Department Affiliated Organization']::text[], '1st and 3rd Monday at 7pm', 'Every two weeks', null, '1st and 3rd Monday of the month', 'SAAC is a student-athlete run group that provides communication between administrators and student-athletes, we strive to create lasting connections in the community and also on campus, we focus and work towards building leadership and responsibility among our SAAC representatives, and are dedicated to enhancing the student-athlete experience through fundraising and providing NCAA litigation', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/saac'),
(71096, 'Student Disability Union', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'N/A', 'Every two weeks', 'Ability Ball (a lively evening showcasing the talents of both individuals with or without disabilities)
Event and meeting details will be shared through our Instagram: @sdu_ucr
We also have a Discord: https://discord.gg/sv2Uru3C6k', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to spread acceptance and awareness for disabled students, to provide them a safe social space on-campus, and to advocate for disabled students'' needs.', 'Welcome! We are the Student Disability Union at UCR!
Our purpose is to create an inclusive, safe, and engaging group on campus that empowers UCR''s disabled community and promotes acceptance through advocacy and education. We hold events that actively collaborate with students and other diverse organizations/clubs to bring the disabled student population together to establish a community, encourage discussion, and participate in fun socials. The ultimate goal is to build relationships, cultivate campus connections, and give a collective voice to an underrepresented and misunderstood minority.
ALL UCR students, with or without disabilities, are welcome to participate!
We organize events/activities on campus that include:
Socials (individuals can chat and chill while participating in fun-themed activities)
Awareness Events (to teach people about disability rights)
Ability Ball (a lively evening showcasing the talents of both individuals with or without disabilities)
Event and meeting details will be shared through our Instagram: @sdu_ucr
We also have a Discord: https://discord.gg/sv2Uru3C6k', 'sdu.ucr.mail@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/sdu_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sdu'),
(70847, 'Student Homeless Aid Relief Project at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Every other Friday at 7pm (Check our Instagram for our times: @sharpucr)', 'Every two weeks', 'https://youtu.be/LMNHzebQcY4
To provide food, clothing and hygiene products for the homeless of the Riverside community while providing students the opportunity to partake in community service and encouraging them to take initiative in helping to meet the needs of the community.
Check out our Instagram @sharpucr for more information on our meeting dates!', 'To provide food, clothing and hygiene products for the homeless of the Riverside community while providing students the opportunity to partake in community service and encouraging them to take initiative in helping to meet the needs of the community.', 'https://youtu.be/LMNHzebQcY4
To provide food, clothing and hygiene products for the homeless of the Riverside community while providing students the opportunity to partake in community service and encouraging them to take initiative in helping to meet the needs of the community.
Check out our Instagram @sharpucr for more information on our meeting dates!', 'sharpucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/sharpucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sharp'),
(71124, 'Student Veterans Organization', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Wednesdays 4pm - 5:00pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Our purpose is to provide service, guidance and support to all Veterans, Service Members,students, or anyone receiving military educational benefits and their families.', 'To provide information and guidance to student Veterans, active duty, retired, reservist, National Guard members or any students receiving military educational benefits on current issues affecting them; help those members in need by providing scholarships (when available), based on achievement as stated on a Scholarship Application, to help them continue their education at UCR; create a network where members can share their knowledge with family members, the UC Riverside community and other organizations outside the school.', 'svo.ucr24@gmail.com', 'http://studentveterans.org/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/svo'),
(424544, 'Students for a National Health Program at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'The efforts of Students for a National Health Program (SNaHP) at UCR are aimed at achieving our ultimate goal of repairing our broken health system through the implementation of a single payer healthcare system for all.', 'Students for a National Health Program (SNaHP) at UCR is dedicated to advancing health equity through education, advocacy, and scholarship in support of a universal, single-payer health care system.
Grounded in the belief that health care is a human right, our chapter works to promote patient-centered care, physician autonomy, and health policy that prioritizes public good over profit. We seek to promote a healthcare system committed to improving access, quality, and aﬀordability of care for the medically underserved communities of Inland Southern California and beyond, regardless of patients'' socioeconomic status, race, gender, sexual orientation, age, residency status, or disability.
Our eﬀorts are aimed at achieving our ultimate goal of repairing our broken health system through the implementation of a single payer healthcare system for all.', 'ucrsomsnahp@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/snahpucr'),
(70837, 'Students for Justice in Palestine (SJP)', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Our meeting days vary, so we encourage you to follow our Instagram page for updates on upcoming meeting times and locations. We regularly post announcements to keep everyone informed!', 'We typically aim to meet a few times each quarter to stay connected and engage with our members.', null, 'Students for Justice in Palestine (SJP) is a diverse group of students, faculty, staff, and community members working towards promoting Palestinian Liberation.', 'Students for Justice in Palestine (SJP) is a diverse group of students, faculty, staff, and community members working towards educating the public on the plight of the Palestinian people, combating Zionism in all its forms, and promoting the liberation of Palestine. We are organized on democratic principles to promote justice, human rights, liberation, and self-determination for the Palestinian people.', 'ucr.sjp48@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/sjpucr?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sjp'),
(165176, 'Students Organize for Syria', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Students Organize for Syria focuses on promoting student solidarity with the Syrian people’s struggle for freedom by holding nationally unified campaigns in the following three categories:

-Education/Awareness

-Advocacy/Solidarity

-Fundraising', 'SOS envisions a free Syria in which the Syrian people have the rights and freedoms that they deserve. Our mission is to stand in solidarity with the Syrian people in their struggle for freedom and human rights, to assist Syrians in their effort to build a self-determined and pluralistic society, and to raise awareness of and help alleviate the humanitarian crisis currently taking place in Syria. We are devoted to sustaining an organized student network that is unified for the cause of a free Syria.', null, 'http://organize4syria.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/sos_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/studentsorganize4syria'),
(406679, 'Students Supporting Israel', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Monthly', null, 'Supporting Israel in a safe area as well as learning about its culture and daily life', 'Students will have a safe place where they feel comfortable to support Israel and its right to exist. Along with this there will be many events held to teach about the life and culture of Israel and its people. Another main part of our organization will be to be a strong', 'jvela196@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ssi'),
(362381, 'Study of Religion Departmental GSA', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'We will meet once quarterly to begin, and expand to monthly should students find the need.', null, null, 'The Study of Religion Departmental GSA will act as a liaison between graduate students in the Study of Religion Department and the broader Graduate Student Association.', null, 'dclev004@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/rlst-gsa'),
(384421, 'Supply Chain Society at UC Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Varies: General meetings happen later in the afternoon and site tours happen from morning to noon.', 'Weekly', null, 'Developing leaders in supply chain management at UCR by providing opportunities for hands-on training, networking, collaborations and career advancement.', 'Mission: Inspire, educate and develop our members to be the future leaders in supply chain management, providing opportunities for hands-on training, networking, collaborations, and career advancement to bridge the skill and knowledge gap between academia and industry.
Vision: Develop UC Riverside as a center for Supply Chain development, bringing more job opportunities and exposure in the field to the university and its surrounding communities.', 'scs.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/scs.ucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/scs.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/supply-chain-society-ucr'),
(430427, 'SURGE at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'The goal is to provide a pipeline to industry knowledge and experience. I hope to regularly participate in nationwide Economic competitions as well as provide the UCR campus with its own economic outlook from the students themselves.', 'The purpose is to research Business-Economics primarily, and the application towards real life cases. Our personal outlook is that outside of prior knowledge and experience many students can find it hard to relate those within their field and often feel behind when compared. Our hope is to eliminate this stigma, and instead provide the opportunity to build from 0 to 100 with students who show the desire to learn, and progress. We cannot know what we don’t know, so to build from 0 there must be a base to work from. We hope that our club can provide this opportunity to build the technical and behaviorals, needed for their own related fields outside of their classes. We will provide professional industry exposure, educational learning opportunities, and real world cases to each of our members.', 'glard001@ucr.edu', 'https://surgeucr.wixsite.com/surge/blank-1', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/surgeucr'),
(71061, 'Sustainable UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Thursday at 7PM', 'Weekly', null, 'Be the change that this world needs! Join us in advocating for sustainability at UCR and in our local communities.', 'For over a decade, Sustainable UCR has been working towards building a better, more sustainable life and community at UCR. In the past, we have worked on installing solar panels during Solarthon, collecting/composting coffee grinds, organizing events during Earth Week, and working with other organizations to make their events more sustainable. Today, we are focused on continuing the legacy of our great work, specifically in the aspects of food, water, waste, energy, and culture.
Join our sustainable movement as we change our community!
Visit our Linktree!
Sustainable UCR is open to any ideas that our members present! We welcome any ideas for projects, events, or collaborations.', 'sustainableucr.org@gmail.com', 'https://instagram.com/sustainableucr/', 'https://www.instagram.com/sustainableucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sustainableucr'),
(430819, 'SWANA Education Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Tuesdays', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The SWANA Education Association (SEA) promotes education and cultural understanding of Southwest Asia and North Africa through workshops, discussions, events, and community engagement.', 'The SWANA Education Association (SEA) is a student organization at the University of California, Riverside dedicated to promoting education about the Southwest Asia and North Africa (SWANA) region. Through educational
programming and meaningful dialogue, SEA strives to deepen understanding of the region''s diverse histories, cultures, languages, traditions, and identities.
SEA believes that education is one of the most powerful tools for fostering curiosity, challenging misconceptions, and building cross-cultural understanding. Our organization creates opportunities for students to engage with the richness and diversity of
the SWANA region in an inclusive, welcoming environment.', 'dibra012@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/seaucr'),
(424149, 'Syrian American Medical Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Syrian American Medical Society (SAMS) started in 1998 as a professional network in the U.S., originally focused on connecting Syrian-descent medical professionals and offering educational and cultural resources. SAMS was founded in 2007.', 'The Syrian American Medical Society (SAMS) was founded in 1998 in the United States as a professional society to provide networking, educational, cultural, and professional services to medical professionals of Syrian descent. SAMS Foundation, the charitable arm of SAMS, was launched in 2007. Since then, SAMS has become one of the most active and leading medical relief organizations working on the front lines of crisis relief in Syria, neighboring countries, and beyond. SAMS has since implemented an integrated model of essential services that emphasizes priority needs, including the delivery of medical education, training, and financial support for physicians and other healthcare workers inside Syria and in neighboring countries. SAMS has established field hospitals, intensive care units, dental and primary care clinics, birth and newborn care facilities, mobile medical units, and dialysis centers.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/6721'),
(293661, 'Table Tennis Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Monday and Wednesday evenings', 'Twice per week', null, 'Table Tennis Club at UCR is sincerely built to help those who are interested in playing table tennis casually or to improve their skills and provide a friendly and welcoming environment in the sport of table tennis no matter the skill level', 'Table Tennis Club at UCR is a community of table tennis players at all skill levels dedicated to fostering casual and competitive play.
Join our Discord for more information and to see when people are playing: https://discord.gg/7nswYnB5dS
Follow our Instagram @ucr_table_tennis
Buy Quality Equipment and Help Support our Club! : https://www.megaspin.net/default.asp?aid=ucr', 'ucrtabletennis@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_table_tennis/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ttcucr'),
(123063, 'Taekwondo Club @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Mondays and Wednesdays from 9:15pm-10:45pm', 'Twice a week.', 'The mission of the Taekwondo Club is to provide training for those of all skill levels. We welcome all those who have previous experience, zero experience, are martial arts enthusiasts, or generally curious of the sport. We aim to teach the rich Korean culture of Taekwondo to all members, as well as the development of competitive skills while having fun.
Come join us! Our practices are Mondays and Wednesdays from 9:15 PM - 10:45 PM in the SRC North, MPR D!
Any questions? Contact us!
Join our Discord server! https://discord.gg/ungzmJyVyY
Email us (ucrtaekwondo@gmail.com) or message us on Instagram (@tkdatucr)!', 'The mission of the Taekwondo Club is to provide training for those already experienced in self-defense, introduce the martial art to new members, and teach the Taekwondo culture to its members.', 'Welcome to Taekwondo Club at UCR!
The mission of the Taekwondo Club is to provide training for those of all skill levels. We welcome all those who have previous experience, zero experience, are martial arts enthusiasts, or generally curious of the sport. We aim to teach the rich Korean culture of Taekwondo to all members, as well as the development of competitive skills while having fun.
Come join us! Our practices are Mondays and Wednesdays from 9:15 PM - 10:45 PM in the SRC North, MPR D!
Any questions? Contact us!
Join our Discord server! https://discord.gg/ungzmJyVyY
Email us (ucrtaekwondo@gmail.com) or message us on Instagram (@tkdatucr)!', 'ucrtaekwondo@gmail.com', 'https://recreation.ucr.edu/competitive-sports/do-sports-easy', 'https://www.instagram.com/tkdatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tkd'),
(71111, 'Taiwanese Graduate Student Association', 'Graduate Student Association', array['Graduate Student Organization']::text[], 'Friday, 4pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Provides networking, educational resources, and information exchange to support member development.', 'This organization serves as a platform to support the academic, professional, and social development of its members. It facilitates peer networking, educational programming, and information sharing to enhance engagement, collaboration, and access to relevant resources. Activities are designed to encourage knowledge exchange, community connection, and informed participation within the university environment.', 'ucrtgsa2025@gmail.com', 'https://sites.google.com/view/tgsaucr/home', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrtgsa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tgsa'),
(386051, 'Tartan Seoul', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'Tartan Seoul is an all-inclusive K-pop dance team for students to come together with a passion for dance and Korean Culture!', 'Tartan Seoul is an all-inclusive K-pop dance team for students to come together with a passion for dance and Korean Culture! All UCR students are free to attend events to socialize and take part in projects with their peers who share similar interests in a safe, enjoyable environment in our team.', 'tartanseoul@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/tartanseoul?igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tartan-seoul'),
(71117, 'Tau Sigma National Honor Society', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Honors']::text[], 'Meeting times vary by quarter. For up-to-date information check our Instagram @tausigma_ucr', 'Twice a quarter', null, 'Tau Sigma National Honor Society – a national honor society designed exclusively for transfer students!', 'Tau Sigma is an induction based national honors society focused on recognizing and promoting the academic excellence and involvement of transfer students.
The University of California- Riverside (UCR) branch of Tau Sigma provides its member''s opportunities to earn scholarships, attend leadership conferences, take leadership positions, and serve others, while joining a robust community of other academically motivated transfer students.', 'tausigmanhsucr@gmail.com', 'http://www.tausigmanhs.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/tausigma_ucr?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNIZDc0MzlxNw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tausigma'),
(381447, 'Tea and Go', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Thursdays 3-6 pm in HUB 379', 'Weekly', 'Learn how to play the games of Go and Mahjong, while enjoying a new traditional tea every meeting!', 'Learn how to play the games of Go and Mahjong, while enjoying a new traditional tea every meeting! 
Fall 2024 meetings Wednesdays 3-5 pm, follow ucr_tag on Instagram for updates on location.', 'Learn how to play the games of Go and Mahjong, while enjoying a new traditional tea every meeting!', 'ucrTeaAndGo@gmail.com', 'https://discord.gg/peSZUJWhvS', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_tag/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tag'),
(70978, 'Tennis on Campus at University of California, Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Monday and Wednesday from 8 P.M. - 10 P.M. @ SRC Tennis Courts', 'Weekly', null, 'Tennis on Campus at UCR is established to provide recreational and competitive tennis activity for students, staffs, alumnus, and faculty at the University.', 'The purpose of this organization is to provide recreational and competitive tennis activity for students, staff, and faculty at UCR. All levels are accepted and our club has the goal to provide a friendly, fun environment where people can bond over tennis and progress in their skills. The club also provides a competitive team that travels and competes against other university tennis clubs. For updates, we highly recommend for you to follow our Instagram and to fill out the club interest form below.
Have questions about the club? Refer to our Frequently Asked Questions!
https://docs.google.com/document/FAQs
Interested in our tennis club? Fill out the club interest form below!
https://docs.google.com/forms/TennisOnCampus
