(74524, 'Test Group', 'Registered Student Organization', null, null, null, null, 'Test', null, null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/testgroup'),
(70821, 'Thai Student Union at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Mon-Fri 5-6pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Thai Student Union (TSU) is established to unite the Thai student body and anyone with Thai interests. Promote understandings of Thai culture and volunteer opportunity for those who are interested in serving the Thai culture and Riverside community.', 'สามัคคี (Samakkhi) - United as one
Welcome to Thai Student Union @ UCR! We strive to provide a space for Thai people and those who are interested in learning and experiencing Thai culture to intermingle and give back to the local communities. Our members can create meaningful connections
through cultural experiences and social events that will enrich them with long-lasting memories. We hope that you will join us on this journey.', 'tsuucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.facebook.com/ucrthaistudentunion/', 'https://www.instagram.com/tsuucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/thaiclubucr'),
(407534, 'The 3E Study', 'Department Affiliated Organization', null, null, 'Monthly', null, 'The 3E Study seeks to generate research to improve health and wellbeing for marginalized emerging adults. We aim to spread awareness about cardiometabolic and mental health, mentoring in college, research opportunities, and social determinants of health.', 'The 3E Club seeks to generate research to improve health and wellbeing for marginalized emerging adults. We aim to spread awareness about cardiometabolic and mental health, mentoring in college, research opportunities, and social determinants of health. We hope to create a community for all students to feel supported and have a space safe on campus.', '3e@ucr.edu', 'https://3e.ucsf.edu/', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/the3estudy'),
(424600, 'The Actuarial Science Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesdays Between 5pm and 9pm (depends on event)', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Actuarial Science Club is a student organization in the University of California Riverside. This club is aimed for students who are in the major or just interested in Actuarial Science.', 'The Actuarial Science Club is to create a supportive and collaborative environment for students that are in the major or interested in actuarial science for either a career or just further interest. Our mission is to explore students'' knowledge on the subject and explore the profession. We wish to help them through a strong community, group studying, workshops, speaker sessions, and develop them with career-ready skills. We wish to grow our major and build a strong network with certified actuaries that are in the profession.', 'Tascucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/tasc_ucr?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tasc'),
(332789, 'The Basics Of Healthcare Initiative', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Board meets every week, members meet every two weeks', null, 'To educate individuals of the basics of healthcare, which is important to be aware of for every citizen regardless of health status and to stress the role of patient advocacy to combat potential lack of access, respect, or simple bedside manners.', 'To educate individuals of the basics of healthcare, which is important to be aware of for every citizen regardless of health status and to stress the role of patient advocacy to combat potential lack of access, respect, or simple bedside manners.
B: barrier-breaking (addressing language/cultural barriers and inequalities)
A: advocating (being a voice for those who do not have one; fighting stigmas and assumptions)
S: supporting (employing kindness and empathy in evaluation and treatment of patient condition)
I: informing (educating and learning about various diseases)
C: considering (acknowledging and respecting patient opinion)
S: spreading awareness (discussing importance of patient’s role as the member of the healthcare team)', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tbhi'),
(430990, 'the Beautiful Minds Project', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'A student organization at UCR dedicated to providing mental health resources &amp; destigmatizing mental health in our Muslim Community', null, 'bmpatucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/bmp'),
(350886, 'The Climbing Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Monday, Thursday, and Friday Evenings (6 - 9PM)', 'Monday(@Hangar18 East Riverside, 2111 Iowa Ave suite a, Riverside, CA 92507), Thursday(@SRC), Friday(@Hangar18) 6 - 9 PM', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to make climbing more accessible to the student body as well as provide climbers with a community in which they can meet their peers and challenge themselves.
~Why Join Us?~
1. Thrilling Climbing Expeditions: Explore SoCal''s stunning natural landscapes, from Bishop to Joshua Tree, we explore it all.
2. Inclusive Community: Connect with climbers of all skill levels in an inclusive, supportive environment.', 'Are you ready to break free from your studies and experience college life in a way like never before?  Look no further than The Climbing Club at UCR, where adventure meets camaraderie, and passion for climbing the great outdoors thrives!', 'The purpose of this organization shall be to make climbing more accessible to the student body as well as provide climbers with a community in which they can meet their peers and challenge themselves.
~Why Join Us?~
1. Thrilling Climbing Expeditions: Explore SoCal''s stunning natural landscapes, from Bishop to Joshua Tree, we explore it all.
2. Inclusive Community: Connect with climbers of all skill levels in an inclusive, supportive environment.
3. Escape the Routine: Put away your homework, swap your textbooks and lab coats for crash pads and beanies on one of our outdoor climbing trips. Scale to new heights while making unforgettable memories with fellow climbers.
ALL SKILL LEVELS WELCOME! Whether you''re a seasoned crusher or have never touched a rock before, our club is open to all.', 'riversideclimbingclub@gmail.com', null, 'https://instagram.com/climbucr?igshid=MjEwN2IyYWYwYw==', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/climbingclub'),
(349723, 'The Comedy Closet', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Mondays 7-9pm', 'Weekly', null, 'An organization calling all comedians. The goal is to perform, teach amateurs the craft of talking to an audience, giving feedback to members, and putting on showcases for the masses to see.', 'An organization for student comedians! The purpose of this organization is to provide amateur comedians and performers the opportunities to express themselves, improve comedy skills, and collaborate with others in the field while having the opportunity to entertain an audience. Our organization focuses on three "pillars" of comedy, stand-up, improv, and sketch comedy.', 'TheComedyClosetUCR@gmail.com', null, 'http://www.instagram.com/comedyclosetucr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/thecomedycloset'),
(76978, 'The Dynamic Genome Outreach Group', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'We meet on different days depending on board availability, but meetings tend to be no longer than an hour.', 'We meet on an as-needed basis.', 'The purpose of the Dynamic Genome Outreach Group, DGOG, is to inspire and educate K-12 students in molecular biology and related research sciences by allowing hands-on experience on model experiments guided by UCR undergraduates.
**Please also e-mail us at dgog.ucr@gmail.com after requesting membership in order to receive updates on events and meetings.**', 'The purpose of The Dynamic Genome Outreach Group, DGOG, is to inspire and educate K-12 students in molecular biology and related research sciences by allowing hands-on experience on model experiments guided by UCR undergraduates.', 'The purpose of the Dynamic Genome Outreach Group, DGOG, is to inspire and educate K-12 students in molecular biology and related research sciences by allowing hands-on experience on model experiments guided by UCR undergraduates.
**Please also e-mail us at dgog.ucr@gmail.com after requesting membership in order to receive updates on events and meetings.**', 'dgog.ucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/dgog.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/dgog'),
(366644, 'The EcoCAR EV Challenge Team at UC Riverside', 'Department Affiliated Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Weekly meetings vary depending on each team', 'Weekly', 'The latest AVTC series, the EcoCAR EV Challenge (2022-2026), will challenge 15 North American universities to engineer a next generation battery electric vehicle (BEV) that utilizes automation and vehicle-to-everything (V2X)
connectivity to implement energy efficient customer-pleasing features, and meet the decarbonization needs of the automotive industry.
Learn more about the competition: https://avtcseries.org/about-the-ecocar-ev-challenge/
Read about our Year 1 achievements: https://www.highlandernews.org/87508/ucr-ecocar-team-wins-two-awards-at-ecocar-ev-challenge-y1-competition-in-orlando-florida/', 'Home of UCR''s Team for the EcoCAR EV Challenge, where we provide students with hands-on experience related to the development of electric vehicles, promoting electrification, STEM education and career opportunities in the automotive field.', 'The latest AVTC series, the EcoCAR EV Challenge (2022-2026), will challenge 15 North American universities to engineer a next generation battery electric vehicle (BEV) that utilizes automation and vehicle-to-everything (V2X)
connectivity to implement energy efficient customer-pleasing features, and meet the decarbonization needs of the automotive industry.
Learn more about the competition: https://avtcseries.org/about-the-ecocar-ev-challenge/
Read about our Year 1 achievements: https://www.highlandernews.org/87508/ucr-ecocar-team-wins-two-awards-at-ecocar-ev-challenge-y1-competition-in-orlando-florida/', 'ecocar@ucr.edu', 'https://ecocar.engr.ucr.edu/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ecocar.ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ecocar-ucr'),
(430443, 'The Encouragement Network', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Wednesday 6-7pm, Thursday 6-7pm', 'Every two weeks', 'The Encouragement Network’s (TEN) mission is to support local community and campus mental health. Our main program is sending encouraging text messages to those in need. Anyone can fill out our form, providing their name (optional), contact information and additional information for a personalized message. Our service aims to build an encouraging support system for all participants in our program. Those interested in becoming a volunteer for our program can reach out to our network to begin the interview process.
In addition to our messaging system, we aim to build a strong social community on campus. We host various events, with a majority of them providing opportunities for students to meet with their fellow peers and connect.
TEN does not provide licensed psychological services such as therapy, counseling and advice. All campus chapters are expected to partner with their campuses respective psychological services to develop protocols for redirecting those in need to appropriate services. TEN will also work to promote campus psychological services to bring awareness to resources available on campus and to potentially reach those in need.', 'The Encouragement Network (TEN) aims to bring awareness to mental health by sending encouraging messages to those in need through a personalized messaging system. TEN aims to create a friendly environment on campus for students to socialize.', 'The Encouragement Network’s (TEN) mission is to support local community and campus mental health. Our main program is sending encouraging text messages to those in need. Anyone can fill out our form, providing their name (optional), contact information and additional information for a personalized message. Our service aims to build an encouraging support system for all participants in our program. Those interested in becoming a volunteer for our program can reach out to our network to begin the interview process.
In addition to our messaging system, we aim to build a strong social community on campus. We host various events, with a majority of them providing opportunities for students to meet with their fellow peers and connect.
TEN does not provide licensed psychological services such as therapy, counseling and advice. All campus chapters are expected to partner with their campuses respective psychological services to develop protocols for redirecting those in need to appropriate services. TEN will also work to promote campus psychological services to bring awareness to resources available on campus and to potentially reach those in need.', 'TheEncouragmentNetwork.net@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ten'),
(406065, 'The Garden Project at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', null, 'check our instagram for meeting times!', 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to work with local schools to build student-run gardens, provide nutritious fresh food, and educate youth about nutrition.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to work with local schools to build student-run gardens, provide nutritious fresh food, and educate youth about nutrition.', 'gsilv034@ucr.edu', 'https://www.thegardenproject.com.co', 'https://www.instagram.com/thegardenprojectucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/wwwinstagramcomthegardenprojectucr'),
(431163, 'The Ihsan Mission at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Ihsan Mission at UCR is a student-run organization dedicated to serving underserved communities through healthcare-focused education, community service, and outreach. Inspired by the Islamic principle of Ihsan.', null, 'ihsanmissionucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ihsanmissionucr'),
(123173, 'The Literacy Initiative', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'We normally meet in the evening.', 'We meet around 3 times per quarter. Once for training/orientation and twice for general meetings.', null, 'The purpose of this organization is to raise child literacy rates in the Riverside community to the child’s respective grade reading level or above through an incentive program.', 'The purpose of this to organization is to raise child literacy rates in the Riverside community to the child’s respective grade reading level or above. We wish to empower our students by giving them the fundamental tool of reading to aid them in their educational path. We also aim to be positive role models for the children and to foster a passion for reading and higher education.', 'theliteracyinitiativeucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/literacyucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/theliteracyinitiative'),
(70970, 'The Mini-Graduate Student Association of the Environmental Toxicology Program', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Mini-GSA']::text[], null, 'Quarterly', null, 'The purpose of the UCR ETOX mini-GSA is to provide a unified voice of the ETOX graduate students within the larger Graduate Student Association and foster a community where ETOX students can easily interact with each other both academically and socially.', 'The purpose of the UCR ETOX mini-GSA is to provide a unified voice of the ETOX graduate students within the larger Graduate Student Association and foster a community where ETOX students can easily interact with each other both academically and socially.', 'wtrox002@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucretox_mgsa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/etoxmini-gsa'),
(120447, 'The National Society of Leadership and Success', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', '· Learn from exceptional leaders like former President Barack Obama during exclusive Speaker Broadcasts.
· Meet new friends and make lifelong connections (on-campus and virtually).
· Overcome challenges with success coaches shortcutting your way to success.
· Access to private networking events.
Visit the NSLS website to learn more about and accept your nomination.', 'The NSLS is the largest leadership honor society in the United States. Our NSLS chapter at University of California, Riverside was started in 2015. Our local chapter is part of the national organization with 700+ chapters and over 1.4 million members.', 'The NSLS is the largest leadership honor society in the United States. Our NSLS chapter at University of California, Riverside was started in 2015. Our local chapter is part of the national organization with 700+ chapters and over 1.4 million members.
Students are selected based on exemplary academic achievement. As of 2021 we have 1,930 members who have access to:
· More than $400,000 in scholarships.
· An exclusive NSLS job board.
· A personalized letter of recommendation.
The NSLS leadership program teaches the interpersonal skills that employers seek to give you an edge in the job market. Hear directly from current members as they share how their experience has changed their life.
If you become a member, some of the other benefits are:
· Learn from exceptional leaders like former President Barack Obama during exclusive Speaker Broadcasts.
· Meet new friends and make lifelong connections (on-campus and virtually).
· Overcome challenges with success coaches shortcutting your way to success.
· Access to private networking events.
Visit the NSLS website to learn more about and accept your nomination.
Frequently Asked Questions:
Some of the common questions we receive are listed below. If you have any other questions, visit nsls.org to chat with a team member or email help@nsls.org.
What do I have to do to become inducted?
Our five-step program takes approximately 12 hours over the course of the semester at your pace.
Is this recognized on campus?
We are a Registered Student Organization (RSO). As of 2021, we had 1,930 in our chapter and there are more than 1.4 million members nationwide.', 'nsls.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.nsls.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/nsls_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/nsls'),
(386389, 'The Play Project', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Wednesdays or Thursdays at 8 PM.', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Play Project strives to serve the community of Riverside, creating playful and engaging activities with the youth.', 'The Play Project is an initiative aimed to connect to the Riverside community through creating fun and playful opportunities for children to exercise, whilst educating children on the importance of a playful lifestyle.', 'theplayprojectucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/theplayprojectucr'),
(293750, 'The Public Health Initiative', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], '6:00 pm', 'Monthly', null, 'The purpose of this organization is to be focused in science and systems designed to protect and improve health at the community and population level. This includes efforts to improve health through disease prevention and promoting healthy behaviors.', 'The purpose of this organization is to be focused in science and systems designed to protect and improve health at the community and population level. This includes efforts to improve health through disease prevention and promoting healthy behaviors as well as community service.', 'publichealthinitiativeucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/publichealthinitiative'),
(425266, 'The Reach Initiative', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Undecided', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Reach Initiative is a student led organization serving underserved communities in Riverside, with a focus on the elderly and individuals with disabilities. Through hands on service and advocacy, we build real connections and create lasting impact.', 'The Reach Initiative is a student led organization committed to serving underserved communities in Riverside, with a special focus on elderly individuals and people with disabilities. Through meaningful service, advocacy, and strong community partnerships, we transform compassion into real impact. Our members don’t just volunteer, they build genuine connections, restore dignity, and create lasting change. If you’re looking for a club where your involvement truly matters and your service makes a difference, The Reach Initiative is where you belong.', null, null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/thereachinitiative'),
(77063, 'The Salsa Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Fridays 5:00pm-7:00pm SRC North MPR B', 'Weekly', 'The purpose and mission of The Salsa Club at UCR is to create a passionate and supportive student community that aims to share the skill, knowledge, and joy of salsa dancing and related dances. We provide instruction in the basics of salsa, bachata, tango, and other latin dances which are growing in popularity within local salsa clubs and Latin dance clubs. We aim to provide an environment where practice of the above dances can be executed, to provide a social network that focuses on dancing events and activities, and to provide a portal for individuals with similar interests to meet and interact.
This organization originally began back in the summer of 2001 when some of the UCR student members of the Ballroom and Swing Club of UCR (BaSC) branched off towards a love of salsa. The club lasted several strong years before losing active status due to various issues, but was reformed in Fall of 2012 by UCR students who were inspired to give new life to the Salsa Club at UCR after hearing stories from the club alumni of their life-changing experiences during their time in the organization.
Our goal as the new generation of the Salsa Club at UCR is to ensure a continued, thriving existence for the club with the addition of a very supportive network of alumni in the salsa community as a way for the members of the Riverside Salsa Family to continue growing and supporting this gateway to a life-long gift of dance, friendship, and perhaps love!
We meet every Friday from 5:00-7:00pm at SRC north MPR B! No need to register in advance! See you there!', 'Our club aims to share our knowledge of salsa dance and related styles (Bachata, Tango, Cumbia, etc). Our group provides dance instruction, practice, as well as a network that knows and provides many community social dance opportunities.', 'The purpose and mission of The Salsa Club at UCR is to create a passionate and supportive student community that aims to share the skill, knowledge, and joy of salsa dancing and related dances. We provide instruction in the basics of salsa, bachata, tango, and other latin dances which are growing in popularity within local salsa clubs and Latin dance clubs. We aim to provide an environment where practice of the above dances can be executed, to provide a social network that focuses on dancing events and activities, and to provide a portal for individuals with similar interests to meet and interact.
This organization originally began back in the summer of 2001 when some of the UCR student members of the Ballroom and Swing Club of UCR (BaSC) branched off towards a love of salsa. The club lasted several strong years before losing active status due to various issues, but was reformed in Fall of 2012 by UCR students who were inspired to give new life to the Salsa Club at UCR after hearing stories from the club alumni of their life-changing experiences during their time in the organization.
Our goal as the new generation of the Salsa Club at UCR is to ensure a continued, thriving existence for the club with the addition of a very supportive network of alumni in the salsa community as a way for the members of the Riverside Salsa Family to continue growing and supporting this gateway to a life-long gift of dance, friendship, and perhaps love!
We meet every Friday from 5:00-7:00pm at SRC north MPR B! No need to register in advance! See you there!', 'ucrsalsaclub@gmail.com', 'http://www.ucrsalsa.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrsalsaclub/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/thesalsaclubatucr'),
(425412, 'The Serve Collective', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Wednesdays: 12pm - 1pm', 'Weekly', null, 'The Serve Collective was created to help organizations further their mission, while students gain real-world experience.', 'The purpose of this organization is to empower students to use business knowledge and professional skills to create meaningful impact within the community. We aim to connect students with nonprofit organizations, small businesses, and community initiatives to provide pro-bono support, volunteer service, and strategic solutions that drive positive social change.', 'theservecollective@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/theservecollective.ucr/#', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/theservecollective'),
(71157, 'The Society of Physics Students', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Usually Fridays, from 6-7PM', 'Every two weeks', 'Established at The University of California at Riverside on November 7th, 2007, the Society of Physics Students (SPS) provides undergraduates and graduates from all disciplines the opportunity to expand and further their knowledge of physical phenomena through the following: Dynamic, interactive meetings which bring together members for the purpose of discussion of physics-related topics Organized field trips to laboratories, particle accelerators, observatories, Universities and a plethora of other institutions which demonstrate physics in the real world Philanthropy/community service, Guided research, Colloquial Projects, and group collaborations aimed to showcase the creative and inginuitive thought of every individual. It is the goal of SPS to to help students transform themselves into contributing members of the professional community or help students expand and further their knowledge. Course work develops only one range of skills. Other skills needed to flourish professionally include effective communication and personal interactions, leadership experience, establishing a personal network of contacts, presenting scholarly work in professional meetings and journals, and outreach services to the campus and local communities.', 'Established at The University of California at Riverside on November 7th, 2007, the Society of Physics Students (SPS) provides undergraduates and graduates from all disciplines the opportunity to expand and further their knowledge of physical phenomena.', 'Established at The University of California at Riverside on November 7th, 2007, the Society of Physics Students (SPS) provides undergraduates and graduates from all disciplines the opportunity to expand and further their knowledge of physical phenomena through the following: Dynamic, interactive meetings which bring together members for the purpose of discussion of physics-related topics Organized field trips to laboratories, particle accelerators, observatories, Universities and a plethora of other institutions which demonstrate physics in the real world Philanthropy/community service, Guided research, Colloquial Projects, and group collaborations aimed to showcase the creative and inginuitive thought of every individual. It is the goal of SPS to to help students transform themselves into contributing members of the professional community or help students expand and further their knowledge. Course work develops only one range of skills. Other skills needed to flourish professionally include effective communication and personal interactions, leadership experience, establishing a personal network of contacts, presenting scholarly work in professional meetings and journals, and outreach services to the campus and local communities.', 'sps.ucriverside@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/ucr_sps', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_sps/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/sps'),
(424815, 'The Sports Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to create a welcoming community for students who enjoy

sports of all kinds, including both playing and watching sports.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to create a welcoming community for students who enjoy
sports of all kinds, including both playing and watching sports. The organization aims to foster
connection and friendship among sports enthusiasts through social events, recreational activities, and
opportunities to bond over professional sports such as the NFL, NBA, MLB, College Sports and other
leagues. The club provides members with a fun and inclusive environment to engage with sports and
build lasting relationships.', 'apana011@ucr.edu', 'https://discord.gg/6mubwvER', 'https://www.instagram.com/sportsclub_ucr?stkn=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/thesportsclub'),
(382276, 'The Surgical Specialties Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Monday 6pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Surgical Specialties Club is for aspiring pre-medical students who are interested in a surgical profession and for students who wish to gain knowledge and experience in the surgical field of medicine.', 'The Surgery Club is for aspiring pre-medical students who are interested in a surgical profession and for students who wish to gain knowledge and experience in the surgical field of medicine. Our goal is to educate pre-med students on the wide range of surgical specialties and subspecialties. Additionally, we wish to guide and educate students on the different pathways to a surgical profession.', 'surgicalspecialtiesucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/surgicalspecialtiesclub'),
(101632, 'The Tzu Chi Collegiate Association at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Weekday evenings for general meetings and socials | Weekend mornings for events', 'Weekly', 'The Tzu Chi Collegiate Association at UCR (Tzu Ching) is the collegiate chapter of a larger foundation known as the Tzu Chi Foundation. Tzu Chi Foundation is a non-profit international charitable organization founded in 1966 by Dharma Master Cheng Yen in the impoverished east coast of Taiwan. The Foundation has dedicated itself in the field of charity, medicine, education, environmental protection, as well as the promotion of humanistic values and community volunteerism in Taiwan and globally for over forty years. Today, Tzu Chi has nearly ten million members around the world.
Tzu Ching directly translates to “youths with compassion and joyous giving.” UCR Tzu Ching members thus engage in the Tzu Chi spirit of compassion by carrying out the Tzu Chi missions of Charity, Medicine, Education, and Culture on campus. Tzu Ching members desire to bring love and care to all people we meet and help. We support one another on the path to becoming better people through retreats, camps, study groups, sharing events, and volunteering. We hope college students, in their prime years to grow as leaders and advocates for change, can gain more knowledge about their own community, as well as a deeper respect for all people. Everyone is welcome to join so that we can take action through compassions and wisdom.', 'A volunteer organization that aims to educate and spread the compassion of individuals by exposing them to diverse volunteer opportunities, including fields in charity, medicine, education, environmental protection, and humanistic culture.', 'The Tzu Chi Collegiate Association at UCR (Tzu Ching) is the collegiate chapter of a larger foundation known as the Tzu Chi Foundation. Tzu Chi Foundation is a non-profit international charitable organization founded in 1966 by Dharma Master Cheng Yen in the impoverished east coast of Taiwan. The Foundation has dedicated itself in the field of charity, medicine, education, environmental protection, as well as the promotion of humanistic values and community volunteerism in Taiwan and globally for over forty years. Today, Tzu Chi has nearly ten million members around the world.
Tzu Ching directly translates to “youths with compassion and joyous giving.” UCR Tzu Ching members thus engage in the Tzu Chi spirit of compassion by carrying out the Tzu Chi missions of Charity, Medicine, Education, and Culture on campus. Tzu Ching members desire to bring love and care to all people we meet and help. We support one another on the path to becoming better people through retreats, camps, study groups, sharing events, and volunteering. We hope college students, in their prime years to grow as leaders and advocates for change, can gain more knowledge about their own community, as well as a deeper respect for all people. Everyone is welcome to join so that we can take action through compassions and wisdom.', 'tcca.ucr@us.tzuchi.org', 'http://www.us.tzuchi.org/us/en/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrtzuching/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tzuching'),
(180111, 'The Verbal Coliseum', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Weekly meetings. Date and time change per quarter, meetings are usually held in the afternoon.', 'Weekly', 'https://youtu.be/sTcJqtuKKq8
We''re the Verbal Coliseum, the only poetry-based club at UCR! During meetings and events, we create, perform, and appreciate the art of poetry. It is a safe space for all creatives of all skill levels and backgrounds. We are always learning, practicing, developing, and exploring together. Weekly meetings, workshops, guest speakers, open mics, and showcases all contribute to the collaborative and comforting ways we use to connect people with the same passion for poetry!', 'The Verbal Coliseum is a group of artists creating, performing, and revolutionizing spoken and written word poetry and other creative writing endeavors on campus.', 'https://youtu.be/sTcJqtuKKq8
We''re the Verbal Coliseum, the only poetry-based club at UCR! During meetings and events, we create, perform, and appreciate the art of poetry. It is a safe space for all creatives of all skill levels and backgrounds. We are always learning, practicing, developing, and exploring together. Weekly meetings, workshops, guest speakers, open mics, and showcases all contribute to the collaborative and comforting ways we use to connect people with the same passion for poetry!', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/theverbalcoliseum/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/verbalcoliseum'),
(334059, 'The Women''s Network', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Biweekly on Wednesdays 6:30-7:30 PM PST', 'Every two weeks', 'The Women’s Network (TWN) was created for ambitious women looking to grow professionally while being uplifted by their community. TWN offers opportunities to gain exposure to the professional world, network with high-profile speakers and meet peers around their campus and the country. TWN meets biweekly (twice a month) and holds speaker meetings, various networking events, resume, internship and LinkedIn workshops, alumni networking receptions and interactive activity sessions to develop relationships with fellow members. Our workshops and guest speakers help prepare you for your next steps and may open your eyes to paths you haven''t even considered.
The purpose of The Women''s Network is to create a community of women that celebrates the desire to achieve, cultivating their ambition in order to prepare the next generation of leaders. TWN strives to provide excellent resources and networking opportunities for young women. To encourage women to be supportive of one another and build each other up. To support young women in any endeavors that they may pursue. To network with potent women in a wide array of different fields.
Fill out this form to become a member and join our network: https://www.thewomens.network/jointwn', 'The Women''s Network exists to create a community of women that celebrates the desire to achieve, cultivating their ambition in order to prepare the next generation of leaders. We encourage women to be supportive of one another and build each other up.', 'The Women’s Network (TWN) was created for ambitious women looking to grow professionally while being uplifted by their community. TWN offers opportunities to gain exposure to the professional world, network with high-profile speakers and meet peers around their campus and the country. TWN meets biweekly (twice a month) and holds speaker meetings, various networking events, resume, internship and LinkedIn workshops, alumni networking receptions and interactive activity sessions to develop relationships with fellow members. Our workshops and guest speakers help prepare you for your next steps and may open your eyes to paths you haven''t even considered.
The purpose of The Women''s Network is to create a community of women that celebrates the desire to achieve, cultivating their ambition in order to prepare the next generation of leaders. TWN strives to provide excellent resources and networking opportunities for young women. To encourage women to be supportive of one another and build each other up. To support young women in any endeavors that they may pursue. To network with potent women in a wide array of different fields.
Fill out this form to become a member and join our network: https://www.thewomens.network/jointwn', 'thewomensnetwork.riverside@gmail.com', 'https://www.thewomens.network/about-us', 'https://www.instagram.com/thewomensnetwork_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/thewomensnetwork_ucr'),
(71200, 'Theta Tau Professional Engineering Fraternity - Sigma Delta Chapter', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesday''s from 20:00 to 22:00', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose of this fraternity shall be to develop and to maintain a high standard of professional interest among its members, and to unite them in a strong bond of fraternal fellowship.', 'The purpose of this fraternity shall be to develop and to maintain a high standard of professional interest among its members, and to unite them in a strong bond of fraternal fellowship.
This fraternity shall operate as a local professional engineering fraternity with the object of petitioning Theta Tau to become a colony and then a chapter of that national professional engineering fraternity. This process was started early 2012 with the founding fathers forming an interest group within the college. The interest group was then colonized on May 19th, 2012.
Now, we are pleased to announce that our chapter petition has been voted on and approved. As of April 26, 2014, we are now established as Sigma Delta Chapter.', 'ThetaTauUCR@gmail.com', 'http://www.thetatauucr.com/', 'https://www.instagram.com/thetatauucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/thetatau'),
(425046, 'Together in Grief', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'Together in Grief is a club dedicated to creating an open dialogue about grief at UCR, providing a supportive space for grieving students to connect and support each other, and educating others on how to support students who are grieving.', 'Together in Grief is a club dedicated to creating an open dialogue about grief at UCR, providing a supportive space for grieving students to connect and support each other, and educating others on how to support students who are grieving.', 'vfeat001@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/together_in_grief_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/togetheringrief'),
(71035, 'Tomorrow''s Teachers in Science and Math', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Meeting dates, times, and locations will be provided with event flyers.', 'Weekly', null, 'For more information:

TTSM is for members of the UCR community who have an interest in teaching, especially in the STEM fields.', 'TTSM brings together students that are considering or actively pursuing a career in teaching Mathematics and Science, with the purpose of creating a place where future educators are able to form a community and build both personal and professional relationships, preparing members for a career in education by providing opportunities to develop leadership and the skills required for the profession and utilizing our passion for education by motivating disadvantaged high school students in their studies, and encouraging them to pursue a college degree following graduation.', 'ttsmatucr@gmail.com', 'http://ttsmucr.weebly.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/ttsmatucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ttsm'),
(431395, 'Triathlon Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'In the evenings / mornings', 'Weekly', null, 'Swim, bike, run, repeat! The UCR Triathlon Club is a student-led community dedicated to multi-sport training, competition, and camaraderie. From absolute beginners to seasoned racers, we offer group workouts and a supportive network for all UCR students!', null, 'triathlonmultisport@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/triathlonclub'),
(402512, 'Turning Point USA at University of California Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Bi-Weekly, Mondays, @7:30pm', 'Every two weeks', 'TPUSA at UCR is a student-led conservative organization at the University of California, Riverside focused on creating a welcoming community for students interested in conservative ideas, civic engagement, free speech, and open political discussion. The chapter aims to give students a space to connect with like-minded peers while also encouraging respectful conversations with students from different backgrounds and viewpoints.
Throughout the school year, TPUSA at UCR plans to host regular tabling, meetings, social events, political discussions, voter-engagement activities, and opportunities to connect students with the broader Turning Point USA network. A major goal of the chapter is to make participation approachable—even for students who may be hesitant to openly express their political beliefs—and to build a community where members can develop leadership skills and become more involved on campus and beyond.
The chapter welcomes students regardless of race, gender, sexuality, or background and emphasizes respectful participation, free expression, and creating opportunities for students to get involved. UCR itself has a long history of student political activism and civic engagement, making campus political organizations part of a broader tradition of student expression.', 'TPUSA at UCR is a student-led conservative organization at the University of California, Riverside focused on creating a welcoming community for students interested in conservative ideas, civic engagement, free speech, and open political discussion.', 'TPUSA at UCR is a student-led conservative organization at the University of California, Riverside focused on creating a welcoming community for students interested in conservative ideas, civic engagement, free speech, and open political discussion. The chapter aims to give students a space to connect with like-minded peers while also encouraging respectful conversations with students from different backgrounds and viewpoints.
Throughout the school year, TPUSA at UCR plans to host regular tabling, meetings, social events, political discussions, voter-engagement activities, and opportunities to connect students with the broader Turning Point USA network. A major goal of the chapter is to make participation approachable—even for students who may be hesitant to openly express their political beliefs—and to build a community where members can develop leadership skills and become more involved on campus and beyond.
The chapter welcomes students regardless of race, gender, sexuality, or background and emphasizes respectful participation, free expression, and creating opportunities for students to get involved. UCR itself has a long history of student political activism and civic engagement, making campus political organizations part of a broader tradition of student expression.', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/tpusa_at_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/tpusa_ucr'),
(191159, 'UCR - Food Recovery', 'Department Affiliated Organization', null, null, null, null, 'Join this group to receive text/email notifications when there is free food around campus. Our goal is to minimize your immediate food insecurity while also reducing campus-wide food waste.', 'Easy Steps: “SIGN IN” and select “JOIN” to subscribe.
GET MESSAGES ABOUT FREE FOOD ACROSS CAMPUS!
Live text/email alerts throughout the day
Campus-wide locations
Includes ready-to-eat meals, snacks and fresh produce
FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS:
What kind of messages are sent out?
When various campus groups have extra food to share.
Who can subscribe to these messages?
Any UCR student (both undergrad and grad), staff, or faculty.
Why/how is this a thing?
After tuition, books, housing and other necessities are paid for, affording nutritious foods can be a struggle.
People have enough to deal with, being hungry shouldn’t be one of them.
Nutrition affects your performance. Feed your body and mind.
This helps reduce campus-wide food waste by ensuring food ends up in bellies and not dumpsters.
ADDITIONAL RESOURCES:
On-campus emergency food resource for students: rpantry.ucr.edu
Learn how to get money for food from CalFresh: basicneeds.ucr.edu/calfresh
How to secure life’s basic necessities: basicneeds.ucr.edu', 'basicneeds@ucr.edu', 'http://basicneeds.ucr.edu', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/foodrecovery'),
(70976, 'UCRaas Collegiate Indian Folk Dance Team', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Monday-Friday from 8:00 pm to 12:00 am', 'Weekly', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to promote South Asian Cultural awareness to a cultural dance which originated from Gujarat. This team will strive to compete at competitions throughout the nation. By doing so, people of all ethnicities will be brought together in the process of working towards our goals of winning competitions. We aim to have practices five times a week to maintain unity amongst the team.', 'Garba and Raas represent traditional dance forms that have been a part of the Indian culture for many years. The University of California, Riverside is proud to announce that its very own Garba/Raas team is in its 16th successful year.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to promote South Asian Cultural awareness to a cultural dance which originated from Gujarat. This team will strive to compete at competitions throughout the nation. By doing so, people of all ethnicities will be brought together in the process of working towards our goals of winning competitions. We aim to have practices five times a week to maintain unity amongst the team.', 'riversideraas@gmail.com', null, 'http://www.instagram.com/ucraas_', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucraas'),
(70843, 'Ultimate Frisbee Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesday and Thursday 8-10pm', 'Twice a week', 'Come On Out!
-We play every Tuesday and Thursday from 8-10pm at the North District Fields.
-You haven’t played before!? No problem, the club is open to players of all skill levels, from brand new player, to UFA prodigy and everything in between.
-We are looking to get more people to learn and enjoy the game of Ultimate Frisbee, and improve our skills while we are at it.
What We Do.
-Practice/pickup games every Tuesday and Thursday from 8-10pm
-Enter tournaments and compete in leagues such as Lei-Out, St. Pat’s Hat, Trouble in Vegas, and Beach, Winter, and Summer Leagues.
-Also starting a USA Ultimate college team to compete in the official college division and play other schools such as Cal Poly Pomona, UC Davis, Cal, UC Irvine, etc. (some time in the future)
And Why!?
-It isn’t called Ultimate just so it sounds cool. This game combines the stamina and running of soccer, the quick feet and agility of football, the defense and hops of basketball, and the smarts and foresight of baseball. It truly is the Ultimate sport!
-We play to better ourselves as athletes and stay in shape. We have fun doing it, and it is a great way to meet people at UCR! Undergrads play, graduate students play, post-doctorates play, and even professors!
Contact Us!
-Follow our Instagram and join the linked group me to get notifications and updates.
-Find us and other clubs on Highlander Link: highlanderlink.ucr.edu There you can officially join clubs, sign waivers, and see what events various clubs are hosting.', 'We practice every Tues.Thursday from 8-10PM at the North District Fields. All skill levels are welcome!', 'Ultimate Frisbee Club at UCR
