(425359, 'Uncensored America at University of California Riverside', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Non-regular meetings', null, 'Uncensored America is a youth-driven free speech organization dedicated to promoting open dialogues on college campuses.', 'Uncensored America is a youth-driven free speech organization dedicated to hosting honest and fun conversations with controversial figures to fight censorship and cancel culture. Our goal is to create a free speech culture to make America free and fun again.', null, 'uncensoredamerica.us', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/uncensoredamerica_ucr'),
(71024, 'Undergraduate Business Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Please check our Facebook or Instagram to find out updated meeting days and times', 'Weekly', null, 'Undergraduate Business Association is dedicated to creating a strong and ever-growing network of professional connections as a vehicle to spread our passion for business and advance the professional goals of our members.', 'https://youtu.be/lrKHAd1YrVk
Undergraduate Business Association is dedicated to creating a strong and evergrowing network of professional connections as a vehicle to spread our passion for business and advance the professional goals of our members. UBA is committed to providing business and leadership education and spreading information about the different fields of business.', 'uba.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://ucruba.wixsite.com/ubaucr', 'https://www.instagram.com/ubaucr/?hl=en', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/uba'),
(418735, 'Undergraduate Research Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Wednesdays 5-6 PM (TBD)', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The Undergraduate Research Club (URC) at UCR promotes student research, collaboration, advocacy, and innovation across all disciplines through mentorship, workshops, and hands-on projects that connect students with faculty and professional opportunities.', 'The Undergraduate Research Club (URC) at the University of California, Riverside is dedicated to fostering a culture of inquiry, discovery, and innovation among undergraduate students across all academic disciplines. URC provides a platform for students to explore research opportunities, develop professional skills, and engage with faculty mentors through workshops, collaborative projects, and educational events.
Our mission is to make research more accessible by connecting students to the tools, resources, and networks they need to succeed whether they are new to research or already involved in a lab or project. Through partnerships with departments, student organizations, and professional institutions, URC promotes interdisciplinary collaboration and helps students share their findings through presentations, publications, and conferences.
URC strives to uphold integrity, inclusivity, and ethical conduct in all scholarly activities while inspiring a new generation of researchers to apply their knowledge for the betterment of the academic and local community.', 'urc.bcoe.ucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/urc.bcoe/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/urcbcoe'),
(180866, 'Unheard Cries Charity', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Mondays, 7:00-8:00 P.M', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose of this club is to spread awareness of Middle Eastern penury and persecution. This organization will fight poverty through specific programs that provide humanitarian assistance for people in need.', 'The purpose of this club is to spread awareness of the Middle Eastern penury and persecution. This organization will fight poverty through specific programs that provide humanitarian assistance for people in need. We achieve our goal through our fundraiser events we host every year like Arabian Nights, Winter Wonderland, and many others. These events help us to gain funds necessary for the certain causes we donate to at that time. For example, our Arabian Nights event usually gathers around 500 people and last year it helped us to raise thousands of dollars for a community center that houses special needs/the elderly in Egypt. We welcome any and all supporters of every background that would like to help us with this great cause!', 'unheardcries.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.unheardcriescharity.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/unheardcriescharityatucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/unheardcriescharity'),
(425081, 'United Health Pathways', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesday from 6:20PM to 8:00PM', 'Weekly', null, 'United Health Pathways guides students toward medical certifications like CPT, EMT, and CNA, connecting them with hospitals for hands-on experience. We inspire future healthcare professionals through outreach, workshops, and networking opportunities.', 'United Health Pathways provides members with comprehensive guidance, resources, and opportunities to pursue medical licensing and healthcare certifications such as CPT, EMT, and CNA. Our organization connects students with local hospitals and healthcare institutions to help them secure externships, internships, shadowing experiences, clinical hours, and employment opportunities. Additionally, we are committed to inspiring the next generation of healthcare professionals by engaging in outreach programs with local K–12 students to spark their interest in the medical field. Through workshops, study groups, and networking events, UHP promotes both professional and personal growth while fostering collaboration among students who share a passion for healthcare careers.', 'ucruhp@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucruhp', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/uhp'),
(284540, 'United Nations International Children''s Emergency Fund @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Wednesday at 7:00 pm', 'Monthly', null, 'UNICEF @ UCR is a club that will advocate for the protection of children''s rights and will uphold these values through community service, fundraising to support UNICEF’s aid programs, and spreading awareness on a local and global level.', 'UNICEF @ UCR is a club that will advocate for the protection of children''s rights and will uphold these values through community service, fundraising to support UNICEF’s aid programs, and spreading awareness on a local and global level.', 'ucriv.unicef@gmail.com', 'https://unicefatucr.weebly.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/unicef_ucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/unicefatucr'),
(341641, 'University Blood Initiative at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Monday 7:00 PM - 8:00 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'The University Blood Initiative at UCR seeks to empower local Riverside blood donor centers and encourage blood donation amongst the Riverside community.', 'As the UCR Chapter of the University Blood Initiative, our goal is to promote, encourage, and organize local blood drives, as well as educate our local community on the importance of blood donation.', 'ucrbloodinitiative@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrbloodinitiative/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrubi'),
(74478, 'US Army ROTC', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'During physical training sessions (Monday and Tuesday 0600-0700) and during Leadership Laboratories/class (Fridays 0630-1300)', 'Weekly', 'The work can be time consuming and weariness may certainly result, but the lessons learned, friendships, and accomplishments made can be invaluable for your life that lies ahead.
It is important to note that ROTC at UCR is mostly done through California State University San Bernardino and Claremont McKenna College. This certainly serves as a means to meet people from many other schools around the Inland Empire including California Baptist University, Azusa Pacific University, Cal Poly Pomona, and many others. However, having a means of transportation can make life in the program much easier.
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L4q6_sN46xQ', 'We work to inform any UCR students about the many options and methods available to commission as an Officer in the U.S. Army and the many career fields UCR students can experience to bolster their resume for the any life plans.', 'Everyone in the UCR Cadet Recruiting team shares the aspiration to one day serve as an Officer in the United States Army. Our goal is to spread awareness of the program to any Students at UCR that share our same aspirations.
While there are many ways to become a U.S. Army Officer, ROTC is a method that allows Cadets to attend school and earn a degree while participating in the training necessary to one day commission.
The work can be time consuming and weariness may certainly result, but the lessons learned, friendships, and accomplishments made can be invaluable for your life that lies ahead.
It is important to note that ROTC at UCR is mostly done through California State University San Bernardino and Claremont McKenna College. This certainly serves as a means to meet people from many other schools around the Inland Empire including California Baptist University, Azusa Pacific University, Cal Poly Pomona, and many others. However, having a means of transportation can make life in the program much easier.
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L4q6_sN46xQ', 'armyrotc@ucr.edu', 'https://studentlife.ucr.edu/reserve-officer-training-corps-rotc', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr.army.rotc/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/crt'),
(363133, 'Vain Fashion Club @ UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], 'Wednesdays at 6pm', 'Every two weeks', 'Vain''s goal is to create a supportive, inspiring, and empowering place for all students who are either interested or curious in any area of fashion. Our meetings will be a place for students to come together and converse on fashion topics and shared interests while also promoting a fashion culture here at UCR. Our club will hold fashion shows where all students have the opportunity to showcase their unique style. These shows are meant to promote fashion as a form of self expression and embrace how it brings everyone together. We will also feature students in our themed photoshoots, not just as models but for students to show off skills in photography, editing, and makeup. Our meetings will be comprised of a wide variety of events: crafting workshops, debates, competitions, information sessions, socials, etc. Furthermore, this club will release quarterly magazines that feature student life on campus in both fashion, culture, and interviews. Our goal is simple: Fashion for Everyone. We want to promote how fashion is the thread that ties our campus culture together', 'Vain Fashion Club @ UCR', 'Vain''s goal is to create a supportive, inspiring, and empowering place for all students who are either interested or curious in any area of fashion. Our meetings will be a place for students to come together and converse on fashion topics and shared interests while also promoting a fashion culture here at UCR. Our club will hold fashion shows where all students have the opportunity to showcase their unique style. These shows are meant to promote fashion as a form of self expression and embrace how it brings everyone together. We will also feature students in our themed photoshoots, not just as models but for students to show off skills in photography, editing, and makeup. Our meetings will be comprised of a wide variety of events: crafting workshops, debates, competitions, information sessions, socials, etc. Furthermore, this club will release quarterly magazines that feature student life on campus in both fashion, culture, and interviews. Our goal is simple: Fashion for Everyone. We want to promote how fashion is the thread that ties our campus culture together', 'fashionatucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrvainfashion'),
(401931, 'Venture Capital Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Mondays 5:00 PM', 'Weekly', null, 'The Venture Capital Association (VCA) at UC Riverside educates students on venture capital, finance and entrepreneurship, offering hands-on experience, networking opportunities, and resources to develop their own ventures.', 'The Venture Capital Association (VCA) at UC Riverside is a dynamic student organization focused on educating and empowering students in venture capital, entrepreneurial finance, and the startup ecosystem. VCA provides members with valuable hands-on experience in evaluating investment opportunities, performing due diligence, and understanding the intricacies of venture capital funding.
Through a wide range of events, including workshops, guest speaker sessions, and networking opportunities, VCA connects students with industry leaders such as venture capitalists, entrepreneurs, and investors. The organization also actively promotes entrepreneurship, offering resources and guidance for students interested in developing and launching their own business ventures.
Whether students aim to explore careers in venture capital, start their own companies, or simply expand their knowledge of the startup world, VCA serves as a valuable platform for growth, learning, and professional development.', 'venturecapitalucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/vca'),
(380090, 'VEX Robotics', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Tuesday 6:00pm - 8:00pm, WCH 221', 'Weekly', null, 'We are a robotics club who competes in VEX U. We strive to create an equal opportunity for everyone to learn and apply their knowledge in real world situations. Every year we tackle a new challenge that is presented to by using the engineering process.', 'Who We Are:
At Ursa Mechanica, we are more than just a team; we are a family united by our love for robotics. Our diverse group of students brings together a wealth of knowledge, skills, and creativity, forming the perfect blend for tackling the challenges posed by VEX Robotics competitions. From programming wizards to mechanical maestros, we have it all, and together, we forge ahead into the realm of cutting-edge robotics.
Our Passion:
Our passion for robotics goes beyond mere wires and circuits. We believe in the power of technology to transform lives and solve real-world problems. Through VEX Robotics, we channel this passion into designing robots that not only excel in competitions but also inspire others to explore the wonders of STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics). We aim to leave a lasting impact on the world, one robot at a time.
What Sets Us Apart:
What sets Ursa Mechanica apart is not just our technical expertise but also our spirit of collaboration and sportsmanship. We understand that the journey is as important as the destination. Every challenge we face, every obstacle we overcome, and every success we achieve, is a testament to our teamwork, determination, and resilience.
Our Mission:
Our mission is clear: to innovate, to inspire, and to make a difference. Through VEX Robotics, we hone our skills, learn from each other, and grow as individuals and as a team. We strive for excellence, aiming to push the boundaries of what is possible in the world of robotics.
Join Us on Our Journey:
We invite you to join us on this exhilarating adventure into the future of robotics. Follow our progress, cheer for us in competitions, and witness the magic of innovation unfold before your eyes. Together, let’s explore the limitless possibilities of robotics and inspire a new generation of inventors, engineers, and dreamers.
Feel Free To Add Our Socials!
Instagram: @ucr_vex.robotics
Discord: https://discord.gg/CsWsfR7wJQ
interested? Join the discord!', 'ucrvexrobotics@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_vex_robotics/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/vexrobotics'),
(420328, 'Vietnamese International Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'A student-run cultural organization dedicated to celebrating heritage and traditions, fostering unity among members, and sharing our culture with the broader campus community through events, performances, and outreach activities.', null, 'tpham297@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/vis'),
(71159, 'Vietnamese Student Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Cultural']::text[], 'Thursdays at 7/8PM', '3 times a quarter (almost every 2 weeks)', null, 'To unite all people of Vietnamese interest. To preserve the Vietnamese cultural heritage. To promote the personal growth and pride of each member. To facilitate a mutual understanding between club members and the student population.', 'To unite all people of Vietnamese interest. To preserve the Vietnamese cultural heritage. To promote the personal growth and pride of each member. To facilitate a mutual understanding between club members, other campus organizations, and the student population through the sharing of experiences.', 'vsaatucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrvsa', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrvsa/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/vsa'),
(406913, 'Virtual Reality X', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Thursdays at 10:30 AM', 'Weekly', null, 'We are a service-oriented organization that uses cutting-edge VR technology to improve the quality of life of seniors in our community and provide invaluable VR resources to at-risk populations through educational content and early dementia screening.', 'The VRx at UCR Club, initiated by undergraduate students at our university, seeks to utilize virtual reality technology to enhance the lives of seniors suffering from Alzheimer''s Disease in Riverside County. Our mission is to provide innovative VR-based dementia screening, educate the community about Alzheimer''s, and offer immersive VR experiences that benefit the cognitive and emotional well-being of the elderly. This club represents a unique intersection of technology, healthcare, and volunteerism, aiming to bridge the gap between younger and older generations through meaningful interactions and support.
Our vision is to establish a compassionate and innovative community where the challenges of Alzheimer''s Disease are met with cutting-edge technology and empathetic care. We envision a future where virtual reality is a key component in the management and care of Alzheimer''s, offering new avenues for early detection, therapeutic intervention, and quality of life improvements. By empowering students and engaging seniors, the VRx at UCR Club aspires to be a leader in promoting mental health and social connection, ultimately transforming the way our society supports its aging population.', 'virtualrxucr@gmail.com', 'https://www.getvirtualrx.org/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrvrx/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/vrx'),
(433754, 'Vivamed', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], 'Mondays @ 5pm', 'Every two weeks', null, 'Vivamed prepares future healthcare professionals through Spanish medical terminology workshops, physician guest speakers, community service, and pre-med networking and career development.', 'VivaMed at UCR prepares future healthcare professionals through Medical Spanish education, educational workshops, physician guest speakers, community service, and pre-health career development. Members learn Spanish medical terminology, attend informational
workshops on topics such as vital signs and medical scribing, volunteer in the community, and build professional connections while exploring careers in healthcare.', 'vsami003@ucr.edu', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/vivamed'),
(419006, 'Voicing Inclusion Thriving Awareness and Leadership', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Action & Awareness']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'VITAL is a student led initiative for wellness and inclusion in the inland empire. Advocating awareness, leadership, and equitable access to knowledge and resources—ensuring that our efforts promote lasting empowerment and strong actions.', 'VITAL is a student-led organization at the University of California, Riverside dedicated to promoting wellness, awareness, and leadership development within the community. Our mission is to educate, empower, and engage students and community members through workshops, outreach initiatives, and collaborative events that foster inclusion, personal growth, and meaningful impact.
VITAL provides opportunities for students to develop leadership skills, participate in community service, and collaborate with campus organizations and local partners to address topics such as mental health, social awareness, and personal development. We prioritize consistency, education, and sustainable partnerships to create lasting positive change for our members and the communities we serve.', 'vitalucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/vital'),
(401454, 'Warhammer Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Fridays', 'Weekly', null, 'Warhammer/Tabletop gaming club at UCR! We host a wide array of miniature-tabletop games, primarily focusing on Warhammer 40k, featuring our competitive team. If you are interested, check us out on discord! 

https://discord.gg/CGV9uE8HTa', 'The Official Warhammer Club at UCR! If you are a new player wanting to get into Warhammer, or a veteran looking for some some games, we got it all! Don''t care about playing and want to show off your painting skills? Join us!
https://discord.gg/CGV9uE8HTa', 'lgent006@ucr.edu', 'https://discord.gg/CGV9uE8HTa', 'https://www.instagram.com/warhammerucr?igsh=YXR5Y2sybmVnbXN2', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrwarhammer'),
(400902, 'We R’ Dancers', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Late Afternoons once to twice a week, Scheduled based on members selection', 'Weekly', null, 'Student-led organization dedicated to celebrating and fostering a vibrant community of performers.Open to dancers of all backgrounds, providing a supportive space to express yourself, grow your skills, and make connections."Led by students, for students"', null, 'werdancers08@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/werdancersucr?igsh=OGQ5ZDc2ODk2ZA%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/wrd'),
(430890, 'Welfare Of Our Furry Friends', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Service']::text[], 'Mondays', 'Every two weeks', null, 'WOOF supports local private animal rescues and foster networks by mobilizing UCR students as volunteers and organizing on-campus donation drives. We provide essential supplies to shelters while offering students documented volunteer experience.', 'The purpose of WOOF (Welfare of Our Furry Friends) is to support local private animal rescues and shelters around the Inland Empire. We focus on smaller, private rescues and foster networks that lack corporate or federal funding by mobilizing UCR students as volunteers and organizing on-campus donation drives and fundraisers. These efforts provide partner organizations with food, toys, treats, bedding, and other essential supplies
WOOF is commited to the belief that every pet deserves love. We work to ensure every partnered organization receives volunteer support and tangible donations, while our members gain documented volunteer experience and make a measurable impact on animal welfare.
Additionally, we seek to establish a formalized, partner-verified volunteer pipeline for pre-med, pre-vet, and pre-health students, and to raise campus awareness of local animal welfare needs.', 'woofucr@gmail.com', 'https://linktr.ee/woof.ucr?utm_source=ig&utm_medium=social&utm_content=link_in_bio', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrwoof/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrwoof'),
(222135, 'Women in Computing at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Weekly', null, 'We aim to support, celebrate, and empower women, non-binary, and underrepresented groups in computing at UCR.', 'Women in Computing (WINC) is dedicated to empowering and supporting a network of individuals in tech at the University of California, Riverside, with a focus on women and marginalized genders. We believe that every individual, regardless of gender identity, should have equal access to opportunities to pursue a career in Computer Science. WINC strives to achieve this by offering inclusive and welcoming member events, educational technical workshops, mentorship from role models in university and industry, research opportunities, scholarships, and more. Our goal is to increase the retention rate of marginalized genders pursuing computing and to provide a safe space for anyone interested in a tech career.
Our goal is to build a community of women programmers and provide a safe and empowering place for students to express themselves. We celebrate all programmers at UCR and encourage them to grow as students and future leaders in the computing fields. WinC is open to anyone: whether you''re just looking to start coding or you have had multiple years in the industry, we''d love to have you!', 'wincucr@gmail.com', 'https://winc.cs.ucr.edu/', 'https://www.instagram.com/wincucr/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/winc'),
(424973, 'Women in Film', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], null, 'Bi-weekly organization events and weekly board meetings', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to establish an open space for female and gender nonconforming voices who are interested in the film industry. We aim to bring support, education, and a collective voice to women and gender minority filmmakers, through workshops, discussions of women in the industry, movie screenings, and offering production opportunities. We welcome anyone regardless of experience. Throughout our time working on student films at UCR, we have noticed a significant lack of women on film sets. This absence is not unique to UCR however, there is a systematic lack of representation and opportunity for women in film and television. Through sharing our experiences and knowledge we strive to create a safe space for individuals to feel heard and welcome in meetings, events, and productions. Our goals are to not only show our resilience in a male-dominated industry, but to achieve our ideas and establish a community of like-minded individuals to support each other throughout our careers. We want everyone to feel inspired and motivated to develop their projects and reach goals they haven’t dreamed of yet.', 'WIF aims to bring support, education, and a collective voice to women and gender minority filmmakers, through workshops, discussions of women in the industry, movie screenings, and offering production opportunities.', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to establish an open space for female and gender nonconforming voices who are interested in the film industry. We aim to bring support, education, and a collective voice to women and gender minority filmmakers, through workshops, discussions of women in the industry, movie screenings, and offering production opportunities. We welcome anyone regardless of experience. Throughout our time working on student films at UCR, we have noticed a significant lack of women on film sets. This absence is not unique to UCR however, there is a systematic lack of representation and opportunity for women in film and television. Through sharing our experiences and knowledge we strive to create a safe space for individuals to feel heard and welcome in meetings, events, and productions. Our goals are to not only show our resilience in a male-dominated industry, but to achieve our ideas and establish a community of like-minded individuals to support each other throughout our careers. We want everyone to feel inspired and motivated to develop their projects and reach goals they haven’t dreamed of yet.', 'womeninfilmucr@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/womeninfilm_ucr?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D&utm_source=qr', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/womeninfilm'),
(419428, 'Women In Neuroendocrinology', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', 'Our organization is dedicated to advancing research and healthcare in women’s health, with a focus on neuroendocrinology and neurology. We aim to educate students about the unique aspects of the female neuroendocrine system and the neurological mechanisms underlying disorders such as epilepsy. In addition, we strive to raise awareness of the longstanding gaps in women’s neurological care. Through these efforts, we hope to contribute to the development of more comprehensive and effective treatments for all women, including both cisgender and transgender patients. Our three pillars of advancement are Research, Clinical Practice, and Public Health. We will potentially be bringing in guest speakers, having interactive workshops, as well as having volunteering/fundraising events!', 'An organization dedicated to advocating for women''s neuroendocrinological health through discussion of research, clinical practice, and participation in civic engagement.', 'Our organization is dedicated to advancing research and healthcare in women’s health, with a focus on neuroendocrinology and neurology. We aim to educate students about the unique aspects of the female neuroendocrine system and the neurological mechanisms underlying disorders such as epilepsy. In addition, we strive to raise awareness of the longstanding gaps in women’s neurological care. Through these efforts, we hope to contribute to the development of more comprehensive and effective treatments for all women, including both cisgender and transgender patients. Our three pillars of advancement are Research, Clinical Practice, and Public Health. We will potentially be bringing in guest speakers, having interactive workshops, as well as having volunteering/fundraising events!', 'womeninneuroendocrinology@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/womeninneuroendocrinologyatucr'),
(405181, 'Women in STEM and the Arts', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Arts and Expression']::text[], null, 'Every two weeks', null, 'WISAA aims to create a most relaxing space for individuals that uplifts as women in STEM by providing an artistic outlet.', null, 'Womeninstemartsucr@gmail.com', 'https://sites.google.com/ucr.edu/womeninstemandartsucr/home', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/womeninstemandthearts'),
(418283, 'Women''s Business Association', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Every Wednesday, 5 PM', 'Every two weeks', null, 'A supportive and empowering space for college students, particularly women and students who identify with femininity, to explore personal growth, professional development, and creative expression within the field of Business.', null, 'ucr.wba@gmail.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/women-s-business-association-at-ucr/about/?viewAsMember=true', null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/womensbusinessassociation'),
(418802, 'Women''s Club Basketball at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Practices depend on student''s class schedules', 'Weekly', 'Team members are expected to attend MANDATORY practices 1or 2 times per week, as well as participate in games each quarter. Practices focus on skill development, conditioning, and team strategy, while games provide the opportunity to compete against other universities.
We are looking for dedicated, team-oriented players who are ready to work hard, improve their game, and contribute to a positive team environment.', 'Women''s club basketball team at UCR. Full roster, away and home games, official jerseys.', 'Team members are expected to attend MANDATORY practices 1or 2 times per week, as well as participate in games each quarter. Practices focus on skill development, conditioning, and team strategy, while games provide the opportunity to compete against other universities.
We are looking for dedicated, team-oriented players who are ready to work hard, improve their game, and contribute to a positive team environment.', 'ucrwcbb@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrwcbb'),
(71106, 'Women''s Club Soccer', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesday and Thursday 7:30pm-9:30pm', 'Weekly', 'We are the Women''s Club Soccer team at UC Riverside! Our team competes against universities and colleges located throughout California. We practice twice a week on Tuesdays and Thursdays from 7:30pm to 9:30pm at the Glen Mor Fields located on campus by the residence halls. The players that participate have prior soccer experience, ranging from youth soccer, club soccer, high school soccer, and even former intercollegiate athletes. We promote learning as much as we can by practicing our soccer skills, but also focus on teamwork, leadership, and respect. We encourage everyone to join if you have the passion and drive to play soccer!', 'Women''s Club Soccer is a competitive sports team at UC Riverside. We practice twice a week and play competitive games against other universities on weekends. We promote fitness, friendship, and leadership.', 'We are the Women''s Club Soccer team at UC Riverside! Our team competes against universities and colleges located throughout California. We practice twice a week on Tuesdays and Thursdays from 7:30pm to 9:30pm at the Glen Mor Fields located on campus by the residence halls. The players that participate have prior soccer experience, ranging from youth soccer, club soccer, high school soccer, and even former intercollegiate athletes. We promote learning as much as we can by practicing our soccer skills, but also focus on teamwork, leadership, and respect. We encourage everyone to join if you have the passion and drive to play soccer!', 'acvje001@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_wcs/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/wcs'),
(76512, 'Women''s Club Volleyball', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesday 7:30PM-9:30PM, Sundays (6-8pm) Contact the president for more information', 'Weekly', null, 'This club provides a healthy environment to competitively practice and play volleyball, as well as allowing campus and community involvement.', 'Thanks to the growing community of students, this club can satisfy the developing demand for a more competitive style of volleyball. The club will facilitate team relationships and competition against other club teams from different schools.', 'wcv.ucr@gmail.com', 'https://beacons.ai/ucrwomensclubvb', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrclubvolleyball/', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/ucrwcv'),
(430917, 'Women''s Rugby Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', null, 'Tuesday and Thursday 7-9pm', 'Twice per week (Tuesday and Thursday)', 'Always open to new members, come give rugby a try! Feel free to message our Instagram below :)
Practice is on the North District Fields- Tuesday and Thursday 7pm', 'We want to teach rugby to members of our UCR community and to foster a welcoming environment where members can be encouraged towards excellence through discipline on and off of the field.', 'The purpose of this organization is to teach rugby to players of all skill levels, promote community and competitive spirit within our team and others in the area, and to strive for excellence both on and off the field through discipline and support.
Always open to new members, come give rugby a try! Feel free to message our Instagram below :)
Practice is on the North District Fields- Tuesday and Thursday 7pm', 'iwell003@ucr.edu', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/ucr_womensrugby', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/womensrugby'),
(430879, 'Women''s Running Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Mondays, Tuesdays, Fridays at start times 7:00AM and 4:15PM. Optional weekends at 8:00AM, every 3 weeks.', 'Weekly', null, 'We run, we walk. No pace is slow! Join the Women Running Club at UCR, where we foster well-being and social connection for women of all backgrounds by building an empowering and safe community centered on running and walking.', 'Women Running at UCR provides a non-competitive, low-pressure environment for walking and running. No pace is too slow, all paces are welcome! Our goal is to promote social health and a sense of belonging through community-building activities at a conversational pace. Showing up is all it takes. We want to see you! We host runs/walks on Mondays, Tuesdays, and Fridays. Events are hosted 2-3 times a quarter!', 'womenrunningatucr@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/womenrunning'),
(425414, 'Women’s Water Polo Club', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'Tuesday’s and thursdays starting fall 2026', 'Two times a week', null, 'The women water polo club will be  collegiate club that trains at UCR and competes within the state and out of state.', 'The Women’s Water Polo Club will be a collegiate club team that trains at UCR and competes in tournaments both within the state and out of state against other collegiate club programs.', 'Swake005@ucr.edu', null, 'www.instagram.com/ucr_womenswpc', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/womenswaterpolo'),
(352914, 'Womxn In the Law', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Academic/Professional']::text[], 'Weekday evenings', 'Weekly', null, 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to create a supportive community and network for diverse womxn pursuing law school. A safe space for minority womxn pre-law undergraduate students that aim to join the legal profession.
Established 2022', 'The purpose(s) of this organization shall be to create a supportive community and network for diverse womxn pursuing law school. Women in the Law is designed to create a safe space for minority womxn pre-law undergraduate students that aim to join the legal profession. We value teamwork, networking, and sharing resources to ensure our members are able to combat any social, sexist, or economic adversities they may face while applying to law school.', 'ucrwitl@gmail.com', 'https://groupme.com/join_group/87875271/AcPvZ5oo  https://groupme.com/join_group/87875271/AcPvZ5oo', 'https://www.instagram.com/ucrwitl', 'https://highlanderlink.ucr.edu/organization/witl'),
(71153, 'Wrestling Club at UCR', 'Registered Student Organization', array['Recreational']::text[], 'ASG Facility 6:30pm - 8:30pm on Mondays - Thursday & UCR SRC North MPR D 5pm - 7pm on Fridays', 'Mondays through Fridays weekly', 'All wrestlers are welcomed. No previous experience in wrestling is required.
